{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]).slice(\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\").merge(\\\"changes_count\\\" => YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])[\\\"changes\\\"].length)' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r11s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r11s0\ntitle: \"Early-out radix-4 RV32M divider\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The ALU still exposes long combinational division and remainder cones on\n  the execute timing path.  A prior 32-cycle divider removed those cones but\n  lost fitness because every divide serialized the in-order pipeline for its\n  full worst-case latency.  CoreMark's divide operands are commonly small, so\n  a bounded radix-4 divider with early termination is a narrower latency/area\n  tradeoff.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU operators with a shared\n  two-bits-per-cycle restoring divider that produces quotient and remainder\n  together and terminates as soon as the remaining high-order quotient work\n  is resolved.  Hold only the execute instruction while the divider is busy,\n  then inject one completed result into the existing EX/MEM path; ordinary\n  ALU and MUL operations continue to accept one instruction per cycle.  Keep\n  divide-by-zero, signed overflow, quotient/remainder sign rules, forwarding,\n  RVFI validity, and the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions exact.  The shorter\n  maximum latency than the prior 32-step design should recover IPC while the\n  absence of a wide combinational divider should improve Tang Nano timing.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove the synthesized combinational divide/remainder cones from the CPU ALU while retaining exact RV32M edge semantics and the ALTOPS arithmetic path for formal and unit-test builds.\"\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a shared radix-4 restoring quotient/remainder unit with signedness handling, divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 cases, busy/done control, and operand-magnitude early termination.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Integrate divider start/wait/complete sequencing so only an in-flight DIV or REM holds execute, while completed results enter the normal EX/MEM and forwarding path.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a divider-busy interlock that freezes younger decode and prevents duplicate EX/MEM retirement without disturbing load-use or dmem-stall priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect divider control and completion signals through the existing pipeline without changing the top-level IO or single-channel RVFI contract.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r11s0\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>6, \"confidence\"=>\"low\"}, \"changes_count\"=>5}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
