nch/gpt-5_4_xhigh/rep1/agent.log:30:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778809274170,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d6b7d516ffe2a70J6wE57c0Bo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"apply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_VfBybKtQ85CDiU2m95wpT4DS\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r1s0.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260514-001-r1s0\\n+title: \\\"Move DIV/REM Off The ALU Critical Path\\\"\\n+category: micro_opt\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current EX-stage ALU is fully combinational and includes RV32M divide\\n+  and remainder operators in its worst-case path. On the Tang Nano 20K that\\n+  logic is likely much slower than the add/shift/branch hot path, yet\\n+  CoreMark's timed region is dominated by list/state/matrix work and appears\\n+  to use division only in cold setup code. If the divider stops limiting Fmax,\\n+  a small stall cost on rare DIV/REM instructions should buy a net fitness\\n+  gain.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Replace the single-cycle combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic with a small\\n+  iterative divider in EX, while keeping ADD/logic/shift/branch and the\\n+  multiply family on the existing fast path. EX would assert a busy condition\\n+  only for divide/remainder ops, hold younger stages until the result is ready,\\n+  then release a single normal retirement with the same RV32M corner-case and\\n+  RVFI semantics. This should shorten the worst timing path, trim LUT pressure,\\n+  and preserve CoreMark/MHz because the hot benchmark loop is not divider\\n+  heavy.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 8\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Remove DIV/REM from the always-hot combinational ALU path while keeping fast ALU ops and MUL-family behavior unchanged.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Add an iterative divider path in EX and hold EX/MEM advance until DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU completes.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Propagate an EX-busy stall so IF/ID/EX hold cleanly during multi-cycle divide operations without extra bubbles or double retirements.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Wire divider busy/done control between EX and the pipeline hazard logic while preserving the existing top-level IO and RVFI contract.\\\"\\n+  - file: test/test_alu.py\\n+    description: \\\"Re-check RV32M divide and remainder corner cases after moving divider semantics out of the single-cycle ALU implementation.\\\"\\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\\n+    description: \\\"Add coverage for multi-cycle DIV/REM stalls, forwarding, and single-channel RVFI retirement behavior.\\\"\\n*** End Patch\"},\"output\":\"Success. Updated the following files:\\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r1s0.yaml\",\"metadata\":{\"diff\":\"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r1s0.yaml\\n===================================================================\\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r1s0.yaml\\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r1s0.yaml\\n@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\\n+id: hyp-20260514-001-r1s0\\n+title: \\\"Move DIV/REM Off The ALU Critical Path\\\"\\n+category: micro_opt\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current EX-stage ALU is fully combinational and includes RV32M divide\\n+  and remainder operators in its worst-case path. On the Tang Nano 20K that\\n+  logic is likely much slower than the add/shift/branch hot path, yet\\n+  CoreMark's timed region is dominated by list/state/matrix work and appears\\n+  to use division only in cold setup code. If the divider stops limiting Fmax,\\n+  a small stall cost on rare DIV/REM instructions should buy a net fitness\\n+  gain.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Replace the single-cycle combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic with a small\\n+  iterative divider in EX, while keeping ADD/logic/shift/branch and the\\n+  multiply family on the existing fast path. EX would assert a busy condition\\n+  only for divide/remainder ops, hold younger stages until the result is ready,\\n+  then release a single normal retirement with the same RV32M corner-case and\\n+  RVFI semantics. This should shorten the worst timing path, trim LUT pressure,\\n+  and preserve CoreMark/MHz because the hot benchmark loop is not divider\\n+  heavy.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 8\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Remove DIV/REM from the always-hot combinational ALU path while keeping fast ALU ops and MUL-family behavior unchanged.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Add an iterative divider path in EX and hold EX/MEM advance until DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU completes.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Propagate an EX-busy stall so IF/ID/EX hold cleanly during multi-cycle divide operations without extra bubbles or double retirements.\\\"\\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Wire divider busy/done control between EX and the pipeline hazard logic while preserving the existing top-level IO and RVFI contract.\\\"\\n+  - file: test/test_alu.py\\n+    description: \\\"Re-check RV32M divide and remainder corner cases after moving divider semantics out of the single-cycle ALU implementation.\\\"\\n+  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\\n+    description: \\\"Add coverage for multi-cycle DIV/REM stalls, forwarding, and single-channel RVFI retirement behavior.\\\"\\n\\n\",\"files\":[{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-2026