s/bench\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"improvement\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"fitness\\\\\\\": 282.82, \\\\\\\"delta_pct\\\\\\\": 0.0, \\\\\\\"vs_baseline\\\\\\\": 0.0, \\\\\\\"fmax_mhz\\\\\\\": 127.03, \\\\\\\"ipc_coremark\\\\\\\": 2e-06, \\\\\\\"cycles\\\\\\\": 4491485, \\\\\\\"iterations\\\\\\\": 10, \\\\\\\"lut4\\\\\\\": 9563, \\\\\\\"ff\\\\\\\": 1866, \\\\\\\"seeds\\\\\\\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \\\\\\\"formal_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"cosim_passed\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\": null, \\\\\\\"implementation_notes\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"2026-05-15T01:37:19.468113Z\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"round_id\\\\\\\": 0, \\\\\\\"slot\\\\\\\": 0}\\\\n\\\\n  Line 2: {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260514-001-r1s0\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Move DIV/REM Off The ALU Critical Path\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current EX-stage ALU is fully combinational and includes RV32M divide\\\\\\\\nand remainder operators in its worst-case path. On the Tang Nano 20K that\\\\\\\\nlogic is likely much slower than the add/shift/branch hot path, yet\\\\\\\\nCoreMark's timed region is dominated by list/state/matrix work and appears\\\\\\\\nto use division only in cold setup code. If the divider stops limiting Fmax,\\\\\\\\na small stall cost on rare DIV/REM instructions should buy a net fitness\\\\\\\\ngain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current EX-stage ALU is fully combinational and includes RV32M divide\\\\\\\\nand remainder operators in its worst-case path. On the Tang Nano 20K that\\\\\\\\nlogic is likely... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778812088721,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_MQBbSXD2iQ3JhJpl2qQtGaM4\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":200},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r1s0 (improvement, +21.46%): Moving DIV/REM off the combinational EX ALU into a busy/stall iterative unit can improve FPGA fitness when CoreMark's timed loop is divider-cold, because shortening the add/shift/branch critical path buys more Fmax than the rare long-op stalls cost.\\\\n2: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r1s1 (regression, +16.65%): On this core's combinational IF/ID frontend, even a tiny stall-only replay buffer plus `fetch_available` hazard gating cost more than the synthetic `io_imemReady` bubbles it hid, so fetch-side caching is not a free IPC win.\\\\n3: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-003-r1s2 (regression, -15.17%): On this bench core, pushing even a static backward-branch predictor into IF by decoding `imem_data`, building the B-immediate, and muxing `next_pc` there costs more fitness than the loop-bubble savings, so frontend critical-path growth is a tighter constraint than branch IPC.\\\\n4: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r2s0 (regression, +6.35%): Splitting `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` out of `alu.sv` into an `ex_long_busy` helper regressed, so cold-op offloading only helps when timing reports show those variants are actually on the critical path and not when the extra EX stall/result-retime control becomes the new cost.\\\\n5: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.09%): When `io_dmemReady` bubbles dominate and IF timing is already tight, a one-entry MEM-side pending-store slot for aligned normal-RAM stores can improve fitness... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778812088822,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e297671f50014xrlR10ResRbrt\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"tool-calls\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"509caba115a58918f9a29bb3900ee3e886c7063e\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e29763046001vYWM6B3eD3NHHq\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-finish\\\",\\\"tokens\\\":{\\\"total\\\":41213,\\\"input\\\":40444,\\\"output\\\":253,\\\"reasoning\\\":516,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":0}},\\\"cost\\\":0}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778812090091,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e297676e9001bnZQ3krEnQKNuX\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e29767244001WKy5Rh2S3ec5RN\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"509caba115a58918f9a29bb3900ee3e886c7063e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778812131660,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2977110b002RiYKXVOQgqzXVj\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e29767244001WKy5Rh2S3ec5RN\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The prior `micro_opt` attempts confirm two things: shortening EX/MEM hot logic helped once, but adding new long-op control around high-half multiplies hurt. I’m checking whether a lighter-weight multiplier-path cleanup has already been tried before I lock the hypothesis.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778812129547,\\\"end\\\":1778812131659},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"msg_0feda3ecb652e333016a0684e16430819b8a344a19f9f5b678\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778812131687,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d689cffbffeShv80JosZNBy9u\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"cal