apply_patch\",\"callID\":\"call_XqxwjQr18VwBOhuPDLnnsjN8\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"patchText\":\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\\n+id: hyp-20260514-001-r3s0\\n+title: \\\"Share One RV32M Multiplier Datapath\\\"\\n+category: micro_opt\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current bench ALU still pays for three parallel multiply datapaths on\\n+  every EX cycle: signed*signed, unsigned*unsigned, and signed*unsigned. The\\n+  last MULH offload attempt showed that adding new long-op control can erase\\n+  the timing win, but the existing `alu.sv` structure is still a strong Fmax\\n+  risk because it duplicates wide multiply hardware even though CoreMark's hot\\n+  loop mostly needs plain low-half `MUL`.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Rework `rtl/alu.sv` so all four multiply-family ops stay single-cycle, but\\n+  are implemented from one correctly-sized shared 32x32 product datapath plus\\n+  small sign-correction logic for the high-half variants instead of three\\n+  separate products. This keeps the divider/store-slot wins intact, avoids new\\n+  EX stall or result-retime machinery, and attacks the same remaining RV32M\\n+  timing cost that motivated the failed MULH split with a much lighter control\\n+  footprint. If Yosys/nextpnr currently map the three products into duplicated\\n+  DSP or LUT fabric, collapsing them into one multiplier should improve Fmax\\n+  and area with essentially no CoreMark IPC cost.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Replace the current three-parallel multiply implementation with one shared RV32M product path and signed-high correction logic, while preserving exact MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results and the existing ALTOPS behavior.\\\"\\n+  - file: test/test_alu.py\\n+    description: \\\"Add directed MULH/MULHU/MULHSU corner cases covering mixed-sign operands, zero, and 0x80000000 overflow edges so the shared-multiplier rewrite stays RV32M-correct.\\\"\\n*** End Patch\"},\"output\":\"Success. Updated the following files:\\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\",\"metadata\":{\"diff\":\"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\\n===================================================================\\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\\n+id: hyp-20260514-001-r3s0\\n+title: \\\"Share One RV32M Multiplier Datapath\\\"\\n+category: micro_opt\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current bench ALU still pays for three parallel multiply datapaths on\\n+  every EX cycle: signed*signed, unsigned*unsigned, and signed*unsigned. The\\n+  last MULH offload attempt showed that adding new long-op control can erase\\n+  the timing win, but the existing `alu.sv` structure is still a strong Fmax\\n+  risk because it duplicates wide multiply hardware even though CoreMark's hot\\n+  loop mostly needs plain low-half `MUL`.\\n+hypothesis: |\\n+  Rework `rtl/alu.sv` so all four multiply-family ops stay single-cycle, but\\n+  are implemented from one correctly-sized shared 32x32 product datapath plus\\n+  small sign-correction logic for the high-half variants instead of three\\n+  separate products. This keeps the divider/store-slot wins intact, avoids new\\n+  EX stall or result-retime machinery, and attacks the same remaining RV32M\\n+  timing cost that motivated the failed MULH split with a much lighter control\\n+  footprint. If Yosys/nextpnr currently map the three products into duplicated\\n+  DSP or LUT fabric, collapsing them into one multiplier should improve Fmax\\n+  and area with essentially no CoreMark IPC cost.\\n+expected_impact:\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\\n+  confidence: medium\\n+changes:\\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\\n+    description: \\\"Replace the current three-parallel multiply implementation with one shared RV32M product path and signed-high correction logic, while preserving exact MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU results and the existing ALTOPS behavior.\\\"\\n+  - file: test/test_alu.py\\n+    description: \\\"Add directed MULH/MULHU/MULHSU corner cases covering mixed-sign operands, zero, and 0x80000000 overflow edges so the shared-multiplier rewrite stays RV32M-correct.\\\"\\n\\n\",\"files\":[{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\",\"relativePath\":\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\",\"type\":\"add\",\"patch\":\"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\\n===================================================================\\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r3s0.yaml\\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\\n+id: hyp-20260514-001-r3s0\\n+title: \\\"Share One RV32M Multiplier Datapath\\\"\\n+category: micro_opt\\n+motivation: |\\n+  The current bench ALU still pays for three parallel multiply datapaths on\\n+  every EX cycle: signed*signed, unsigned*unsigned, and signed*unsigned. The\\n+  last MULH offload attempt showed that adding new long-op control can erase\\n+  the timing win, but the existing `alu.sv` structure is still a strong Fmax\\n+  risk because 