onetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/v1/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n21: {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260428-014-r7s1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Single-Entry Retiring Store Buffer\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current best core gained a large Fmax and LUT win by moving DIV/REM out\\\\\\\\nof the hot EX path, so the next structural bottleneck is less likely to be\\\\\\\\nraw datapath area and more likely to be cycles lost to the random dmem\\\\\\\\nhandshake model. Today every dmem-not-ready cycle for a STORE freezes the\\\\\\\\nwhole pipeline, even though the store address, replicated data, byte mask,\\\\\\\\nand RVFI memory metadata are already known in MEM and the store produces no\\\\\\\\nregister result for younger ALU/control instructions. A prior two-entry\\\\\\\\nstore buffer proved the idea through formal and cosim but failed placement\\\\\\\\non the larger pre-DIV RTL. A smaller one-entry RAM-store buffer should retain\\\\\\\\nmost of the useful stall hiding while keeping the arbitration, state, and\\\\\\\\nplacement pressure low enough for the post-DIV design.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current best core gained a large Fmax and LUT win by moving DIV/REM out\\\\\\\\nof the hot EX path, so the next structural bottleneck is less likely to be\\\\\\\\nraw datapath area and more likely to be cycles lost to the random dmem\\\\\\\\nhandshake model. Today every dmem-not-ready cycle for a STORE freezes the\\\\\\\\nwhole pipeline, even though the store address, replicated data, byte mask,\\\\\\\\nand RVFI memory metadata are already known in MEM and the store produces no\\\\\\\\nregister result f... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n31: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810709811,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847f