":\\\".agent.hyp-20260514-001-r1s0.log\\\\n.agent.hyp-20260514-001-r2s0.log\\\\n.agent.hyp-20260514-002-r1s1.log\\\\n.agent.hyp-20260514-002-r2s1.log\\\\n.agent.hyp-20260514-003-r1s2.log\\\\n.agent.hyp-20260514-003-r2s2.log\\\\nhyp-20260514-001-r2s0.yaml\\\\nhyp-20260514-003-r2s2.yaml\\\",\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"loaded\\\":[]},\\\"title\\\":\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778810745514,\\\"end\\\":1778810745515}},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"fc_087d6483a12a8cdb016a067f7864c4819bbf95b98272a4cc98\\\"}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2961eec900113xSJeQUhLX806\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2961e543001iisyWqD53YSgnZ\\\"}}\\n42: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810745617,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2961f310001FiDKzgN7tNCl6n\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"tool-calls\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"87e16010a0ea624fc023bf5fdd5614f80b9a40a4\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2961e543001iisyWqD53YSgnZ\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-finish\\\",\\\"tokens\\\":{\\\"total\\\":80094,\\\"input\\\":652,\\\"output\\\":70,\\\"reasoning\\\":12,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":79360}},\\\"cost\\\":0}}\\n43: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810746803,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2961f7b2001qxOn9rftJlHP96\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2961f33c001M3qXMdh3M7J4O6\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"87e16010a0ea624fc023bf5fdd5614f80b9a40a4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n44: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810757431,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e29620d68002x3WumOjVZDEsvR\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2961f33c001M3qXMdh3M7J4O6\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I found that the target directory already contains agent logs and the neighboring round-2 hypothesis files, so I’m matching the existing bench hypothesis style before writing this one.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778810752360,\\\"end\\\":1778810757430},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"msg_0b25a2432b496444016a067f804440819ba07400025ac1fa1c\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}}}}\\n45: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810757453,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_Eb1XURjT4k95i8kWK7nfjUHH\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r2s0.yaml\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":200},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-001-r2s0.yaml</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: id: hyp-20260514-001-r2s0\\\\n2: title: \\\\\\\"Move Cold MULH Ops Off The EX Hot Path\\\\\\\"\\\\n3: category: micro_opt\\\\n4: motivation: |\\\\n5:   The current bench ALU still computes three separate sign/zero-extended\\\\n6:   multiply products in the one-cycle EX datapath, and each product is written\\\\n7:   as a 64-bit-by-64-bit expression even though the ISA operands are only 32\\\\n8:   bits wide. That is a strong candidate for the remaining Fmax limiter after\\\\n9:   DIV/REM was moved out of the hot path. CoreMark's timed region is multiply\\\\n10:   heavy because of the matrix kernel, but it overwhelmingly cares about plain\\\\n11:   low-half `MUL`; the high-half multiply variants are correctness-critical yet\\\\n12:   benchmark-cold.\\\\n13: hypothesis: |\\\\n14:   Keep plain `MUL` as the hot single-cycle multiply, but remove `MULH`,\\\\n15:   `MULHU`, and `MULHSU` from the always-hot combinational ALU path. In\\\\n16:   `rtl/alu.sv`, collapse the current triple-product implementation so the fast\\\\n17:   path only needs one correctly-sized low-half multiply for `MUL` plus the\\\\n18:   existing simple ALU ops. In `rtl/ex_stage.sv`, add a small cold helper for\\\\n19:   the high-half multiply variants, reusing the existing long-op stall pattern\\\\n20:   used by DIV/REM so those rare instructions remain architecturally correct\\\\n21:   without capping global Fmax. This should preserve CoreMark IPC much better\\\\n22:   than making all multiply ops... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n46: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810757472,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_Z6me8oQvBxKfxHl3K26q0DKI\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-003-r2s2.yaml\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":200},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260514-003-r2s2.yaml</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: id: hyp-20260514-003-r2s2\\\\n2: title: \\\\\\\"Tiny PC-Indexed Taken BTB\\\\\\\"\\\\n3: category: predictor\\\\n4: motivation: |\\\\n5:   The last predictor attempt lost fitness because it lengthened the frontend\\\\n6:   critical path with `imem_data` decode and branch-immediate construction in IF.\\\\n7:   But the branch penalty is still real: this core waits until EX to correct any\\\\n8:   taken control flow, so hot loops and repeated calls keep paying wrong-path\\\\n9:   fetch bubbles. The most promising predictor angle is therefore one that keeps\\\\n10:   prediction state PC-indexed and decode-free on the fetch path.\\\\n11: hypothesis: |\\\\n12:   Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer that is consulted by PC\\\\n13:   alone and predicts only previously-taken control-flow sites. IF should use a\\\\n14:   `valid/tag/target` BTB hit to fetch the remembered target instead of `pc+4`,\\\\n15:   without decoding the fetched instruction or rebuilding immediates on the hot\\\\n16:   path. EX remains the point of truth for branch direction, JAL/JALR targets,\\\\n17:   traps, and RVFI; it simply compares the resolved next PC against the carried\\\\n18:   prediction metadata, redirects on misses, and updates or invalidates the BTB\\\\n19:   entry. This should recover much of the loop/call bubble cost while avoiding\\\\n20:   the timing regression seen from instruction-driven IF prediction logic.\\\\n21: expected_impact:\\\\n22:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\\\\n... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n\\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810559846,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e295f1d65001QrJR1uv7ygRfQO\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e295f17f5001GNnDPyTjrmDAXK\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"87e16010a0ea624fc023bf5fdd5614f80b9a40a4\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810573053,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e295f4742001ZkdHG4DcVhWelu\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e295f17f5001GNnDPyTjrmDAXK\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reviewing prior `cores/bench` experiments and the current bench RTL to pick a single structural hypothesis before writing the YAML.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778810570562,\\\"end\\\":1778810573052},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"msg_08f91a9ac4adfb7b016a067eca4c508199a4e609fa3d73293b\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810573115,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"grep\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_1sbkVAXyhSle1UlCz38Nn7zz\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"category:\\\\\\\\s*structural|\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\"|structural\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments\\\",\\\"include\\\":\\\"log.jsonl\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"Found 1 matches\\\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\\\n  Line 3: {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260514-002-r1s1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Stall-Only Fetch Replay Buffer\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"structural\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The bench core turns every random `io_imemReady=0` cycle into a frontend\\\\\\\\nbubble even when the same hot-loop PC has already been fetched many times.\\\\\\\\nUnder the tournament's fixed ~22% instruction-stall model, recovering even a\\\\\\\\nfraction of those lost fetches should raise iterations/cycle without\\\\\\\\nwidening retirement or touching the already timing-sensitive EX datapath.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The bench core turns every random `io_imemReady=0` cycle into a frontend\\\\\\\\nbubble even when the same hot-loop PC has already been fetched many times.\\\\\\\\nUnder the tournament's fixed ~22% instruction-stall model, recovering even a\\\\\\\\nfraction of those lost fetches should raise iterations/cycle without\\\\\\\\nwidening retirement or touching the already timing-sensitive EX datapath.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a tiny direct-mapped instruction replay buffer in IF that records\\\\\\\\n`{pc, instr}` on successful live fetches and is consulted only when the\\\\\\\\nexternal imem port is not ready. On an imem-stall hit, IF should supply the\\\\\\\\ncached instruction and assert an effective fetch-ready signal so decode\\\\\\\\nadvances instead of seeing a forced bubble. Keep the zero-wait path direct\\\\\\\\nwhen `io_imemReady=1`, and preserve the current redirect, reset, and RVFI\\\\\\\\nretirement behavior... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810573131,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_BoOeYSHMZJEkETkNo34bWAmW\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":200},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r1s0 (improvement, +21.46%): Moving DIV/REM off the combinational EX ALU into a busy/stall iterative unit can improve FPGA fitness when CoreMark's timed loop is divider-cold, because shortening the add/shift/branch critical path buys more Fmax than the rare long-op stalls cost.\\\\n2: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r1s1 (regression, +16.65%): On this core's combinational IF/ID frontend, even a tiny stall-only replay buffer plus `fetch_available` hazard gating cost more than the synthetic `io_imemReady` bubbles it hid, so fetch-side caching is not a free IPC win.\\\\n3: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-003-r1s2 (regression, -15.17%): On this bench core, pushing even a static backward-branch predictor into IF by decoding `imem_data`, building the B-immediate, and muxing `next_pc` there costs more fitness than the loop-bubble savings, so frontend critical-path growth is a tighter constraint than branch IPC.\\\\n\\\\n(End of file - total 3 lines)\\\\n</content>\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"preview\\\":\\\"- 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r1s0 (improvement, +21.46%): Moving DIV/REM off the combinational EX ALU into a busy/stall iterative unit can improve FPGA fitness when CoreMark's timed loop is divider-cold, because shortening the add/shift/branch critical path buys more Fmax than the rare long-op stalls cost.\\\\n- 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r1s1 (regression, +16.65%): On this core's combinational IF/ID frontend, even a tiny stall-only replay buffer plus `fetch_available` hazard gating ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810573210,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"glob\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_vieOyyDfNiYjLDJycSUZVS9Y\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/*.yaml\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"No files found\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"truncated\\\":false},\\\"title\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778810573199,\\\"end\\\":1778810573209}},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"fc_08f91a9ac4adfb7b016a067eccecf081999226a046132b6a10\\\"}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e295f51440025gER9JhGEjo5Mn\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e295f17f5001GNnDPyTjrmDAXK\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778810573514,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d6a0e847ffeDUqiATilNC60cC\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e295f52c8001DpLZ6aEjiQNX5A\\\",\\\"r