,\\\"end\\\":1778827782639},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"msg_09f967431fe925cb016a06c2063b748199b80cf622cbcde2c3\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778827792879,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d59cc256ffemzPwtz6CRSLfTQ\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"apply_patch\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_tucfOkcNVXuE62U2t6ngUD08\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"patchText\\\":\\\"*** Begin Patch\\\\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\\\\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r11s2\\\\n+title: \\\\\\\"ID-Stage Exact JAL Redirect Predictor\\\\\\\"\\\\n+category: predictor\\\\n+motivation: |\\\\n+  The bench core's predictor regressions all came from spending extra logic on\\\\n+  conditional control flow: IF-path decode/BTB/RAS lookups, ID-stage branch\\\\n+  feedback, or EX-stage hold/correction machinery. `JAL` is a much cleaner\\\\n+  predictor target because it is unconditionally taken and its target is known\\\\n+  exactly from `pc + imm`, so the core can recover call and unconditional-jump\\\\n+  bubbles without paying branch-compare or history-table cost.\\\\n+hypothesis: |\\\\n+  Split the redirect path so decoded `JAL` instructions can steer fetch one\\\\n+  stage earlier from ID, while conditional branches and `JALR` stay on the\\\\n+  current EX-resolution path. The key point is that this is an exact predictor,\\\\n+  not a speculative one: ID already has the opcode, immediate, and PC, so it\\\\n+  can issue a guaranteed-correct redirect for `JAL` without adding BTB/BHT/RAS\\\\n+  state or the correction plumbing that hurt prior branch-predictor attempts.\\\\n+  If CoreMark's helper calls and unconditional jumps are frequent enough, this\\\\n+  should recover a control-flow bubble at low timing cost because the new logic\\\\n+  stays off the fragile IF `pc -> next_pc` path on ordinary fallthrough cycles\\\\n+  and avoids the branch-direction machinery that repeatedly regressed.\\\\n+expected_impact:\\\\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\\\\n+  confidence: medium\\\\n+changes:\\\\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\\\\n+    description: \\\\\\\"Detect `JAL` in decode, form an early exact redirect target from the existing `p... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778827792985,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d59cc256ffemzPwtz6CRSLfTQ\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a661257001Nnz1Jqx9IYq5Oe\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"tool-calls\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"d3afe3414d7c46c672663a5aedfb3550c60f1868\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a64d074001Z3b1fhHAutvXi6\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d59cc256ffemzPwtz6CRSLfTQ\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-finish\\\",\\\"tokens\\\":{\\\"total\\\":65601,\\\"input\\\":2310,\\\"output\\\":743,\\\"reasoning\\\":3668,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":58880}},\\\"cost\\\":0}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778827794266,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d59cc256ffemzPwtz6CRSLfTQ\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a661755001pezIEBBfMiA5cM\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a6612b7001kJevRXPOHco6A6\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d59cc256ffemzPwtz6CRSLfTQ\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"d3afe3414d7c46c672663a5aedfb3550c60f1868\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778827798523,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d59cc256ffemzPwtz6CRSLfTQ\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a662716001RBvyIhwDLzFXQu\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a6612b7001kJevRXPOHco6A6\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d59cc256ffemzPwtz6CRSLfTQ\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The hypothesis file is in place. I’m doing one quick read-back to confirm the schema-sensitive fields and relative `rtl/...` paths are correct.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778827798294,\\\"end\\\":1778827798514},\\\"metadata\\\":{\