total\\\":43710,\\\"input\\\":43133,\\\"output\\\":128,\\\"reasoning\\\":449,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":0}},\\\"cost\\\":0}}\\n5: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778828980695,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d588058affeZWwx64D7A1sL53\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a7831d6001DEbHeAAKhDEDR1\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a782d38001tvDfo9n5th3jop\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d588058affeZWwx64D7A1sL53\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"2b139e11419dfb4bdbac65dfa0bf66838ce197f1\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n6: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778828985451,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d588058affeZWwx64D7A1sL53\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_AUMpKjD93lPnPrlk6dE8flmh\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":400},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r1s0 (improvement, +21.46%): Moving DIV/REM off the combinational EX ALU into a busy/stall iterative unit can improve FPGA fitness when CoreMark's timed loop is divider-cold, because shortening the add/shift/branch critical path buys more Fmax than the rare long-op stalls cost.\\\\n2: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r1s1 (regression, +16.65%): On this core's combinational IF/ID frontend, even a tiny stall-only replay buffer plus `fetch_available` hazard gating cost more than the synthetic `io_imemReady` bubbles it hid, so fetch-side caching is not a free IPC win.\\\\n3: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-003-r1s2 (regression, -15.17%): On this bench core, pushing even a static backward-branch predictor into IF by decoding `imem_data`, building the B-immediate, and muxing `next_pc` there costs more fitness than the loop-bubble savings, so frontend critical-path growth is a tighter constraint than branch IPC.\\\\n4: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r2s0 (regression, +6.35%): Splitting `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` out of `alu.sv` into an `ex_long_busy` helper regressed, so cold-op offloading only helps when timing reports show those variants are actually on the critical path and not when the extra EX stall/result-retime control becomes the new cost.\\\\n5: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.09%): When `io_dmemReady` bubbles dominate and IF timing is already tight, a one-entry MEM-side pending-store slot for aligned normal-RAM stores can improve fitness... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n7: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778828985477,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d588058affeZWwx64D7A1sL53\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"grep\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_owiC45nOYoksMADtwhVt3Sv8\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\"|predictor|BTB|BHT|backedge|RAS|JAL redirect|branch_hold|predict_redirect\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments\\\",\\\"include\\\":\\\"log.jsonl\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"Found 13 matches\\\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\\\n  Line 4: {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260514-003-r1s2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Static Backward-Branch IF Predictor\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current bench core resolves every conditional branch in EX and always\\\\\\\\nfetches `pc+4` until that point, so taken loop branches pay a two-bubble\\\\\\\\nwrong-path recovery cost. CoreMark spends much of its timed region in short\\\\\\\\nbackward loops, making a tiny static branch predictor a strong IPC lever\\\\\\\\nwithout the LUT and routing cost of a learned table, BTB, or return stack.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current bench core resolves every conditional branch in EX and always\\\\\\\\nfetches `pc+4` until that point, so taken loop branches pay a two-bubble\\\\\\\\nwrong-path recovery cost. CoreMark spends much of its timed region in short\\\\\\\\nbackward loops, making a tiny static branch predictor a strong IPC lever\\\\\\\\nwithout the LUT and routing cost of a learned table, BTB, or return stack.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a decode-light IF-stage predictor that recognizes legal B-type branches\\\\\\\\nand predicts backward branches taken when the branch immediate is negative.\\\\\\\\nIF computes the B immediate and predicted target, carries\\\\\\\\n`predicted_taken/predicted_target` through the existing pipeline metadata,\\\\\\\\nand EX redirects only when the resolved branch next PC disagrees with that\\\\\\\\nprediction. JAL and JALR stay on the current EX redirect... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n8: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778828985493,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d588058affeZWwx64D7A1sL53\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"glob\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_1nKGvxsWvA3BK2kt0VeTtohv\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/*.yaml\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"No files found\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"count\\\":0,\\\"truncated\\\":false},\\\"title\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778828985457,\\\"end\\\":1778828985492}},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"fc_09d03325476dab54016a06c6b95528819a880a6726f23dff02\\\"}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a7844