t\\\\nplace to hide an exact control redirect.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The predictor history on `cores/bench` says the same thing repeatedly: early\\\\ncontrol recovery is real, but any always-hot IF/ID redirect path costs more\\\\nFmax than it buys back in IPC. The least-bad predictor miss so far was the\\\\nexact `JAL` redirect, which suggests the real problem was not misprediction\\\\nor correction plumbing, but paying decode-to-PC feedback on every flowing\\\\ncycle. This core already has unavoidable dead frontend windows from load-use\\\\nbubbles, `mem_wait`, and long DIV stalls, and those cycles are the cleanest\\\\nplace to hide an exact control redirect.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a `JAL`-only exact predictor that activates only when a legal `JAL` is\\\\nsitting in the decode view while an older hazard is already freezing the\\\\nfrontend. Reuse the existing decode/immediate work to latch one pending exact\\\\n`{pc,target}` entry during that otherwise-dead cycle, then when the stall\\\\nclears let IF both accept the current `JAL` into the pipeline and advance PC\\\\nto the latched target without using the normal EX kill-and-redirect path.\\\\nEX later recognizes the matching exact-predicted `JAL` and suppresses its\\\\nredundant redirect, so there is no BTB/BHT/RAS state, no branch-direction\\\\nguess, and no mispredict-correction machinery beyond the existin... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Reset-Light Divider And Store Helper State\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The strongest bench gain so far came from removing unnecessary reset load from\\\\nthe always-hot register file, but the later whole-pipeline reset-light attempt\\\\nregressed because it touched hot interstage state. The remaining reset-heavy\\\\nlogic now sits mostly in cold helper blocks: the iterative divider datapath,\\\\nthe EX-stage divide snapshot payload, and the pending-store slot in MEM.\\\\nThose words are only consumed when separate valid or state bits are asserted,\\\\nso forcing them onto reset is likely pure routing and mux cost.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The strongest bench gain so far came from removing unnecessary reset load from\\\\nthe always-hot register file, but the later whole-pipeline reset-light attempt\\\\nregressed because it touched hot interstage state. The remaining reset-heavy\\\\nlogic now sits mostly in cold helper blocks: the iterative divider datapath,\\\\nthe EX-stage divide snapshot payload, and the pending-store slot in MEM.\\\\nThose words are only consumed when separate valid or state bits are asserted,\\\\nso forcing them onto reset is likely pure routing and mux cost.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Keep the pipeline registers and frontend untouched, but make only the cold\\\\nhelper payloads resetless. In `rtl/div_unit.sv`, reset only the FSM state and\\\\noverwrite datapath registers on `start`; in `rtl/ex_stage.sv`, reset only\\\\n`div_active_q` and `div_result_valid_q` while treating the saved divide\\\\npayload as don't-care until a launch; in `rtl/mem_stage.sv`, reset only\\\\n`slot_valid_q` and let slot address, data, and mask be overwritten on\\\\nenqueue. This should preserve IPC and architectural behavior because the\\\\nexisting valid or state bits already gate every use of that data, while\\\\ncutting reset fanout and reset-data muxing in logic that sits near the\\\\nsuccessful divider and store-slot optimizations without reopening the fragile\\\\nIF or in... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-002-r13s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Predecoded MEM Request Descriptor Pipe\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Structural ideas that touched IF or made the pending-store slot smarter have\\\\nmostly regressed, but the current `mem_stage.sv` is now a dense always-hot\\\\nblock after the successful store-slot and different-word-load-bypass work.\\\\nEvery cycle it recomputes byte masks, replicated store data, aligned\\\\naddresses, misalignment checks, and slot-arbitration inputs from the raw EX\\\\npayload. Repartitioning that work is a cleaner structural target than adding\\\\nmore speculation or a more complex store buffer.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Structural ideas that touched IF or made the pending-store slot smarter have\\\\nmostly regressed, but the current `mem_stage.sv` is now a dense always-hot\\\\nblock after the successful store-slot and different-word-load-bypass work.\\\\nEvery cycle it recomputes byte masks, replicated store data, aligned\\\\naddresses, misalignment checks, and slot-arbitration inputs from the raw EX\\\\npayload. Repartitioning that work is a cleaner structural target than adding\\\\nmore speculation or a more complex store buffer.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Introduce a compact EX-generated memory-request descriptor and carry it in\\\\n`ex_mem_t` so MEM receives predecoded aligned address, byte offset/mask,\\\\nreplicated store data, and memory-op legality/classification bits for each\\\\nload or store. Keep the profitable single-entry buffered-store behavior and\\\\nthe existing different-word load bypass exactly as they are architecturally,\\\\nbut shorten the MEM combinational cone to mostly arbitration, ready/valid\\\\nhandling, load extraction, and RVFI reporting. This should buy Fmax by\\\\nsimplifying the stage that now contains the store-slot policy, without\\\\nrevisiting the fragile IF path or adding the extra retirement machinery that\\\\nearlier structural attempts showed was too expensive.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 4, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-003-r13s2\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Registered One-Cycle Exact JAL Predictor\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Predictor work on this core has repeatedly failed when it adds same-cycle\\\\ndecode or compare logic to the fragile `pc -> next_pc` path, but the exact\\\\n`JAL` redirect was the closest predictor miss so far. That suggests the bad\\\\ntrade is the direct ID-to-PC feedback loop, not the idea of recovering one\\\\nunconditional-jump bubble itself.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"Predictor work on this core has repeatedly failed when it adds same-cycle\\\\ndecode or compare logic to the fragile `pc -> next_pc` path, but the exact\\\\n`JAL` redirect was the closest predictor miss so far. That suggests the bad\\\\ntrade is the direct ID-to-PC feedback loop, not the idea of recovering one\\\\nunconditional-jump bubble itself.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a tiny deferred exact-redirect predictor for `JAL` only. When ID decodes\\\\na legal `JAL`, latch a one-entry `{valid, pc, target}` record and let IF\\\\nconsume that registered target on the following cycle instead of `pc+4`, so\\\\nthe fetch-side decision is driven only by flop outputs rather than a live\\\\ndecode/immediate/adder feedback path. Carry exact-prediction metadata into EX\\\\nso `JAL` still behaves as a normal architectural control transfer there:\\\\nEX should keep the canonical `pc_next`, `rd_wdata = pc+4`, and RVFI behavior,\\\\nand suppress only the redundant physical redirect when the registered target\\\\nalready won. This should recover one wrong-path fetch on every `JAL` or call\\\\nwith lower Fmax risk than the prior ID-stage exact redirect, while avoiding\\\\nthe rare-activation limit and architectural desynchronization bug of the\\\\nstall-window variant.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 3, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"low\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add compact exact-prediction metadata in the ID/EX payload so EX can recognize a deferred `JAL` redirect and preserve architectural `pc_next` semantics.\\\"}... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[]},\"title\":\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778831891237,\"end\":1778831891258}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_0b40e444d58370ff016a06d21314e8819aa30a156158cadc60\"}},\"id\":\"prt_e2aa49b05001PNKPzb3zwGFRaq\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d55bf01effelz3317yK3Yj9aF\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2aa45911001cditP8HmVK6LVE\"}}\n./bench/gpt-5_4_xhigh/rep1/agent.log:1577:{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778831934310,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d55bf01effelz3317yK3Yj9aF\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_vYdz73x6aRzR2sgi1F2jiAuX\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.log\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":220},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-003-r13s2.log</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830481067,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f16a9001mLh1w73NRXNnwu\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f0f98001ismmpb1RHKkJif\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"7cdcd28dde3f16a5fd60d047b488ae5cd5a1ba9e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n2: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495298,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f4b89001moqM0I32C1Dwi3\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f0f98001ismmpb1RHKkJif\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reviewing prior `predictor` experiments and lessons first so the new hypothesis avoids the known IF-path and control-path regressions.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778830494601,\\\"end\\\":1778830495297},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"msg_06a770734b5be8c2016a06cc9e7d70819a947df39ca6a57d8b\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}}}}\\n3: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495394,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"grep\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_MIu2V8jPJyFUwS9DMPRXuDU3\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\s*:\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\"|predictor|branch|JAL|BTB|BHT|RAS|backedge\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments\\\",\\\"include\\\":\\\"log.jsonl\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"Found 20 matches\\\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\\\n  Line 2: {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260514-001-r1s0\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Move DIV/REM Off The ALU Critical Path\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"micro_opt\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current EX-stage ALU is fully combinational and includes RV32M divide\\\\\\\\nand remainder operators in its worst-case path. On the Tang Nano 20K that\\\\\\\\nlogic is likely much slower than the add/shift/branch hot path, yet\\\\\\\\nCoreMark's timed region is dominated by list/state/matrix work and appears\\\\\\\\nto use division only in cold setup code. If the divider stops limiting Fmax,\\\\\\\\na small stall cost on rare DIV/REM instructions should buy a net fitness\\\\\\\\ngain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The current EX-stage ALU is fully combinational and includes RV32M divide\\\\\\\\nand remainder operators in its worst-case path. On the Tang Nano 20K that\\\\\\\\nlogic is likely much slower than the add/shift/branch hot path, yet\\\\\\\\nCoreMark's timed region is dominated by list/state/matrix work and appears\\\\\\\\nto use division only in cold setup code. If the divider stops limiting Fmax,\\\\\\\\na small stall cost on rare DIV/REM instructions should buy a net fitness\\\\\\\\ngain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Replace the single-cycle combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic with a small\\\\\\\\niterative divider in EX, while keeping ADD/logic/shift/branch and the\\\\\\\\nmultiply family on the existing fast path. EX would assert a busy condition\\\\\\\\nonly for divide/remainder ops, hold younger stages until the r... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n4: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495410,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_MNrbI4X30f5KyPCh3GkkcRgn\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/core.yaml\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":80},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/core.yaml</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: name: bench\\\\n2: description: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\\\\n3:   freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\\\\n4:   and operates only on this directory.\\\\n5: isa: rv32im\\\\n6: nret: 1\\\\n7: target_fpga: tang-nano-20k\\\\n8: targets:\\\\n9:   fmax_mhz: 135\\\\n10:   lut4: 10000\\\\n11:   coremark_iter_s: 300\\\\n12:   coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\\\\n13: current:\\\\n14:   fmax_mhz: 220.99\\\\n15:   lut4: 3164\\\\n16:   ff: 1394\\\\n17:   coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\\\\n18:   coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\\\\n19:   source_id: hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\\\\n20:   updated: '2026-05-15T06:45:15.353663Z'\\\\n\\\\n(End of file - total 20 lines)\\\\n</content>\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"preview\\\":\\\"name: bench\\\\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\\\\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\\\\n  and operates only on this directory.\\\\nisa: rv32im\\\\nnret: 1\\\\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\\\\ntargets:\\\\n  fmax_mhz: 135\\\\n  lut4: 10000\\\\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\\\\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\\\\ncurrent:\\\\n  fmax_mhz: 220.99\\\\n  lut4: 3164\\\\n  ff: 1394\\\\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\\\\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\\\\n  source_id: hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\\\\n  updated: '2026-05-15T06:45:15.353663Z'\\\",\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"loaded\\\":[]},\\\"title\\\":\\\"cores/bench/core.yaml\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778830495340,\\\"end\\\":1778830495409}},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"fc_06a770734b5be8c2016a06cc9f33e0819aab1aebf20c452805\\\"}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f4e6b0... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n5: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495412,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_3x4PrHgrfEZIJybIrtTrbgBn\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":400},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r1s0 (improvement, +21.46%): Moving DIV/REM off the combinational EX ALU into a busy/stall iterative unit can improve FPGA fitness when CoreMark's timed loop is divider-cold, because shortening the add/shift/branch critical path buys more Fmax than the rare long-op stalls cost.\\\\n2: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r1s1 (regression, +16.65%): On this core's combinational IF/ID frontend, even a tiny stall-only replay buffer plus `fetch_available` hazard gating cost more than the synthetic `io_imemReady` bubbles it hid, so fetch-side caching is not a free IPC win.\\\\n3: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-003-r1s2 (regression, -15.17%): On this bench core, pushing even a static backward-branch predictor into IF by decoding `imem_data`, building the B-immediate, and muxing `next_pc` there costs more fitness than the loop-bubble savings, so frontend critical-path growth is a tighter constraint than branch IPC.\\\\n4: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r2s0 (regression, +6.35%): Splitting `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` out of `alu.sv` into an `ex_long_busy` helper regressed, so cold-op offloading only helps when timing reports show those variants are actually on the critical path and not when the extra EX stall/result-retime control becomes the new cost.\\\\n5: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.09%): When `io_dmemReady` bubbles dominate and IF timing is already tight, a one-entry MEM-side pending-store slot for aligned normal-RAM stores can improve fitness... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n6: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495621,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f4f80001u1VwF0CDhkce0u\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"tool-calls\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"7cdcd28dde3f16a5fd60d047b488ae5cd5a1ba9e\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f0f98001ismmpb1RHKkJif\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-finish\\\",\\\"tokens\\\":{\\\"total\\\":44228,\\\"input\\\":27572,\\\"output\\\":268,\\\"reasoning\\\":516,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":15872}},\\\"cost\\\":0}}\\n7: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830497061,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f5524001H0lMXUekjiRPRx\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f5016001HmEq3mpVKjTTD0\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"7cdcd28dde3f16a5fd60d047b488ae5cd5a1ba9e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n8: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830505085,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f61d4001WVxyfdMOooAWtW\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f5016001HmEq3mpVKjTTD0\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The prior `predictor` ideas all lost in one of three ways: IF-path timing tax, always-on ID-to-PC feedback, or extra EX correction/hold machinery. I'm checking the most recent near-miss details before picking a new angle.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778830500308,\\\"end\\\":1778830505080},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"msg_02778cddbcc9ce43016a06cca43468819a9b940767f8793a42\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}}}}\\n9: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830505108,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"grep\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_3mJC6wwSMvGJtL7iL4Rus4C1\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"hyp-20260515-003-r11s2|hyp-20260515-003-r12s2|hyp-20260515-003-r10s2|hyp-20260515-003-r7s2|hyp-20260515-003-r9s2\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments\\\",\\\"include\\\":\\\"log.jsonl\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"Found 5 matches\\\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\\\n  Line 22: {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260515-003-r7s2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"