nch hot path, yet\\\\\\\\nCoreMark's timed region is dominated by list/state/matrix work and appears\\\\\\\\nto use division only in cold setup code. If the divider stops limiting Fmax,\\\\\\\\na small stall cost on rare DIV/REM instructions should buy a net fitness\\\\\\\\ngain.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Replace the single-cycle combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU logic with a small\\\\\\\\niterative divider in EX, while keeping ADD/logic/shift/branch and the\\\\\\\\nmultiply family on the existing fast path. EX would assert a busy condition\\\\\\\\nonly for divide/remainder ops, hold younger stages until the r... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495410,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_MNrbI4X30f5KyPCh3GkkcRgn\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/core.yaml\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":80},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/core.yaml</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: name: bench\\\\n2: description: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\\\\n3:   freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\\\\n4:   and operates only on this directory.\\\\n5: isa: rv32im\\\\n6: nret: 1\\\\n7: target_fpga: tang-nano-20k\\\\n8: targets:\\\\n9:   fmax_mhz: 135\\\\n10:   lut4: 10000\\\\n11:   coremark_iter_s: 300\\\\n12:   coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\\\\n13: current:\\\\n14:   fmax_mhz: 220.99\\\\n15:   lut4: 3164\\\\n16:   ff: 1394\\\\n17:   coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\\\\n18:   coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\\\\n19:   source_id: hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\\\\n20:   updated: '2026-05-15T06:45:15.353663Z'\\\\n\\\\n(End of file - total 20 lines)\\\\n</content>\\\",\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"preview\\\":\\\"name: bench\\\\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\\\\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\\\\n  and operates only on this directory.\\\\nisa: rv32im\\\\nnret: 1\\\\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\\\\ntargets:\\\\n  fmax_mhz: 135\\\\n  lut4: 10000\\\\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\\\\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\\\\ncurrent:\\\\n  fmax_mhz: 220.99\\\\n  lut4: 3164\\\\n  ff: 1394\\\\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\\\\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\\\\n  source_id: hyp-20260515-001-r10s0\\\\n  updated: '2026-05-15T06:45:15.353663Z'\\\",\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"loaded\\\":[]},\\\"title\\\":\\\"cores/bench/core.yaml\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778830495340,\\\"end\\\":1778830495409}},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"fc_06a770734b5be8c2016a06cc9f33e0819aab1aebf20c452805\\\"}},\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f4e6b0... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495412,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"read\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_3x4PrHgrfEZIJybIrtTrbgBn\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\\\",\\\"offset\\\":1,\\\"limit\\\":400},\\\"output\\\":\\\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\\\n<type>file</type>\\\\n<content>\\\\n1: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r1s0 (improvement, +21.46%): Moving DIV/REM off the combinational EX ALU into a busy/stall iterative unit can improve FPGA fitness when CoreMark's timed loop is divider-cold, because shortening the add/shift/branch critical path buys more Fmax than the rare long-op stalls cost.\\\\n2: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r1s1 (regression, +16.65%): On this core's combinational IF/ID frontend, even a tiny stall-only replay buffer plus `fetch_available` hazard gating cost more than the synthetic `io_imemReady` bubbles it hid, so fetch-side caching is not a free IPC win.\\\\n3: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-003-r1s2 (regression, -15.17%): On this bench core, pushing even a static backward-branch predictor into IF by decoding `imem_data`, building the B-immediate, and muxing `next_pc` there costs more fitness than the loop-bubble savings, so frontend critical-path growth is a tighter constraint than branch IPC.\\\\n4: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-001-r2s0 (regression, +6.35%): Splitting `MULH`/`MULHU`/`MULHSU` out of `alu.sv` into an `ex_long_busy` helper regressed, so cold-op offloading only helps when timing reports show those variants are actually on the critical path and not when the extra EX stall/result-retime control becomes the new cost.\\\\n5: - 2026-05-14 hyp-20260514-002-r2s1 (improvement, +12.09%): When `io_dmemReady` bubbles dominate and IF timing is already tight, a one-entry MEM-side pending-store slot for aligned normal-RAM stores can improve fitness... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_finish\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830495621,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f4f80001u1VwF0CDhkce0u\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"tool-calls\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"7cdcd28dde3f16a5fd60d047b488ae5cd5a1ba9e\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f0f98001ismmpb1RHKkJif\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-finish\\\",\\\"tokens\\\":{\\\"total\\\":44228,\\\"input\\\":27572,\\\"output\\\":268,\\\"reasoning\\\":516,\\\"cache\\\":{\\\"write\\\":0,\\\"read\\\":15872}},\\\"cost\\\":0}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"step_start\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830497061,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f5524001H0lMXUekjiRPRx\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f5016001HmEq3mpVKjTTD0\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"snapshot\\\":\\\"7cdcd28dde3f16a5fd60d047b488ae5cd5a1ba9e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"step-start\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830505085,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"prt_e2a8f61d4001WVxyfdMOooAWtW\\\",\\\"messageID\\\":\\\"msg_e2a8f5016001HmEq3mpVKjTTD0\\\",\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The prior `predictor` ideas all lost in one of three ways: IF-path timing tax, always-on ID-to-PC feedback, or extra EX correction/hold machinery. I'm checking the most recent near-miss details before picking a new angle.\\\",\\\"time\\\":{\\\"start\\\":1778830500308,\\\"end\\\":1778830505080},\\\"metadata\\\":{\\\"openai\\\":{\\\"itemId\\\":\\\"msg_02778cddbcc9ce43016a06cca43468819a9b940767f8793a42\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830505108,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"grep\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_3mJC6wwSMvGJtL7iL4Rus4C1\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"hyp-20260515-003-r11s2|hyp-20260515-003-r12s2|hyp-20260515-003-r10s2|hyp-20260515-003-r7s2|hyp-20260515-003-r9s2\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments\\\",\\\"include\\\":\\\"log.jsonl\\\"},\\\"output\\\":\\\"Found 5 matches\\\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\\\n  Line 22: {\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"hyp-20260515-003-r7s2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Learned EX-Stage Loop Hold Predictor\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"predictor\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Every predictor that steered fetch earlier regressed because this core's\\\\\\\\nfrontend is extremely sensitive to extra `pc -> next_pc` logic, yet the\\\\\\\\nbranch penalty is still real. The least-explored remaining predictor angle\\\\\\\\nis to leave target selection exactly where it is today and predict only\\\\\\\\nwhether a branch is worth pre-emptively holding for, so hot taken loop\\\\\\\\nbackedges lose less fetch bandwidth without paying a bubble on every static\\\\\\\\nbackedge.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"motivation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Every predictor that steered fetch earlier regressed because this core's\\\\\\\\nfrontend is extremely sensitive to extra `pc -> next_pc` logic, yet the\\\\\\\\nbranch penalty is still real. The least-explored remaining predictor angle\\\\\\\\nis to leave target selection exactly where it is today and predict only\\\\\\\\nwhether a branch is worth pre-emptively holding for, so hot taken loop\\\\\\\\nbackedges lose less fetch bandwidth without paying a bubble on every static\\\\\\\\nbackedge.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"hypothesis\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Add a tiny learned direction-only predictor that is consulted only when a\\\\\\\\nconditional branch reaches EX. Instead of changing IF or ID target\\\\\\\\nselection, remember the most recent taken backward branch PC (or a similarly\\\\\\\\ntiny exact-PC taken history)... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":1778830505112,\\\"sessionID\\\":\\\"ses_1d570f114ffeZmsYuV4IwnX0tV\\\",\\\"part\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"grep\\\",\\\"callID\\\":\\\"call_2IEDK0CM5jdphVotq75tx6DV\\\",\\\"state\\\":{\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"implementation_notes|timing|Fmax|predictor|JAL|backedge|hold\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4_xhigh-rep1/cores/bench/experiments\\\",\\