{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r13s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r13s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Partition the fast ALU path from RV32M\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current combinational ALU puts simple RV32I operations and the wide\n  shared multiplier/divider results behind one operation-selection cone.\n  CoreMark is dominated by the simple path, while the RV32M hardware still\n  contributes substantial routing and select fan-in on the EX critical path.\n  A targeted datapath partition can improve timing without adding a pipeline\n  stage or changing instruction latency.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split alu.sv into an explicitly separated fast result for ADD/SUB, logical,\n  compare, shift, and LUI operations and an RV32M result containing the\n  existing shared multiplier/sign-correction and exact DIV/REM behavior.\n  Select between those two results with a validated M-operation range, while\n  retaining the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions and all divide corner cases.\n  This should keep the common EX path away from the wide M-extension result\n  muxing and improve Tang Nano timing with no IPC or RVFI changes.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Partition the ALU into fast RV32I and RV32M result cones with an explicit M-operation select, preserving shared multiply, divide/remainder semantics, ALTOPS behavior, and the combinational interface.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r13s0\", \"title\"=>\"Partition the fast ALU path from RV32M\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"motivation\"=>\"The current combinational ALU puts simple RV32I operations and the wide\\nshared multiplier/divider results behind one operation-selection cone.\\nCoreMark is dominated by the simple path, while the RV32M hardware still\\ncontributes substantial routing and select fan-in on the EX critical path.\\nA targeted datapath partition can improve timing without adding a pipeline\\nstage or changing instruction latency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Split alu.sv into an explicitly separated fast result for ADD/SUB, logical,\\ncompare, shift, and LUI operations and an RV32M result containing the\\nexisting shared multiplier/sign-correction and exact DIV/REM behavior.\\nSelect between those two results with a validated M-operation range, while\\nretaining the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions and all divide corner cases.\\nThis should keep the common EX path away from the wide M-extension result\\nmuxing and improve Tang Nano timing with no IPC or RVFI changes.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>3, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Partition the ALU into fast RV32I and RV32M result cones with an explicit M-operation select, preserving shared multiply, divide/remainder semantics, ALTOPS behavior, and the combinational interface.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
