 through ID/EX and suppress EX-time re-resolution, or duplicate redirect and RVFI pc_next bookkeeping can fail pc_fwd even when the other formal checks pass.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:22:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Atomic direct-call queue predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Direct JAL calls have an architecturally exact target, but the current\\nqueue continues down the sequential path until EX resolves the jump.  That\\ncreates avoidable wrong-path fetch and recovery cycles on CoreMark call\\nsites.  A table-free predictor can target this deterministic case without\\nadding BTB/BHT lookup logic to the instruction-address critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Direct JAL calls have an architecturally exact target, but the current\\nqueue continues down the sequential path until EX resolves the jump.  That\\ncreates avoidable wrong-path fetch and recovery cycles on CoreMark call\\nsites.  A table-free predictor can target this deterministic case without\\nadding BTB/BHT lookup logic to the instruction-address critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Recognize only legal, word-aligned direct JAL instructions with rd=x1 at\\nthe valid queue head and predict their immediate target when the head is\\nconsumed.  Atomically discard younger sequential queue entries, fetch the\\ntarget using the same effective target for imem_addr, fetch_pc, and queued\\nentry metadata, and retain a pending target when imemReady is low.  Carry\\nprediction metadata with the call so EX suppresses the later redirect only\\nwhen the exact target was predicted; leave indirect jumps, conditional\\nbranches, misaligned targets, and all normal recovery behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-valid and predicted-target fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles for exact direct-call validation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a queue-head-only aligned direct-JAL call predictor with atomic queue replacement, target fetch-PC update, and imem-stall-safe state handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate direct-call prediction metadata through the ID/EX register without altering architectural decode controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare a predicted direct-call target with the resolved JAL target and suppress only an exact-match recovery redirect while preserving trap and RVFI next-PC behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-valid and predicted-target fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles for exact direct-call validation.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a queue-head-only aligned direct-JAL call predictor with atomic queue replacement, target fetch-PC update, and imem-stall-safe state handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate direct-call prediction metadata through the ID/EX register without altering architectural decode controls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare a predicted direct-call target with the resolved JAL target and suppress only an exact-match recovery redirect while preserving trap and RVFI next-PC behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:23:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Share the EX branch comparator\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently selects among equality, signed relational, and\\nunsigned relational operators in separate branch-case arms.  FPGA\\nsynthesis can therefore retain multiple compare cones and their muxing on\\nthe branch redirect path, adding LUT and routing pressure to an already\\ntiming-sensitive stage.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently selects among equality, signed relational, and\\nunsigned relational operators in separate branch-case arms.  FPGA\\nsynthesis can therefore retain multiple compare cones and their muxing on\\nthe branch redirect path, adding LUT and routing pressure to an already\\ntiming-sensitive stage.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the separate branch comparisons with one shared 33-bit subtract\\nand derive equality, unsigned less-than, and signed less-than from its\\nzero, borrow, and sign information.  Select only the resulting predicate\\nfor the decoded branch operation, while preserving all six RV32I branch\\nsemantics, forwarding inputs, branch-target computation, misalignment\\ntraps, redirect timing, and RVFI pc_next behavior.  Sharing the compare\\ndatapath should reduce EX logic and routing without adding a pipeline\\nstage or changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared 33-bit branch subtract/zero-detect comparator for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU, preserving forwarding, redirect, misalignment, and RVFI behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a shared 33-bit branch subtract/zero-detect comparator for BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU, preserving forwarding, redirect, misalignment, and RVFI behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 388.15, \"delta_pct\": -16.09, \"vs_baseline\": 37.24, \"fmax_mhz\": 168.83, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4349632, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10204, \"ff\": 1990, \"seeds\": [167.17, 168.83, 172.56], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T16:57:13.193610Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r8s0 (regression, -16.09%): Sharing branch predicates through a 33-bit subtract still regressed CoreMark because the subtract, signed-sign logic, and predicate selection increased EX redirect-path timing/routing, so comparator sharing must be validated after synthesis rather than assumed to reduce cones.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Predecode instructions in the fetch queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The successful two-entry prefetch queue already provides a natural elastic\\nboundary between instruction memory and the backend, but the current queue\\nstores only raw instructions.  Every queue-head transfer therefore places\\ndecoder and immediate-generation logic on the same cycle as register-file\\nreads and ID/EX capture.  That front-end combinational path can limit Fmax\\neven though the queue has already paid the cost of holding the instruction.\\nThe design is also close to its LUT budget, so the improvement should come\\nfrom repartitioning existing logic rather than adding a wider pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The successful two-entry prefetch queue already provides a natural elastic\\nboundary between instruction memory and the backend, but the current queue\\nstores only raw instructions.  Every queue-head transfer therefore places\\ndecoder and immediate-generation logic on the same cycle as register-file\\nreads and ID/EX capture.  That front-end combinational path can limit Fmax\\neven though the queue has already paid the cost of holding the instruction.\\nThe design is also close to its LUT budget, so the improvement should come\\nfrom repartitioning existing logic rather than adding a wider pipeline.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move decode and immediate generation to the instruction-accept side of the\\nexisting two-entry queue.  Each queued entry will retain the raw instruction\\nand PC for RVFI and hazard checks, plus its predecoded control bundle and\\nimmediate.  ID will consume those registered fields and only perform the\\nregister-file read and payload capture.  Decode results must be captured\\nonly when imemReady accepts a word, including the redirect refill, and the\\nqueue flush/empty paths must invalidate or zero all predecoded fields.  This\\nkeeps instruction timing, branch resolution, load-use interlocks, memory\\nbehavior, and RVFI metadata unchanged while shortening the queue-head to\\nID/EX critical path; the extra queue-entry flops are expected to be cheaper\\nthan the resulting timing margin.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend if_id_t with the registered predecoded control bundle and immediate carried by each fetch-queue entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate decode/immediate generation for accepted instruction words and store, shift, flush, and redirect-refill the predecoded fields atomically with queue entries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume predecoded control and immediate fields from if_id_t, removing the queue-head decoder and immediate-generator cones while preserving source fields and valid/flush behavior.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend if_id_t with the registered predecoded control bundle and immediate carried by each fetch-queue entry.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate decode/immediate generation for accepted instruction words and store, shift, flush, and redirect-refill the predecoded fields atomically with queue entries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume predecoded control and immediate fields from if_id_t, removing the queue-head decoder and immediate-generator cones while preserving source fields and valid/flush behavior.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: causal_ch0\\nnsn_xori_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 13:56:00 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 13:56:00 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:01 (1)\\nSBY 13:56:00 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 13:56:00 [insn_xori_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: insn_xori_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 13:56:00 [insn_xori_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_176_111 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:176.7-176.38 step 20\\nSBY 13:56:00 [insn_xori_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_177_113 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:177.7-177.40 step 20\\nSBY 13:56:00 [insn_xori_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\nmake: Target `all' not remade because of errors.\\n\\nFormal: 10 passed, 43 failed\\nFailed: causal_ch0 insn_add_ch0 insn_addi_ch0 insn_and_ch0 insn_andi_ch0 insn_auipc_ch0 insn_beq_ch0 insn_bge_ch0 insn_bgeu_ch0 insn_div_ch0 insn_divu_ch0 insn_jal_ch0 insn_jalr_ch0 insn_lb_ch0 insn_lbu_ch0 insn_lh_ch0 insn_lhu_ch0 insn_lui_ch0 insn_lw_ch0 insn_mul_ch0 insn_mulh_ch0 insn_mulhsu_ch0 insn_mulhu_ch0 insn_or_ch0 insn_ori_ch0 insn_rem_ch0 insn_remu_ch0 insn_sb_ch0 insn_sh_ch0 insn_sll_ch0 insn_slli_ch0 insn_slt_ch0 insn_slti_ch0 insn_sltiu_ch0 insn_sltu_ch0 insn_sra_ch0 insn_srai_ch0 insn_srl_ch0 insn_srli_ch0 insn_sub_ch0 insn_sw_ch0 insn_xor_ch0 insn_xori_ch0\\n\\n--- causal_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 13:55:50 [causal_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 0..\\nSBY 13:55:50 [causal_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 1..\\nSBY 13:55:50 [causal_ch0] engine_0: ## 