{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\") | {motivation,hypothesis,changes,outcome,fitness,delta_pct,fmax_mhz,cycles,lesson}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"motivation\": \"The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\\nand remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\\ntiming cost through the shared EX stage.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\\nand remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\\ntiming cost through the shared EX stage.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 32-iteration restoring divider sidecar and make DIV, DIVU, REM, and\\nREMU multi-cycle EX operations.  On a divide issue, hold the in-order\\npipeline behind EX until the sidecar completes, then inject exactly one\\nresult into the existing EX/MEM path with normal forwarding and RVFI\\nretirement.  Keep ADD/branch/load/store/MUL operations on the existing\\nsingle-cycle path, preserve divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 behavior, and\\nretain the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS combinational substitutions so formal\\nchecking remains tractable.  Removing the synthesized / and % cones from\\nthe common path should raise Fmax with limited CoreMark cycle cost.\\n\",\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"fitness_delta_pct\": 5,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    \"changes\": [\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the common ALU path while retaining ALTOPS and all non-divider RV32M operations.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add a compact iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and RV32M edge-case handling.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Issue divider operations to the sidecar, hold the in-order execute boundary while busy, and return one completed result through the existing EX/MEM metadata path.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Integrate divider busy/complete control so decode and fetch stall only for the active multi-cycle divide while retirement remains single-issue and ordered.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n        \"description\": \"Add a divider interlock with priority over normal decode progress and preserve load-use, data-bus, and redirect semantics.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the common ALU path while retaining ALTOPS and all non-divider RV32M operations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a compact iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and RV32M edge-case handling.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Issue divider operations to the sidecar, hold the in-order execute boundary while busy, and return one completed result through the existing EX/MEM metadata path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Integrate divider busy/complete control so decode and fetch stall only for the active multi-cycle divide while retirement remains single-issue and ordered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a divider interlock with priority over normal decode progress and preserve load-use, data-bus, and redirect semantics.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 435.51,\n  \"delta_pct\": -5.85,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 189.43,\n  \"cycles\": 4349632,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -5.85%): A 32-iteration DIV/REM EX sidecar can remove the combinational divider cone yet still lose on CoreMark because holding the in-order pipeline behind `divider_busy` serializes each relatively rare divide for its full latency; multi-cycle arithmetic must earn back its IPC cost in measured Fmax.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
