{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining evidence points to the EX forwarding/control network as the safest local target. I’m proposing a narrowly scoped producer-valid optimization: an EX/MEM load carries an address, not a forwardable result, so forwarding should skip it and use the already-available MEM/WB load value after the existing load-use bubble. This preserves pipeline timing and RVFI behavior while trimming a stale producer path."}}
