{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r14s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]).slice(\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"changes\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r14s0.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r14s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Suppress stale EX/MEM load forwarding\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The EX/MEM forwarding input is currently marked as a valid register\n  producer for every register-writing instruction, including loads.  In\n  EX/MEM a load's ALU result is only its address; the loaded value is not\n  available until MEM/WB, while the existing load-use interlock already\n  inserts the required bubble.  Removing this stale producer case targets\n  the EX forwarding select and operand-mux network without changing the\n  pipeline depth or adding storage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Qualify EX/MEM forwarding with the producer's `!mem_to_reg` control bit so\n  only ALU and jump results can be selected from EX/MEM.  Loads will continue\n  to forward from MEM/WB after the existing load-use interlock, preserving\n  exact architectural results, RVFI ordering, and dmem-stall behavior.  The\n  narrower producer-valid condition should reduce forwarding-control fanout\n  and avoid routing the unusable load-address result into the common EX\n  operand path, producing a small Fmax improvement with no IPC penalty.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add an EX/MEM load qualifier so address results from loads are never selected as forwarding data, while retaining EX/MEM priority for ALU and jump producers.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the EX/MEM mem_to_reg bit into the forwarding unit without changing the core IO or retirement contract.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-001-r14s0\", \"category\"=>\"micro_opt\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>2, \"confidence\"=>\"low\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add an EX/MEM load qualifier so address results from loads are never selected as forwarding data, while retaining EX/MEM priority for ALU and jump producers.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Wire the EX/MEM mem_to_reg bit into the forwarding unit without changing the core IO or retirement contract.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
