 and EX2 with an EX1-to-EX2 register will\\nseparate forwarding/operand selection from the ALU and branch-result cone.\\nKeep EX2 fully pipelined so it still accepts one instruction per cycle, and\\nupdate valid, redirect, load-use, and forwarding bookkeeping for the extra\\nstage.  The shorter combinational paths should raise Fmax enough to offset\\nthe additional taken-branch recovery cycle on CoreMark.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Retiming and control integration for the new EX1/EX2 pipeline stages, including redirect and retirement alignment.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the inter-stage payload needed to carry decoded operands, control, PC, and RVFI metadata across EX1.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split operand forwarding/selection from arithmetic and branch resolution with a registered EX1-to-EX2 boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retimed stall and flush rules for the extra execute stage and its delayed branch recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adjust producer visibility and forwarding priorities for the retimed execute pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Retiming and control integration for the new EX1/EX2 pipeline stages, including redirect and retirement alignment.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the inter-stage payload needed to carry decoded operands, control, PC, and RVFI metadata across EX1.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split operand forwarding/selection from arithmetic and branch resolution with a registered EX1-to-EX2 boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retimed stall and flush rules for the extra execute stage and its 