m\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted_taken and predicted_target metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize legal aligned backward conditional branches, compute their predicted target, and use it for next-PC selection while respecting stalls, flushes, reset, and EX redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate the IF prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and decoded control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried prediction and generate redirect only for a conditional-branch misprediction, preserving misalignment traps and RVFI next-PC semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted_taken and predicted_target metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize legal aligned backward conditional branches, compute their predicted target, and use it for next-PC selection while respecting stalls, flushes, reset, and EX redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate the IF prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and decoded control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried prediction and generate redirect only for a conditional-branch misprediction, preserving misalignment traps and RVFI next-PC semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 247.83, \"delta_pct\": -12.37, \"vs_baseline\": -12.37, \"fmax_mhz\": 106.8, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10078, \"ff\": 1897, \"seeds\": [122.99, 106.8, 105.51], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T14:46:49.428927Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -12.37%): Static BTFNT in IF was too aggressive for CoreMark\\u2014backward-branch exits and weakly taken backward branches trigger EX-time redirect/flush penalties, so fetch-side speculation must be benchmark-profiled or made selective.\"}\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Source-aware load-use hazard gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessary one-cycle\\npipeline stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessary one-cycle\\npipeline stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add precise source-use metadata for the instruction in IF/ID and gate the\\nload-use comparison with it: compare rs1 only for instructions that read\\nrs1, rs2 only for instructions that read rs2, and neither for instructions\\nwith no register sources.  Preserve the existing x0 exclusion, redirect\\nflushing, and dmem-stall priority.  Removing false bubbles should improve\\nCoreMark iterations per cycle with negligible area and timing cost while\\nleaving the architectural forwarding behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each validated RV32I/RV32M instruction class, defaulting unused sources off.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decoder's IF/ID source-use metadata to the top-level hazard-control wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use metadata from decode into the load-use hazard unit without changing the core IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each validated RV32I/RV32M instruction class, defaulting unused sources off.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decoder's IF/ID source-use metadata to the top-level hazard-control wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use metadata from decode into the load-use hazard unit without changing the core IO contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\ncd\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Status: failed\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:13 (13)\\nSBY 11:57:39 [r