{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-a2934e6\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T14:36:03.815332Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share the multiplier across RV32M high-half operations\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU currently computes three independent 64-bit products on every\\ncombinational evaluation: signed-by-signed, unsigned-by-unsigned, and\\nsigned-by-unsigned. This duplicates multiplier hardware and contributes to\\nboth the LUT budget and routing pressure on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU currently computes three independent 64-bit products on every\\ncombinational evaluation: signed-by-signed, unsigned-by-unsigned, and\\nsigned-by-unsigned. This duplicates multiplier hardware and contributes to\\nboth the LUT budget and routing pressure on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the three parallel products with one unsigned 32x32 64-bit product.\\nDerive MULH and MULHSU high halves by subtracting the appropriate sign\\ncorrection terms from that product, while retaining the same low-half MUL\\nresult and the existing ALTOPS behavior. Sharing the multiplier should\\nreduce area and routing congestion, improving Fmax without adding cycles or\\nchanging the pipeline's RV32M latency.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Use one unsigned 64-bit product and sign-correction logic for MULH and MULHSU instead of three parallel multipliers, preserving ALTOPS and exact RV32M results.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Use one unsigned 64-bit product and sign-correction logic for MULH and MULHSU instead of three parallel multipliers, preserving ALTOPS and exact RV32M results.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 404.74, \"delta_pct\": 43.11, \"vs_baseline\": 43.11, \"fmax_mhz\": 181.79, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10073, \"ff\": 1860, \"seeds\": [181.79, 175.38, 185.53], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T14:43:31.330052Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.11%): Sharing one unsigned 32x32 product and deriving MULH/MULHSU with sign-correction subtractions preserves RV32M results while eliminating duplicated multiplier hardware without adding pipeline latency.\"}\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Source-aware load-use hazard gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessary one-cycle\\npipeline stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessary one-cycle\\npipeline stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add precise source-use metadata for the instruction in IF/ID and gate the\\nload-use comparison with it: compare rs1 only for instructions that read\\nrs1, rs2 only for instructions that read rs2, and neither for instructions\\nwith no register sources.  Preserve the existing x0 exclusion, redirect\\nflushing, and dmem-stall priority.  Removing false bubbles should improve\\nCoreMark iterations per cycle with negligible area and timing cost while\\nleaving the architectural forwarding behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each validated RV32I/RV32M instruction class, defaulting unused sources off.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decoder's IF/ID source-use metadata to the top-level hazard-control wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use metadata from decode into the load-use hazard unit without changing the core IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each validated RV32I/RV32M instruction class, defaulting unused sources off.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decoder's IF/ID source-use metadata to the top-level hazard-control wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description