{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"micro_opt\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.delta_pct // \\\"\\\"),(.fitness // \\\"\\\"),(.fmax_mhz // \\\"\\\"),(.lut4 // \\\"\\\"),(.lesson // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"baseline-bench-a2934e6\tBaseline retest for cores/bench\timprovement\t0.0\t282.82\t127.03\t9563\t\nhyp-20260710-001-r1s0\tShare the multiplier across RV32M high-half operations\timprovement\t43.11\t404.74\t181.79\t10073\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.11%): Sharing one unsigned 32x32 product and deriving MULH/MULHSU with sign-correction subtractions preserves RV32M results while eliminating duplicated multiplier hardware without adding pipeline latency.\nhyp-20260710-001-r2s0\tSource-aware load-use hazard gating\tbroken\t\t\t\t\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r2s0 (broken, n/a): Gating load-use stalls with decoder-generated rs1/rs2-use metadata can remove a mandatory interlock and corrupt architectural registers; operand-use classification must be proven against every instruction's actual reads and IF/ID validity.\nhyp-20260710-001-r3s0\tShare the RV32M divide datapath\tregression\t-27.84\t333.82\t145.2\t7965\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -27.84%): Writing shared signed divide/remainder selection around separate unsigned `/` and `%` operators still computes both wide cones and adds magnitude/sign-correction logic, so RTL-level operand sharing is not sufficient to reduce divider cost without an explicitly shared or iterative datapath.\nhyp-20260710-001-r4s0\tConstrain the shared multiplier to 32-bit operands\tregression\t-25.79\t343.29\t149.32\t10571\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r4s0 (regression, -25.79%): Wrapping a 64-bit multiply result with explicitly 32-bit unsigned temporaries did not guarantee a narrower synthesized multiplier and sharply regressed CoreMark, so operand-width intent must be validated against post-synthesis timing and area rather than inferred from RTL types alone.\nhyp-20260710-001-r5s0\tFactor the EX control-flow target adder\tregression\t-17.77\t380.38\t165.45\t10089\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r5s0 (regression, -17.77%): Explicitly naming a shared `pc + imm` target in `always_comb` did not guarantee EX adder/routing reduction and regressed CoreMark, so datapath factoring must be validated after synthesis rather than assumed from RTL common-subexpression structure.\nhyp-20260710-001-r6s0\tCollapse EX forwarding into direct operand bypasses\tregression\t-36.41\t294.14\t127.94\t10338\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (regression, -36.41%): Replacing 2-bit forwarding selects with 32-bit priority-selected operands regressed CoreMark because moving the value muxing into the hazard network increased EX-path fanout/routing, so forwarding refactors must be judged on post-synthesis timing rather than mux-count alone.\nhyp-20260710-001-r7s0\tUse explicit memory lane selection\tregression\t-7.59\t427.48\t185.94\t10444\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r7s0 (regression, -7.59%): Replacing restricted-shift load extraction with nested explicit lane cases regressed CoreMark, showing that extra MEM-stage muxing and routing can outweigh the expected barrel-shifter savings and must be validated after synthesis.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
