{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r9s2.yaml && find cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses -maxdepth 1 -type f -name 'hyp-*.yaml' -print\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r9s2\ntitle: \"Queue-head loop trip-count predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark contains stable-count backward loops, but broad static backward\n  prediction mispredicts loop exits and a general BTB/BHT lookup damaged the\n  fetch timing path.  A loop predictor can target the predictable taken\n  iterations while learning the exact exit point, avoiding the systematic\n  exit penalties of BTFNT without adding a full branch target structure.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny tagged loop predictor that learns the trip count of eligible\n  backward conditional branches from EX-resolved outcomes.  At queue-head\n  consumption, predict a trained loop branch taken until its learned final\n  iteration, then predict not-taken for the exit; untrained or unstable\n  branches remain sequential.  For a taken prediction, atomically replace\n  younger queue entries and advance the registered fetch PC to the encoded\n  branch target.  Carry prediction metadata through ID/EX and recover only\n  when the resolved next PC differs, while training and all queue replacement\n  state transitions remain coordinated so RVFI PCs and stalls are unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a compact tagged loop table with trip-count learning, confidence/stability tracking, queue-head prediction, reset, and EX outcome training.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-valid, predicted-taken, and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect loop-predictor queue-head lookup, EX training, and prediction recovery without changing the RV32IM or RVFI interfaces.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Perform the registered queue-head loop prediction transaction atomically, flushing younger entries and updating fetch_pc_q to a predicted taken target while preserving redirect and imem-stall priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate loop prediction metadata with the consumed instruction into ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate predicted loop next-PC behavior against the resolved conditional branch, redirect on mismatch, and preserve alignment traps and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r9s2.yaml\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
