{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category == \\\"structural\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.fitness // \\\"-\\\"),(.delta_pct // \\\"-\\\"),(.lesson // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\tSplit execute datapath into two pipeline stages\tbroken\t-\t-\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r1s1 (broken, n/a): Splitting EX into EX1/EX2 changes producer availability, so forwarding, valid/flush, and load-use hazard logic must be derived from the exact new stage timing or dependent instructions can corrupt architectural register writes.\nhyp-20260710-002-r2s1\tAdd a decoupled instruction prefetch queue\timprovement\t462.59\t14.29\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +14.29%): A two-entry instruction prefetch queue with an independent fetch PC lets instruction-bus backpressure overlap backend/data stalls, but redirect handling must atomically invalidate queued wrong-path entries.\nhyp-20260710-002-r3s1\tDeepen the decoupled instruction prefetch FIFO\tregression\t325.83\t-29.56\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r3s1 (regression, -29.56%): Deepening the prefetch queue to a four-entry circular FIFO regressed despite preserving streaming semantics, showing that the indexed head mux and added pointer/count control can outweigh stall absorption when extra buffering is not the bottleneck.\nhyp-20260710-002-r4s1\tDecouple stores with a one-entry write buffer\tplacement_failed\t-\t-\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (placement_failed, n/a): Even a one-entry registered normal-RAM store buffer can exhaust Tang Nano 20K placement headroom—the added bus mux, buffer state, and hazard control left no BELs for the existing `dmem` `RAM16SDP4`, so store decoupling must be checked against post-synthesis resource margin rather than functional correctness alone.\nhyp-20260710-002-r5s1\tMove division into an iterative EX sidecar\tregression\t435.51\t-5.85\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -5.85%): A 32-iteration DIV/REM EX sidecar can remove the combinational divider cone yet still lose on CoreMark because holding the in-order pipeline behind `divider_busy` serializes each relatively rare divide for its full latency; multi-cycle arithmetic must earn back its IPC cost in measured Fmax.\nhyp-20260710-002-r6s1\tBypass completed loads directly into execute\tbroken\t-\t-\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): A direct MEM-to-EX load bypass must release the load-use interlock only when the same-cycle `dmem_ready` response is valid and aligned; gating the hazard solely on producer alignment can let dependents advance without a usable load value and break cosimulation.\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tResolve conditional branches at decode\tbroken\t-\t-\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r7s1 (broken, n/a): An early-resolved conditional branch must carry its resolved target/next-PC marker through ID/EX and suppress EX-time re-resolution, or duplicate redirect and RVFI pc_next bookkeeping can fail pc_fwd even when the other formal checks pass.\nhyp-20260710-002-r8s1\tPredecode instructions in the fetch queue\tbroken\t-\t-\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r8s1 (broken, n/a): Predecoded control and immediates become part of a fetch-queue entry's identity, so every push/pop, simultaneous refill, redirect refill, and flush must carry them atomically with the raw instruction and PC or formal instruction/RVFI checks fail across the ISA.\nhyp-20260710-002-r9s1\tRetimed two-slot elastic fetch buffer\tregression\t310.21\t-32.94\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r9s1 (regression, -32.94%): Replacing compact two-entry queue counting with explicit valid-bit pop/push promotion logic regressed CoreMark, showing that extra slot-valid decode and simultaneous-transition muxing can outweigh removing small arithmetic on FPGA fetch control paths.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
