{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r10s1.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]).slice(\\\"id\\\", \\\"category\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r10s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Response-gated load-use execute bypass\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The five-stage core currently inserts a full front-end bubble for every\n  load-use pair, even when the data bus returns the load in its first\n  available cycle.  CoreMark's pointer-heavy code creates enough dependent\n  loads that this costs iterations/cycle, while the existing EX/MEM-to-EX\n  bypass already provides the natural structural point for a response path.\n  The prior direct-load-bypass attempt was unsafe because it released the\n  interlock without proving that a usable same-cycle response existed.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the unconditional one-cycle load-use bubble with a response-gated\n  interlock.  Let the dependent instruction enter ID/EX, then hold that\n  instruction and the outstanding EX/MEM load only while io_dmemReady is low.\n  When the load is valid, aligned, addressed to a nonzero destination, and\n  io_dmemReady is high, forward the already extracted load value directly\n  from MEM to the dependent EX operands; otherwise retain the stall or use\n  the normal register/MEM-WB path.  Keep EX/MEM ALU forwarding disabled for\n  loads, qualify the bypass with the exact memory response and load width,\n  and preserve misalignment traps, redirect behavior, RVFI ordering, and\n  store/load bus side effects.  Removing the avoidable load-use bubble should\n  raise CoreMark IPC with only a small response mux and control change.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with a response-aware hold that stalls only when an EX/MEM load has no valid dmem response, while retaining backend stall and redirect priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a distinct EX/MEM load-response forwarding selection and prevent the ordinary ALU-result bypass from forwarding a load address as data.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add a highest-priority, response-valid load-data operand path for dependent rs1/rs2 values, falling back safely when the load is misaligned or the bus is stalled.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the existing width/sign/alignment-correct load extraction as a same-cycle bypass value, qualified by a valid aligned load response.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect dmemReady, EX/MEM load metadata, the MEM response bypass, and the retimed hazard/forwarding controls without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>5, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
