rktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r8s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-9678/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r8s1 (broken, n/a): Predecoded control and immediates become part of a fetch-queue entry's identity, so every push/pop, simultaneous refill, redirect refill, and flush must carry them atomically with the raw instruction and PC or formal instruction/RVFI checks fail across the ISA.\"}\n25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Retirement-trained ABI return stack predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current core resolves JALR returns in EX, so every correctly formed\\nfunction return first fetches sequential instructions and then flushes the\\ntwo-entry queue.  General BTB/BHT and broad static prediction already hurt\\nthis fixture through timing or exit-branch mispredictions.  ABI returns are\\na narrower opportunity because their target is an exact call-stack value.\\nThe previous RAS attempts trained from speculative queue activity; keeping\\npredictor state tied to retirement should avoid that desynchronization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current core resolves JALR returns in EX, so every correctly formed\\nfunction return first fetches sequential instructions and then flushes the\\ntwo-entry queue.  General BTB/BHT and broad static prediction already hurt\\nthis fixture through timing or exit-branch mispredictions.  ABI returns are\\na narrower opportunity because their target is an exact call-stack value.\\nThe previous RAS attempts trained from speculative queue activity; keeping\\npredictor state tied to retirement should avoid that desynchronization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small return-address stack used only for the exact RV32 ABI return\\nform JALR x0, x1, 0.  Push pc+4 when a legal JAL ra instruction retires and\\npop when a legal ABI return retires, so nested calls, stalls, and wrong-path\\nqueue contents cannot corrupt the predictor state.  At queue-head consume,\\nuse a nonempty RAS top to atomically replace the younger sequential queue\\nentries and set fetch_pc_q to the predicted return target; carry a\\npredicted-return marker through ID/EX and suppress EX recovery only when\\nthe resolved aligned JALR target exactly matches the prediction.  If the\\nstack is empty or the target mismatches, retain the existing EX redirect\\npath and architectural result.  Do not predict conditional branches,\\ndirect JALs, or other JALR forms, and keep predictor target selection out of\\nthe normal fetch lookup by using the registered queue transaction path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a compact resettable return-address stack with retirement push/pop updates, exact ABI-return qualification, top-of-stack prediction, and empty-stack handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add return-prediction-valid and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect retirement-based call/return training, queue-head return lookup, atomic prediction control, and EX validation without changing the RVFI or memory interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a registered, atomic queue replacement for a predicted ABI return, updating fetch_pc_q and queued PCs consistently while preserving redirect and imem-stall priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate the return-prediction metadata with the consumed instruction and expose the exact return qualification needed by the predictor.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Validate predicted return targets against the resolved JALR target and issue recovery only on mismatch, preserving alignment traps and RVFI pc_next semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 