\\nSBY 14:20:41 [insn_beq_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_198_153 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:198.6-198.31 step 20\\nSBY 14:20:41 [insn_beq_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-003-r9s2/formal/last_run-36910.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-003-r9s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-36910/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"scribe_skipped\": \"TimeoutError: scribe timed out after 240s\"}\n29:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r10s0\", \"title\": \"Split the RVFI retirement order counter\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The retirement order is maintained by a single 64-bit incrementer in the\\nwriteback/RVFI boundary.  That counter is not part of architectural\\nexecution, but its feedback path can still consume a long carry chain and\\nLUT routing resources on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The retirement order is maintained by a single 64-bit incrementer in the\\nwriteback/RVFI boundary.  That counter is not part of architectural\\nexecution, but its feedback path can still consume a long carry chain and\\nLUT routing resources on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the monolithic 64-bit order increment with separate low and high\\n32-bit counters.  On each valid retirement, increment the low half and\\nincrement the high half only when the low half is 0xffffffff; expose their\\nconcatenation as the unchanged 64-bit rvfi_order_0.  This should shorten\\nthe common feedback path to a 32-bit carry chain and reduce RVFI-side LUT\\npressure without changing retirement timing, pipeline behavior, or the\\nrequired exact +1 sequence across 64-bit rollover.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Split rvfi_order_q into low/high 32-bit state with explicit rollover carry, preserving reset behavior and the exact 64-bit RVFI order output.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Split rvfi_order_q into low/high 32-bit state with explicit rollover carry, preserving reset behavior and the exact 64-bit RVFI order output.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 325.08, \"delta_pct\": -29.73, \"vs_baseline\": 14.94, \"fmax_mhz\": 141.4, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4349632, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10166, \"ff\": 1981, \"seeds\": [141.4, 135.67, 144.32], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T17:35:04.081415Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r10s0 (regression, -29.73%): Splitting the RVFI 64-bit counter into low/high halves did not guarantee a shorter synthesized feedback path, and the low-half terminal compare plus high-half enable can add enough FPGA control/routing cost to overwhelm the intended carry-chain reduction.\"}\n30:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Response-gated load-use execute bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage core currently inserts a full front-end bubble for every\\nload-use pair, even when the data bus returns the load in its first\\navailable cycle.  CoreMark's pointer-heavy code creates enough dependent\\nloads that this costs iterations/cycle, while the existing EX/MEM-to-EX\\nbypass already provides the natural structural point for a response path.\\nThe prior direct-load-bypass attempt was unsafe because it released the\\ninterlock without proving that a usable same-cycle response existed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage core currently inserts a full front-end bubble for every\\nload-use pair, even when the data bus returns the load in its first\\navailable cycle.  CoreMark's pointer-heavy code creates enough dependent\\nloads that this costs iterations/cycle, while the existing EX/MEM-to-EX\\nbypass already provides the natural structural point for a response path.\\nThe prior direct-load-bypass attempt was unsafe because it released the\\ninterlock without proving that a usable same-cycle response existed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the unconditional one-cycle load-use bubble with a response-gated\\ninterlock.  Let the dependent instruction enter ID/EX, then hold that\\ninstruction and the outstanding EX/MEM load only while io_dmemReady is low.\\nWhen the load is valid, aligned, addressed to a nonzero destination, and\\nio_dmemReady is high, forward the already extracted load value directly\\nfrom MEM to the dependent EX operands; otherwise retain the stall or use\\nthe normal register/MEM-WB path.  Keep EX/MEM ALU forwarding disabled for\\nloads, qualify the bypass with the exact memory response and load width,\\nand preserve misalignment traps, redirect behavior, RVFI ordering, and\\nstore/load bus side effects.  Removing the avoidable load-use bubble should\\nraise CoreMark IPC with only a small response mux and control change.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with a response-aware hold that stalls only when an EX/MEM load has no valid dmem response, while retaining backend stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a distinct EX/MEM load-response forwarding selection and prevent the ordinary ALU-result bypass from forwarding a load address as data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a highest-priority, response-valid load-data operand path for dependent rs1/rs2 values, falling back safely when the load is misaligned or the bus is stalled.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing width/sign/alignment-correct load extraction as a same-cycle bypass value, qualified by a valid aligned load response.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect dmemReady, EX/MEM load metadata, the MEM response bypass, and the retimed hazard/forwarding controls without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with a response-aware hold that stalls only when an EX/MEM load has no valid dmem response, while retaining backend stall and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a distinct EX/MEM load-response forwarding selection and prevent the ordinary ALU-result bypass from forwarding a load address as data.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a highest-priority, response-valid load-data operand path for dependent rs1/rs2 values, falling back safely when the load is misaligned or the bus is stalled.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing width/sign/alignment-correct load extraction as a same-cycle bypass value, qualified by a valid aligned load response.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect dmemReady, EX/MEM load metadata, the MEM response bypass, and the retimed hazard/forwarding controls without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 10}\n31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Confidence-gated loop target predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, so a taken loop branch\\ndiscards younger instructions from the two-entry fetch queue.  Static\\nbackward prediction mispredicts exits, while the earlier BTB/BHT attempt\\nput an expensive lookup on the fetch timing path.  CoreMark's repeated\\nloops make a small, trained target cache a narrower opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, so a taken loop branch\\ndiscards younger instructions from the two-entry fetch queue.  Static\\nbackward prediction mispredicts exits, while the earlier BTB/BHT attempt\\nput an expensive lookup on the fetch timing path.  CoreMark's repeated\\nloops make a small, trained target cache a narrower opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a two-entry tagged loop-target table trained only by EX-resolved\\nconditional branches.  Each entry stores the branch PC, its resolved\\ntaken target, and a saturating confidence state; predict taken only after\\nrepeated same-PC taken outcomes, and stop predicting after a not-taken\\noutcome has decayed the confidence.  The queue-head lookup uses the\\nregistered target from the table rather than computing a PC-plus-immediate\\nadder on the ordinary imem address path.  On a confident hit, atomically\\nreplace younger queue contents and advance fetch to the stored target;\\ncarry the prediction with the branch and let EX recover only when the\\nresolved next PC differs.  Keep reset, imem stalls, alignment traps,\\nRVFI pc_next, and predictor training coordinated with the same queue\\ntransaction so untrained, exit, and unstable branches remain sequential.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a resettable two-entry tagged loop-target table with saturating confidence, stored targets, queue-head lookup, and EX outcome training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-valid, predicted-taken, and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor, including queue-head lookup, EX training, prediction mismatch recovery, and complete RTL source integration.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform an atomic confident-loop prediction transaction that flushes younger entries and updates fetch_pc_q from the stored target while preserving redirect and imem-ready priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate loop prediction metadata alongside the consumed instruction into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the stored prediction with the resolved conditional-branch next PC and redirect only on mismatch, preserving traps and RVFI semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a resettable two-entry tagged loop-target table with saturating confidence, stored targets, queue-head lookup, and EX outcome training.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted-valid, predicted-taken, and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and connect the predictor, including queue-head lookup, EX training, prediction mismatch recovery, and complete RTL source integration.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Perform an atomic confident-loop prediction transaction that flushes younger entries and updates fetch_pc_q from the stored target while preserving redirect and imem-ready priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate loop prediction metadata alongside the consumed instruction into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the stored prediction with the resolved conditional-branch next PC and redirect only on mismatch, preserving traps and RVFI semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 196.39, \"delta_pct\": -57.55, \"vs_baseline\": -30.56, \"fmax_mhz\": 85.7, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4363691, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 11393, \"ff\": 2156, \"seeds\": [85.7, 93.35, 84.61], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T17:42:31.493583Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r10s2 (regression, -57.55%): Confidence gating did not make a two-entry loop-target predictor cheap enough because queue-head `if_head_*` lookup, `predict_fire` target selection, and carried prediction metadata still widen the fetch/redirect control path; predictor selectivity cannot offset front-end timing overhead unless the prediction transaction is isolated from ordinary `imem_addr` selection.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
