tle\":\"Decouple stores with a one-entry write buffer\",\"outcome\":\"placement_failed\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"ipc_coremark\":null,\"error\":\"placement_failed\",\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r4s1 (placement_failed, n/a): Even a one-entry registered normal-RAM store buffer can exhaust Tang Nano 20K placement headroom—the added bus mux, buffer state, and hazard control left no BELs for the existing `dmem` `RAM16SDP4`, so store decoupling must be checked against post-synthesis resource margin rather than functional correctness alone.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\",\"title\":\"Move division into an iterative EX sidecar\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"fitness\":435.51,\"delta_pct\":-5.85,\"fmax_mhz\":189.43,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"error\":null,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -5.85%): A 32-iteration DIV/REM EX sidecar can remove the combinational divider cone yet still lose on CoreMark because holding the in-order pipeline behind `divider_busy` serializes each relatively rare divide for its full latency; multi-cycle arithmetic must earn back its IPC cost in measured Fmax.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\",\"title\":\"Bypass completed loads directly into execute\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"ipc_coremark\":null,\"error\":\"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\",\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (broken, n/a): A direct MEM-to-EX load bypass must release the load-use interlock only when the same-cycle `dmem_ready` response is valid and aligned; gating the hazard solely on producer alignment can let dependents advance without a usable load value and break cosimulation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\",\"title\":\"Resolve conditional branches at decode\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"fitness\":null,\"delta_pct\":null,\"fmax_mhz\":null,\"ipc_coremark\":null,\"error\":\"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\nde=0)\\nSBY 13:44:52 [insn_slli_ch0] e