{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis,changes,fitness,fmax_mhz,lut4,error,lesson}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\",\"title\":\"Share the RV32M divide datapath\",\"motivation\":\"The ALU currently describes separate signed division, unsigned division,\\nsigned remainder, and unsigned remainder operators.  Synthesis can therefore\\nbuild multiple large divider/remainder cones even though only one M-extension\\noperation is selected per cycle.  This adds LUT pressure and routing delay on\\nthe same timing-sensitive execute path that benefited from multiplier sharing.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The ALU currently describes separate signed division, unsigned division,\\nsigned remainder, and unsigned remainder operators.  Synthesis can therefore\\nbuild multiple large divider/remainder cones even though only one M-extension\\noperation is selected per cycle.  This adds LUT pressure and routing delay on\\nthe same timing-sensitive execute path that benefited from multiplier sharing.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the four independent `/` and `%` expressions with one unsigned\\ndivide/remainder datapath selected by the current signedness and remainder\\noperation.  Convert signed operands to magnitudes before division, then apply\\nthe architectural quotient and remainder signs; explicitly retain divide-by-\\nzero and INT_MIN/-1 overflow behavior.  Keep the existing one-cycle ALU\\ninterface and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions unchanged.  Sharing the\\ndivider logic should reduce area and routing congestion and improve Fmax\\nwithout changing instruction throughput or pipeline timing.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Share a single unsigned quotient/remainder datapath across DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU, with sign correction and explicit RV32M edge-case handling while preserving ALTOPS behavior.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Share a single unsigned quotient/remainder datapath across DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU, with sign correction and explicit RV32M edge-case handling while preserving ALTOPS behavior.\"}],\"fitness\":333.82,\"fmax_mhz\":145.2,\"lut4\":7965,\"error\":null,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r3s0 (regression, -27.84%): Writing shared signed divide/remainder selection around separate unsigned `/` and `%` operators still computes both wide cones and adds magnitude/sign-correction logic, so RTL-level operand sharing is not sufficient to reduce divider cost without an explicitly shared or iterative datapath.\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\",\"title\":\"Move division into an iterative EX sidecar\",\"motivation\":\"The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\\nand remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\\ntiming cost through the shared EX stage.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\\nand remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\\ntiming cost through the shared EX stage.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a 32-iteration restoring divider sidecar and make DIV, DIVU, REM, and\\nREMU multi-cycle EX operations.  On a divide issue, hold the in-order\\npipeline behind EX until the sidecar completes, then inject exactly one\\nresult into the existing EX/MEM path with normal forwarding and RVFI\\nretirement.  Keep ADD/branch/load/store/MUL operations on the existing\\nsingle-cycle path, preserve divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 behavior, and\\nretain the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS combinational substitutions so formal\\nchecking remains tractable.  Removing the synthesized / and % cones from\\nthe common path should raise Fmax with limited CoreMark cycle cost.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the common ALU path while retaining ALTOPS and all non-divider RV32M operations.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/divider.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a compact iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and RV32M edge-case handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Issue divider operations to the sidecar, hold the in-order execute boundary while busy, and return one completed result through the existing EX/MEM metadata path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate divider busy/complete control so decode and fetch stall only for the active multi-cycle divide while retirement remains single-issue and ordered.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a divider interlock with priority over normal decode progress and preserve load-use, data-bus, and redirect semantics.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/alu.sv\",\"description\":\"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the common ALU path while retaining ALTOPS and all non-divider RV32M operations.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/divider.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a compact iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and RV32M edge-case handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Issue divider operations to the sidecar, hold the in-order execute boundary while busy, and return one completed result through the existing EX/MEM metadata path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate divider busy/complete control so decode and fetch stall only for the active multi-cycle divide while retirement remains single-issue and ordered.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a divider interlock with priority over normal decode progress and preserve load-use, data-bus, and redirect semantics.\"}],\"fitness\":435.51,\"fmax_mhz\":189.43,\"lut4\":5838,\"error\":null,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r5s1 (regression, -5.85%): A 32-iteration DIV/REM EX sidecar can remove the combinational divider cone yet still lose on CoreMark because holding the in-order pipeline behind `divider_busy` serializes each relatively rare divide for its full latency; multi-cycle arithmetic must earn back its IPC cost in measured Fmax.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
