\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Explicitly share the PC-plus-immediate control-flow target between branches and direct JALs, retain correct JALR target formation and alignment-trap behavior, and keep the existing EX/MEM and redirect interfaces unchanged.\\\"}]}, \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 2, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Explicitly share the PC-plus-immediate control-flow target between branches and direct JALs, retain correct JALR target formation and alignment-trap behavior, and keep the existing EX/MEM and redirect interfaces unchanged.\\\"}], \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"regression\\\", \\\"fitness\\\": 380.38, \\\"delta_pct\\\": -17.77, \\\"vs_baseline\\\": 34.5, \\\"fmax_mhz\\\": 165.45, \\\"ipc_coremark\\\": 2e-06, \\\"cycles\\\": 4349632, \\\"iterations\\\": 10, \\\"lut4\\\": 10089, \\\"ff\\\": 1989, \\\"seeds\\\": [172.0, 161.79, 165.45], \\\"formal_passed\\\": true, \\\"cosim_passed\\\": true, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"implementation_notes\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-07-10T15:58:50.412214Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 5, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r5s0 (regression, -17.77%): Explicitly naming a shared `pc + imm` target in `always_comb` did not guarantee EX adder/routing reduction and regressed CoreMark, so datapath factoring must be validated after synthesis rather than assumed from RTL common-subexpression structure.\\\"}\\n15:{\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Move division into an iterative EX sidecar\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\\\\nand remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\\\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\\\\ntiming cost through the shared EX stage.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\\\\nand remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\\\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\\\\ntiming cost through the shared EX stage.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Add a 32-iteration restoring divider sidecar and make DIV, DIVU, REM, and\\\\nREMU multi-cycle EX operations.  On a divide issue, hold the in-order\\\\npipeline behind EX until the sidecar completes, then inject exactly one\\\\nresult into the existing EX/MEM path with normal forwarding and RVFI\\\\nretirement.  Keep ADD/branch/load/store/MUL operations on the existing\\\\nsingle-cycle path, preserve divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 behavior, and\\\\nretain the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS combinational substitutions so formal\\\\nchecking remains tractable.  Removing the synthesized / and % cones from\\\\nthe common path should raise Fmax with limited CoreMark cycle cost.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/alu.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the common ALU path while retaining ALTOPS and all non-divider RV32M operations.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/divider.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add a compact iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and RV32M edge-case handling.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Issue divider operations to the sidecar, hold the in-order execute boundary while busy, and return one completed result through the existing EX/MEM metadata path.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/cor