{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'replay|cache|bank|imem stall|instruction bus|memory wait|store buffer|load-use' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c1-400 | tail -n 100\"","aggregated_output":"3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Split execute datapath into two pipeline stages\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline P&R critical path runs from the ID/EX register through the\\nforwarded-operand muxes and 32-bit EX arithmetic into EX/MEM, consuming\\nroughly 4.1-4.4 ns and limiting the worst seed to 127.03 MHz.  CoreMark is\\nalready close to the LUT budget, so improvi\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Source-aware load-use hazard gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessa\n6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Add a decoupled instruction prefetch queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current fetch stage has no storage between the instruction bus and\\ndecode: every cycle with io_imemReady low injects a front-end bubble, even\\nwhen the backend is otherwise able to make progress.  The benchmark also\\ninjects independent data-bus stalls, during whic\n7:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny trained branch target predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The prior static backward-taken predictor reduced fitness because it\\npredicted loop exits and weakly taken backward branches incorrectly, while\\nits IF-side target calculation also created a severe timing regression.\\nCoreMark still has repeated conditional branches where tra\n12:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Decouple stores with a one-entry write buffer\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current MEM stage freezes the whole backend whenever io_dmemReady is\\nlow, even when the blocked operation is a store whose address and data are\\nalready fully known.  The two-entry instruction queue can hide some of\\nthose cycles, but it eventually fills while \n15:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Move division into an iterative EX sidecar\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\\nand remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary inst\n17:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Collapse EX forwarding into direct operand bypasses\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX operand path currently computes a two-bit forwarding select through\\nregister comparisons and then decodes that select in a separate pair of\\noperand muxes.  That select-then-mux structure sits directly before the\\nALU and branch comparator, adding contr\n18:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Bypass completed loads directly into execute\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage topology inserts a full bubble after every load\\nwhenever the following instruction uses the loaded register, even when the\\ndata bus is zero-wait and the load data is already available combinationally.\\nCoreMark has a dense load/use stream, so\n19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Queue-head adaptive conditional branch predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX after the two-entry fetch queue\\nhas admitted sequential instructions, so taken loop branches pay a recovery\\npenalty.  Static backward prediction was a regression because CoreMark has\\nloop exits and weakly biased bran\n21:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Resolve conditional branches at decode\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, after the two-entry fetch\\nqueue and decode have admitted sequential-path instructions.  Every taken\\nbranch therefore requires a queue flush and recovery fetch, which directly\\nreduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The prior\n24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Predecode instructions in the fetch queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The successful two-entry prefetch queue already provides a natural elastic\\nboundary between instruction memory and the backend, but the current queue\\nstores only raw instructions.  Every queue-head transfer therefore places\\ndecoder and immediate-generation logic on t\n30:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Response-gated load-use execute bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage core currently inserts a full front-end bubble for every\\nload-use pair, even when the data bus returns the load in its first\\navailable cycle.  CoreMark's pointer-heavy code creates enough dependent\\nloads that this costs iterations/cycle, while the existi\n31:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Confidence-gated loop target predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, so a taken loop branch\\ndiscards younger instructions from the two-entry fetch queue.  Static\\nbackward prediction mispredicts exits, while the earlier BTB/BHT attempt\\nput an expensive lookup on the fetch timing path.  CoreMar\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
