{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\\\") | {motivation,hypothesis,changes,error}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"motivation\":\"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, after the two-entry fetch\\nqueue and decode have admitted sequential-path instructions.  Every taken\\nbranch therefore requires a queue flush and recovery fetch, which directly\\nreduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The prior predictor experiments\\nshowed that adding speculative target logic to the fetch path is fragile\\nand can hurt timing, so moving the existing branch decision earlier is a\\nmore contained structural opportunity.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, after the two-entry fetch\\nqueue and decode have admitted sequential-path instructions.  Every taken\\nbranch therefore requires a queue flush and recovery fetch, which directly\\nreduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The prior predictor experiments\\nshowed that adding speculative target logic to the fetch path is fragile\\nand can hurt timing, so moving the existing branch decision earlier is a\\nmore contained structural opportunity.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Repartition conditional-branch handling so a valid queue-head branch is\\ncompared in ID using register-file operands plus narrowly scoped\\nEX/MEM-to-ID and MEM/WB-to-ID forwarding.  On a taken branch, atomically\\nconsume the branch, flush only younger queue entries, and restart the\\nindependent fetch PC at the aligned target; on a not-taken branch, keep\\nsequential fetch flowing without an EX-time recovery redirect.  Stall the\\nbranch when an older load has not produced a usable value, preserve the\\nexisting EX/MEM retirement payload, and carry an early-resolved marker so\\nEX does not redirect or resolve the same branch twice.  JAL/JALR, illegal\\ninstructions, misalignment traps, RVFI next-PC fields, and single-issue\\nordering remain unchanged.  Removing the normal taken-branch recovery\\nbubble should raise CoreMark IPC without a predictor table or a deeper\\nfetch structure.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":5,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate decode-stage branch resolution, early-target queue control, ID forwarding, and the existing EX redirect/trap signals while preserving RVFI retirement ordering.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add an early-branch-resolved marker and target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline payloads.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add an atomic queue-head branch consume/flush operation that uses the decode-resolved target and keeps fetch_pc_q, imem_addr, and queued PCs consistent.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose branch source operands and decoded branch metadata for early compare/target generation while retaining normal branch retirement fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add conservative ID branch interlocks for unresolved older producers, especially loads and data-bus stalls, without weakening existing load-use or redirect stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Suppress duplicate EX-time conditional-branch redirects for early-resolved branches and preserve branch RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment-trap behavior.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate decode-stage branch resolution, early-target queue control, ID forwarding, and the existing EX redirect/trap signals while preserving RVFI retirement ordering.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add an early-branch-resolved marker and target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline payloads.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add an atomic queue-head branch consume/flush operation that uses the decode-resolved target and keeps fetch_pc_q, imem_addr, and queued PCs consistent.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose branch source operands and decoded branch metadata for early compare/target generation while retaining normal branch retirement fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add conservative ID branch interlocks for unresolved older producers, especially loads and data-bus stalls, without weakening existing load-use or redirect stalls.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Suppress duplicate EX-time conditional-branch redirects for early-resolved branches and preserve branch RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment-trap behavior.\"}],\"error\":\"formal_failed: pc_fwd_ch0\\nde=0)\\nSBY 13:44:52 [insn_slli_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 13:44:52 [insn_slli_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:05 (5)\\nSBY 13:44:52 [insn_slli_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:04 (4)\\nSBY 13:44:52 [insn_slli_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 13:44:52 [insn_slli_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 13:44:52 [insn_slli_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:56  Status: passed\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:56 (56)\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:54 (54)\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\\nSBY 13:45:34 [reg_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: pc_fwd_ch0\\n\\n--- pc_fwd_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 13:44:38 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 8..\\nSBY 13:44:38 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 9..\\nSBY 13:44:38 [pc_fw