{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r11s1.yaml; test -f cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r11s1.yaml && echo 'hypothesis file present'\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r11s1\ntitle: \"Register the memory request/response boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current MEM stage leaves the EX/MEM address on the external data-memory\n  port and feeds the combinational RAM result, lane extraction, and MEM/WB\n  capture in one long timing path.  That path is especially costly on the\n  Tang Nano wrapper, where the dmem array is part of the synthesized design.\n  A small elastic boundary can isolate address generation from RAM response\n  timing without adding storage to the instruction front end.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split memory access into a registered request stage and a response stage.\n  Capture the aligned address, write data, byte enables, load width/sign\n  metadata, and the complete RVFI payload in a one-entry memory-request\n  register; drive the dmem ports only from that stable register and capture\n  the returned word in the following response register.  Keep a bypass path\n  for non-memory instructions and use valid/ready interlocks so memory\n  requests remain ordered, held stable across io_dmemReady stalls, and can\n  accept one request per cycle after filling.  Preserve precise traps,\n  load/store masks, RVFI retirement order, and the existing two-entry fetch\n  queue while shortening the EX-to-RAM and RAM-to-writeback timing cones.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add the registered memory-request/response payload and valid metadata needed to preserve ordering and all RVFI fields across the split memory boundary.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement the elastic request and response stages, stable dmem signaling during stalls, registered load extraction, and precise misalignment handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate memory-stage ready/valid flow with the existing EX/MEM, MEM/WB, forwarding, and single-channel RVFI retirement boundary.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add conservative backpressure for a full or waiting memory request while allowing the prefetch queue and independent non-memory pipeline flow to continue safely.\"\nhypothesis file present\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
