{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r12s1.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]).slice(\\\"id\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"expected_impact\\\",\\\"changes\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r12s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Decouple the backend around a single memory slot\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The proven two-entry fetch queue already hides instruction-bus stalls, but\n  a data-bus stall still freezes EX, ID, and writeback behind the instruction\n  in EX/MEM.  With roughly 22% randomized dmem backpressure, this makes an\n  otherwise independent stream pay the full memory response latency and\n  leaves the front-end's available buffering underused.\nhypothesis: |\n  Restructure the backend as an in-order decoupled execute path plus a\n  one-entry memory transaction slot.  Capture a load/store request and its\n  complete RVFI metadata in the slot, explicitly distinguish request\n  acceptance from response-valid, and let independent non-memory results\n  advance into a small ordered completion holding register while the slot\n  waits.  Commit memory and younger results in original program order, block\n  only when the holding capacity or a memory dependency is exhausted, and\n  keep MMIO and misaligned accesses on the conservative blocking path.  This\n  should overlap dmem stalls with useful ALU/branch work without changing the\n  top-level buses, retirement width, or instruction-fetch queue.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add explicit memory-request, completion-holding, and age/valid metadata while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement a stable one-entry request/response slot with separate request-accepted and response-valid state, exact load extraction, store masks, and precise trap handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the decoupled memory slot and ordered completion path with EX, writeback, forwarding, and single-channel RVFI retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace the global dmem-stall freeze with conservative capacity, dependency, and in-order-commit interlocks.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Retire completed memory and non-memory results in age order without duplicate register writes or RVFI orders.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r12s1\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>6, \"confidence\"=>\"low\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add explicit memory-request, completion-holding, and age/valid metadata while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Implement a stable one-entry request/response slot with separate request-accepted and response-valid state, exact load extraction, store masks, and precise trap handling.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Integrate the decoupled memory slot and ordered completion path with EX, writeback, forwarding, and single-channel RVFI retirement.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Replace the global dmem-stall freeze with conservative capacity, dependency, and in-order-commit interlocks.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Retire completed memory and non-memory results in age order without duplicate register writes or RVFI orders.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
