{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r13s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Fall-through fetch response into decode\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The successful two-entry prefetch queue hides sustained instruction-bus\n  stalls, but its empty-to-nonempty transition still costs a bubble: a ready\n  instruction is first written into slot zero and can only be consumed on the\n  following cycle.  Under the benchmark's randomized iStall pattern, queue\n  drains and redirect recovery make this refill latency recurring.  The core\n  has substantial Fmax headroom, so recovering these front-end cycles is a\n  better structural target than adding more queue state.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a fall-through response path in the existing two-entry fetch queue.  When\n  the queue is empty, the bus is ready, and decode is able to accept an\n  instruction, present the current fetch response directly as the IF/ID view\n  and advance fetch_pc_q without storing and re-reading that word.  If decode\n  stalls, retain the normal enqueue behavior; if EX redirects, suppress the\n  bypass and atomically refill from the redirect target.  Keep the bypass\n  disabled during redirect and propagate the effective availability signal to\n  hazard logic so load-use bubbles cannot consume or drop an unheld response.\n  This removes empty-queue refill bubbles without changing the top-level bus,\n  single-retirement RVFI contract, or the proven compact queue steady state.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an empty-queue, ready-response fall-through path with atomic consume-versus-enqueue handling, while preserving redirect flush and fetch PC updates.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Use the fall-through IF/ID valid view for consume and connect its effective availability to the existing pipeline control without changing RVFI ports.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Treat a ready fall-through instruction as non-empty for stall and flush decisions, retaining load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect priority.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
