{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r14s1.yaml && ruby -e \\\"require 'yaml'; YAML.load_file('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r14s1.yaml'); puts 'YAML OK'\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r14s1\ntitle: \"Early conditional-branch resolution in decode\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The proven two-entry instruction queue already overlaps instruction stalls,\n  but conditional branches still resolve in EX and flush younger queued work\n  on taken paths. CoreMark has frequent loop and control-flow branches, so\n  removing that recovery penalty is a higher-value structural opportunity than\n  adding more queue state. The earlier decode attempt failed on PC-forwarding\n  bookkeeping, making an explicit next-PC transaction and conservative EX\n  fallback essential.\nhypothesis: |\n  Repartition conditional-branch resolution so a valid queue-head branch is\n  compared in ID using register-file operands plus narrowly scoped forwarding\n  from EX/MEM and MEM/WB. When the operands are unavailable because an older\n  load is outstanding, hold the branch and use the existing EX resolution;\n  otherwise compute the aligned target and next PC in ID, flush only younger\n  queue contents atomically, and carry an early-resolved marker and resolved\n  next PC through ID/EX. EX must treat that marker as authoritative, suppress\n  duplicate redirects, and preserve the marker's pc_next and trap behavior.\n  This should remove taken-branch recovery cycles without adding predictor\n  tables, widening the ordinary fetch address path, or changing RVFI ordering.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add early-branch-valid, early-next-PC, and target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so branch identity and RVFI pc_next remain aligned through stalls and flushes.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement decode-stage conditional-branch comparison, immediate target formation, alignment qualification, and operand forwarding inputs while retaining a conservative unresolved path.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the early branch decision with queue consume/flush control and ensure the existing load-use and data-stall priorities prevent a branch from advancing without valid operands.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Honor the carried early-resolution transaction, suppress duplicate EX redirects for resolved branches, and retain normal EX resolution and misalignment trapping for fallback branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Stall decode-stage branches only for genuinely unavailable older load results and preserve redirect, dmem-stall, and queue-empty precedence.\"\nYAML OK\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
