arithmetic\\ncones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\\nfew DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\\ntiming cost through the shared EX stage.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 32-iteration restoring divider sidecar and make DIV, DIVU, REM, and\\nREMU multi-cycle EX operations.  On a divide issue, hold the in-order\\npipeline behind EX until the sidecar completes, then inject exactly one\\nresult into the existing EX/MEM path with normal forwarding and RVFI\\nretirement.  Keep ADD/branch/load/store/MUL operations on the existing\\nsingle-cycle path, preserve divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 behavior, and\\nretain the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS combinational substitutions so formal\\nchecking remains tractable.  Removing the synthesized / and % cones from\\nthe common path should raise Fmax with limited CoreMark cycle cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the common ALU path while retaining ALTOPS and all non-divider RV32M operations.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and RV32M edge-case handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Issue divider operations to the sidecar, hold the in-order execute boundary while busy, and return one completed result through the existing EX/MEM metadata path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate divider busy/complete control so decode and fetch stall only for the active multi-cycle divide while retirement remains single-issue and ordered.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divider interlock with priority over normal decode progress and preserve load-use, data-bus, and redirect semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"