orktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r8s1/formal/last_run-9678.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r8s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-9678/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r9s1\",\"title\":\"Retimed two-slot elastic fetch buffer\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-32.94,\"fitness\":310.21,\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the count-based two-entry queue control with a fixed two-slot\\nelastic buffer using explicit valid bits and direct slot-0/slot-1\\ntransitions.  Keep the independent sequential fetch PC and the existing\\none-word-per-cycle refill behavior, but eliminate count increment/decrement\\nand general FIFO indexing from the normal path.  A normal consume promotes\\nslot 1 only when valid, a consume-plus-refill replaces or appends directly,\\nand redirect atomically clears both slots while accepting the target word\\ninto slot 0 when io_imemReady is high.  Preserve the exact queue-head PC and\\ninstruction pairing, imem-stall behavior, redirect priority, and all valid\\nsemantics so the backend and RVFI timing remain unchanged.  The reduced\\ncontrol fanout and simpler next-state muxing should improve Fmax without\\npaying the area and timing cost of a deeper queue.\\n\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Restructure the two-entry prefetch queue around explicit slot-valid state and direct normal, simultaneous refill, and redirect transitions while preserving PC/instruction atomicity and handshake behavior.\"}],\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"error\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r10s1\",\"title\":\"Response-gated load-use execute bypass\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the unconditional one-cycle load-use bubble with a response-gated\\ninterlock.  Let the dependent instruction enter ID/EX, then hold that\\ninstruction and the outstanding EX/MEM load only while io_dmemReady is low.\\nWhen the load is valid, aligned, addressed to a nonzero destination, and\\nio_dmemReady is high, forward the already extracted load value directly\\nfrom MEM to the dependent EX operands; otherwise retain the stall or use\\nthe normal register/MEM-WB path.  Keep EX/MEM ALU forwarding disabled for\\nloads, qualify the bypass with the exact memory response and load width,\\nand preserve misalignment traps, redirect behavior, RVFI ordering, and\\nstore/load bus side effects.  Removing the avoidable load-use bubble should\\nraise CoreMark IPC with only a small response mux and control change.\\n\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the unconditional load-use bubble with a response-aware hold that stalls only when an EX/MEM load has no valid dmem response, while retaining backend stall and redirect priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a distinct EX/MEM load-response forwarding selection and prevent the ordinary ALU-result bypass from forwarding a load address as data.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a highest-priority, response-valid load-data operand path for dependent rs1/rs2 values, falling back safely when the load is misaligned or the bus is stalled.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Expose the existing width/sign/alignment-correct load extraction as a same-cycle bypass value, qualified by a valid aligned load response.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect dmemReady, EX/MEM load metadata, the MEM response bypass, and the retimed hazard/forwarding controls without changing the top-level IO or RVFI contract.\"}],\"implementation_notes\":null,\"error\":\"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r11s1\",\"title\":\"Register the memory request/response boundary\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"hypothesis\":\"Split memory access into a registered request stage and a response stage.\\nCapture the aligned address, write data, byte enables, load width/sign\\nmetadata, and the complete RVFI payload in a one-entry memory-request\\nregister; drive the dmem ports only from that stable register and capture\\nthe returned word in the following response register.  Keep a bypass path\\nfor non-memory instructions and use valid/ready interlocks so memory\\nrequests remain ordered, held stable across io_dmemReady stalls, and can\\naccept one request per cycle after filling.  Preserve precise traps,\\nload/store masks, RVFI retirement order, and the existing two-entry fetch\\nqueue while shortening the EX-to-RAM and RAM-to-writeback timing cones.\\n\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add the registered memory-request/response payload and valid metadata needed to preserve ordering and all RVFI fields across the split memory boundary.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement the elastic request and response stages, stable dmem signaling during stalls, registered load extraction, and precise misalignment handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate memory-stage ready/valid flow with the existing EX/MEM, MEM/WB, forwarding, and single-channel RVFI retirement boundary.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Add conservative backpressure for a full or waiting memory request while allowing the prefetch queue and independent non-memory pipeline flow to continue safely.\"}],\"implementation_notes\":null,\"error\":\"formal_failed: insn_lb_ch0\\nt__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_190_142 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:190.9-190.59 step 20\\nSBY 14:59:15 [insn_lhu_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_insn_check_sv_190_149 at rvfi_insn_check.sv:190.9-190.59 step 20\\nSBY 14:59:15 [insn_lhu_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\nSBY 14:59:15 [insn_sw_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:02  Checking assertions in step 20..\\nSBY 14:59:15 [insn_sw_ch0] en