omplete RVFI metadata in the slot, explicitly distinguish request\\nacceptance from response-valid, and let independent non-memory results\\nadvance into a small ordered completion holding register while the slot\\nwaits.  Commit memory and younger results in original program order, block\\nonly when the holding capacity or a memory dependency is exhausted, and\\nkeep MMIO and misaligned accesses on the conservative blocking path.  This\\nshould overlap dmem stalls with useful ALU/branch work without changing the\\ntop-level buses, retirement width, or instruction-fetch queue.\\n\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add explicit memory-request, completion-holding, and age/valid metadata while preserving the existing RVFI payload fields.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a stable one-entry request/response slot with separate request-accepted and response-valid state, exact load extraction, store masks, and precise trap handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the decoupled memory slot and ordered completion path with EX, writeback, forwarding, and single-channel RVFI retirement.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the global dmem-stall freeze with conservative capacity, dependency, and in-order-commit interlocks.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/wb_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Retire completed memory and non-memory results in age order without duplicate register writes or RVFI orders.\"}],\"implementation_notes\":null,\"error\":\"placement_failed\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r13s1\",\"title\":\"Fall-through fetch response into decode\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"delta_pct\":-35.34,\"fitness\":299.09,\"hypothesis\":\"Add a fall-through response path in the existing two-entry fetch queue.  When\\nthe queue is empty, the bus is ready, and decode is able to accept an\\ninstruction, present the current fetch response directly as the IF/ID view\\nand advance fetch_pc_q without storing and re-reading that word.  If decode\\nstalls, retain the normal enqueue behavior; if EX redirects, suppress the\\nbypass and atomically refill from the redirect target.  Keep the bypass\\ndisabled during redirect and propagate the effective availability signal to\\nhazard logic so load-use bubbles cannot consume or drop an unheld response.\\nThis removes empty-queue refill bubbles without changing the top-level bus,\\nsingle-retirement RVFI contract, or the proven compact queue steady state.\\n\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add an empty-queue, ready-response fall-through path with atomic consume-versus-enqueue handling, while preserving redirect flush and fetch PC updates.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Use the fall-through IF/ID valid view for consume and connect its effective availability to the existing pipeline control without changing RVFI ports.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Treat a ready fall-through instruction as non-empty for stall and flush decisions, retaining load-use, dmem-stall, and redirect priority.\"}],\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"error\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r14s1\",\"title\":\"Early conditional-branch resolution in decode\",\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"delta_pct\":null,\"fitness\":null,\"hypothesis\":\"Repartition conditional-branch resolution so a valid queue-head branch is\\ncompared in ID using register-file operands plus narrowly scoped forwarding\\nfrom EX/MEM and MEM/WB. When the operands are unavailable because an older\\nload is outstanding, hold the branch and use the existing EX resolution;\\notherwise compute the aligned target and next PC in ID, flush only younger\\nqueue contents atomically, and carry an early-resolved marker and resolved\\nnext PC through ID/EX. EX must treat that marker as authoritative, suppress\\nduplicate redirects, and preserve the marker's pc_next and trap behavior.\\nThis should remove taken-branch recovery cycles without adding predictor\\ntables, widening the ordinary fetch address path, or changing RVFI ordering.\\n\",\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add early-branch-valid, early-next-PC, and target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so branch identity and RVFI pc_next remain aligned through stalls and flushes.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement decode-stage conditional-branch comparison, immediate target formation, alignment qualification, and operand forwarding inputs while retaining a conservative unresolved path.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the early branch decision with queue consume/flush control and ensure the existing load-use and data-stall priorities prevent a branch from advancing without valid operands.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Honor the carried early-resolution transaction, suppress duplicate EX redirects for resolved branches, and retain normal EX resolution and misalignment trapping for fallback branches.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Stall decode-stage branches only for genuinely unavailable older load results and preserve redirect, dmem-stall, and queue-empty precedence.\"}],\"implementation_notes\":null,\"error\":\"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
