ace.vcd\\nSBY 15:48:03 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_55 at rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 step 20\\nSBY 15:48:03 [pc_fwd_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-003-r13s2/formal/last_run-24544.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-003-r13s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-24544/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 13, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r13s2 (broken, n/a): A registered RAS response cannot be treated as a decode-only `prediction_wait`; queue pop, prediction-token capture, fetch-target update, and EX recovery must share one valid transaction or a stalled return loses instruction identity and fails RVFI `pc_fwd` and register checks.\"}\n41:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r14s0\", \"title\": \"Suppress stale EX/MEM load forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM forwarding input is currently marked as a valid register\\nproducer for every register-writing instruction, including loads.  In\\nEX/MEM a load's ALU result is only its address; the loaded value is not\\navailable until MEM/WB, while the existing load-use interlock already\\ninserts the required bubble.  Removing this stale producer case targets\\nthe EX forwarding select and operand-mux network without changing the\\npipeline depth or adding storage.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX/MEM forwarding input is currently marked as a valid register\\nproducer for every register-writing instruction, including loads.  In\\nEX/MEM a load's ALU result is only its address; the loaded value is not\\navailable until MEM/WB, while the existing load-use interlock already\\ninserts the required bubble.  Removing this stale producer case targets\\nthe EX forwarding select and operand-mux network without changing the\\npipeline depth or adding storage.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Qualify EX/MEM forwarding with the producer's `!mem_to_reg` control bit so\\nonly ALU and jump results can be selected from EX/MEM.  Loads will continue\\nto forward from MEM/WB after the existing load-use interlock, preserving\\nexact architectural results, RVFI ordering, and dmem-stall behavior.  The\\nnarrower producer-valid condition should reduce forwarding-control fanout\\nand avoid routing the unusable load-address result into the common EX\\noperand path, producing a small Fmax improvement with no IPC penalty.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an EX/MEM load qualifier so address results from loads are never selected as forwarding data, while retaining EX/MEM priority for ALU and jump producers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX/MEM mem_to_reg bit into the forwarding unit without changing the core IO or retirement contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an EX/MEM load qualifier so address results from loads are never selected as forwarding data, while retaining EX/MEM priority for ALU and jump producers.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the EX/MEM mem_to_reg bit into the forwarding unit without changing the core IO or retirement contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 377.02, \"delta_pct\": -18.5, \"vs_baseline\": 33.31, \"fmax_mhz\": 163.99, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4349632, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10583, \"ff\": 1982, \"seeds\": [163.99, 186.36, 159.21], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T19:00:20.882808Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r14s0 (regression, -18.50%): Qualifying both EX/MEM forwarding selects with `!mem_to_reg` regressed CoreMark, showing that added producer-control gating and fanout can outweigh pruning an unusable load-address bypass, so narrow forwarding optimizations still require post-synthesis timing validation.\"}\n42:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r14s1\", \"title\": \"Early conditional-branch resolution in decode\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The proven two-entry instruction queue already overlaps instruction stalls,\\nbut conditional branches still resolve in EX and flush younger queued work\\non taken paths. CoreMark has frequent loop and control-flow branches, so\\nremoving that recovery penalty is a higher-value structural opportunity than\\nadding more queue state. The earlier decode attempt failed on PC-forwarding\\nbookkeeping, making an explicit next-PC transaction and conservative EX\\nfallback essential.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The proven two-entry instruction queue already overlaps instruction stalls,\\nbut conditional branches still resolve in EX and flush younger queued work\\non taken paths. CoreMark has frequent loop and control-flow branches, so\\nremoving that recovery penalty is a higher-value structural opportunity than\\nadding more queue state. The earlier decode attempt failed on PC-forwarding\\nbookkeeping, making an explicit next-PC transaction and conservative EX\\nfallback essential.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Repartition conditional-branch resolution so a valid queue-head branch is\\ncompared in ID using register-file operands plus narrowly scoped forwarding\\nfrom EX/MEM and MEM/WB. When the operands are unavailable because an older\\nload is outstanding, hold the branch and use the existing EX resolution;\\notherwise compute the aligned target and next PC in ID, flush only younger\\nqueue contents atomically, and carry an early-resolved marker and resolved\\nnext PC through ID/EX. EX must treat that marker as authoritative, suppress\\nduplicate redirects, and preserve the marker's pc_next and trap behavior.\\nThis should remove taken-branch recovery cycles without adding predictor\\ntables, widening the ordinary fetch address path, or changing RVFI ordering.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add early-branch-valid, early-next-PC, and target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so branch identity and RVFI pc_next remain aligned through stalls and flushes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement decode-stage conditional-branch comparison, immediate target formation, alignment qualification, and operand forwarding inputs while retaining a conservative unresolved path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate the early branch decision with queue consume/flush control and ensure the existing load-use and data-stall priorities prevent a branch from advancing without valid operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the carried early-resolution transaction, suppress duplicate EX redirects for resolved branches, and retain normal EX resolution and misalignment trapping for fallback branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Stall decode-stage branches only for genuinely unavailable older load results and preserve redirect, dmem-stall, and queue-empty precedence.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add early-branch-valid, early-next-PC, and target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles so branch identity and RVFI pc_next remain aligned through stalls and flushes.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement decode-stage conditional-branch comparison, immediate target formation, alignment qualification, and operand forwarding inputs while retaining a conservative unresolved path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Integrate the early branch decision with queue consume/flush control and ensure the existing load-use and data-stall priorities prevent a branch from advancing without valid operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Honor the carried early-resolution transaction, suppress duplicate EX redirects for resolved branches, and retain normal EX resolution and misalignment trapping for fallback branches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Stall decode-stage branches only for genuinely unavailable older load results and preserve redirect, dmem-stall, and queue-empty precedence.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14}\n43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Shadow-link-register return predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark contains frequent ABI returns, but JALR resolution currently waits\\nfor EX and flushes sequential fetch. General BTB/BHT and RAS attempts either\\nhurt Fmax or lost instruction identity across queue stalls. The common ABI\\nreturn target is already the architectural x1 value, so a narrowly scoped\\npredictor can avoid a tag table, stack management, and target-add arithmetic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark contains frequent ABI returns, but JALR resolution currently waits\\nfor EX and flushes sequential fetch. General BTB/BHT and RAS attempts either\\nhurt Fmax or lost instruction identity across queue stalls. The common ABI\\nreturn target is already the architectural x1 value, so a narrowly scoped\\npredictor can avoid a tag table, stack management, and target-add arithmetic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Maintain a registered shadow of architectural x1 from the writeback stream\\nand predict only a valid queue-head JALR with rd=x0, rs1=x1, and imm=0 when\\nno older in-flight instruction can still write x1. Use x1 with bit zero\\ncleared as the target, atomically replace younger prefetch entries and the\\nfetch PC with that target, and carry a prediction token and target through\\nID/EX. EX suppresses its redirect only for an aligned exact match; all\\nhazards, shadow misses, non-ABI JALRs, and mismatches use the existing\\nconservative recovery path. Keep the predictor state transaction aligned\\nwith queue consume/refill and imem stalls so a stalled return cannot retag\\nits instruction or violate RVFI pc_next ordering.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Track the committed x1 shadow, conservatively gate return prediction on older x1 writers, and wire the atomic predictor transaction between ID, IF, and EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add return-prediction-valid and predicted-target fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads while preserving the RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize the exact queue-head ABI return and atomically flush younger entries, issue the shadow-x1 target, and retain a pending target across imem stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Qualify the exact ABI return and latch its prediction token and target with the consumed instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the carried shadow-link prediction with the resolved aligned JALR target and suppress recovery only on an exact match.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Track the committed x1 shadow, conservatively gate return prediction on older x1 writers, and wire the atomic predictor transaction between ID, IF, and EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add return-prediction-valid and predicted-target fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads while preserving the RVFI metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize the exact queue-head ABI return and atomically flush younger entries, issue the shadow-x1 target, and retain a pending target across imem stalls.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Qualify the exact ABI return and latch its prediction token and target with the consumed instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the carried shadow-link prediction with the resolved aligned JALR target and suppress recovery only on an exact match.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
