{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Add a decoupled instruction prefetch queue\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current fetch stage has no storage between the instruction bus and\n  decode: every cycle with io_imemReady low injects a front-end bubble, even\n  when the backend is otherwise able to make progress.  The benchmark also\n  injects independent data-bus stalls, during which the current pipeline stops\n  fetching and cannot use those cycles to build up useful instruction supply.\n  A small queue targets this structural coupling without changing retirement\n  width or the architectural memory behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the direct combinational IF-to-ID path with a two-entry instruction\n  prefetch queue and an independent fetch PC.  Fetch into an available queue\n  slot whenever the instruction bus is ready, while decode consumes the head\n  whenever the pipeline is not stalled; simultaneous dequeue/enqueue keeps the\n  queue streaming at one instruction per cycle.  A redirect must atomically\n  invalidate both queued entries and restart fetching at the resolved target,\n  and an empty queue must stall decode rather than capture an invalid\n  instruction.  This should hide a portion of random instruction-bus latency\n  behind data stalls and other backend bubbles, improving CoreMark\n  iterations/cycle with only a small amount of front-end state.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the fetch-queue valid/consume handshake so decode stalls only when the queue is empty, while preserving redirect priority and existing RVFI retirement ordering.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the single PC/combinational IF payload with a two-entry prefetch queue, independent fetch pointer, simultaneous fill/drain logic, and redirect flush/restart handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Retarget front-end stall and flush decisions to the queue-empty/consume handshake, keeping load-use, dmem-stall, and wrong-path invalidation behavior correct.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
