{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.yaml && sed -n '1,240p' schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Decouple stores with a one-entry write buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current MEM stage freezes the whole backend whenever io_dmemReady is\n  low, even when the blocked operation is a store whose address and data are\n  already fully known.  The two-entry instruction queue can hide some of\n  those cycles, but it eventually fills while the store remains in EX/MEM.\n  A small in-order store buffer targets this remaining structural coupling\n  without adding a second retirement channel or widening the core.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a one-entry registered store buffer between the EX/MEM producer and the\n  data bus.  Capture a store's aligned address, replicated write data, byte\n  mask, and retirement metadata once it reaches MEM, then let the pipeline\n  continue with younger non-memory instructions while the buffered write waits\n  for io_dmemReady.  Preserve strict memory ordering by backpressuring a\n  younger load or store until the older buffered store drains, and keep the\n  existing load path blocking until its response is accepted.  The buffer's\n  registered bus drive removes store-induced backend bubbles under the\n  benchmark's random dStall model, while its single-entry interface avoids the\n  indexed FIFO timing cost seen in the failed four-entry fetch experiment.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/store_buffer.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry in-order store buffer that holds address, data, byte mask, valid state, and ready-to-drain handshake for the dmem bus.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Define the minimal store-buffer payload or control fields needed to separate buffered stores from the normal MEM/WB retirement payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the store buffer between EX/MEM and dmem, allowing non-memory instructions to advance while preserving ordered blocking for younger memory operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Split store acceptance from load response handling and emit store-buffer enqueue, drain, and busy signals without changing RVFI fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Stall only when a younger memory operation would violate the single-entry store buffer's ordering, while retaining load-use and data-stall interlocks.\"\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
