{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && rg -n 'critical|timing|MHz|stall|branch|queue|pipeline' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 40\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\\\")' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && rg -n 'critical|timing|MHz|stall|branch|queue|pipeline' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 40\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\",\"title\":\"Add a decoupled instruction prefetch queue\",\"category\":\"structural\",\"motivation\":\"The current fetch stage has no storage between the instruction bus and\\ndecode: every cycle with io_imemReady low injects a front-end bubble, even\\nwhen the backend is otherwise able to make progress.  The benchmark also\\ninjects independent data-bus stalls, during which the current pipeline stops\\nfetching and cannot use those cycles to build up useful instruction supply.\\nA small queue targets this structural coupling without changing retirement\\nwidth or the architectural memory behavior.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current fetch stage has no storage between the instruction bus and\\ndecode: every cycle with io_imemReady low injects a front-end bubble, even\\nwhen the backend is otherwise able to make progress.  The benchmark also\\ninjects independent data-bus stalls, during which the current pipeline stops\\nfetching and cannot use those cycles to build up useful instruction supply.\\nA small queue targets this structural coupling without changing retirement\\nwidth or the architectural memory behavior.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Replace the direct combinational IF-to-ID path with a two-entry instruction\\nprefetch queue and an independent fetch PC.  Fetch into an available queue\\nslot whenever the instruction bus is ready, while decode consumes the head\\nwhenever the pipeline is not stalled; simultaneous dequeue/enqueue keeps the\\nqueue streaming at one instruction per cycle.  A redirect must atomically\\ninvalidate both queued entries and restart fetching at the resolved target,\\nand an empty queue must stall decode rather than capture an invalid\\ninstruction.  This should hide a portion of random instruction-bus latency\\nbehind data stalls and other backend bubbles, improving CoreMark\\niterations/cycle with only a small amount of front-end state.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the fetch-queue valid/consume handshake so decode stalls only when the queue is empty, while preserving redirect priority and existing RVFI retirement ordering.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single PC/combinational IF payload with a two-entry prefetch queue, independent fetch pointer, simultaneous fill/drain logic, and redirect flush/restart handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Retarget front-end stall and flush decisions to the queue-empty/consume handshake, keeping load-use, dmem-stall, and wrong-path invalidation behavior correct.\"}]},\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the fetch-queue valid/consume handshake so decode stalls only when the queue is empty, while preserving redirect priority and existing RVFI retirement ordering.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Replace the single PC/combinational IF payload with a two-entry prefetch queue, independent fetch pointer, simultaneous fill/drain logic, and redirect flush/restart handling.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Retarget front-end stall and flush decisions to the queue-empty/consume handshake, keeping load-use, dmem-stall, and wrong-path invalidation behavior correct.\"}],\"outcome\":\"improvement\",\"fitness\":462.59,\"delta_pct\":14.29,\"vs_baseline\":63.56,\"fmax_mhz\":201.21,\"ipc_coremark\":0.000002,\"cycles\":4349632,\"iterations\":10,\"lut4\":10155,\"ff\":1990,\"seeds\":[198.57,209.34,201.21],\"formal_passed\":true,\"cosim_passed\":true,\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-07-10T15:12:39.953390Z\",\"slot\":1,\"round_id\":2,\"lesson\":\"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r2s1 (improvement, +14.29%): A two-entry instruction prefetch queue with an independent fetch PC lets instruction-bus backpressure overlap backend/data stalls, but redirect handling must atomically invalidate queued wrong-path entries.\"}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share the multiplier across RV32M high-half operations\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU currently computes three independent 64-bit products on every\\ncombinational evaluation: signed-by-signed, unsigned-by-unsigned, and\\nsigned-by-unsigned. This duplicates multiplier hardware and contributes to\\nboth the LUT budget and routing pressure on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU currently computes three independent 64-bit products on every\\ncombinational evaluation: signed-by-signed, unsigned-by-unsigned, and\\nsigned-by-unsigned. This duplicates multiplier hardware and contributes to\\nboth the LUT budget and routing pressure on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the three parallel products with one unsigned 32x32 64-bit product.\\nDerive MULH and MULHSU high halves by subtracting the appropriate sign\\ncorrection terms from that product, while retaining the same low-half MUL\\nresult and the existing ALTOPS behavior. Sharing the multiplier should\\nreduce area and routing congestion, improving Fmax without adding cycles or\\nchanging the pipeline's RV32M latency.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Use one unsigned 64-bit product and sign-correction logic for MULH and MULHSU instead of three parallel multipliers, preserving ALTOPS and exact RV32M results.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Use one unsigned 64-bit product and sign-correction logic for MULH and MULHSU instead of three parallel multipliers, preserving ALTOPS and exact RV32M results.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 404.74, \"delta_pct\": 43.11, \"vs_baseline\": 43.11, \"fmax_mhz\": 181.79, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10073, \"ff\": 1860, \"seeds\": [181.79, 175.38, 185.53], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T14:43:31.330052Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r1s0 (improvement, +43.11%): Sharing one unsigned 32x32 product and deriving MULH/MULHSU with sign-correction subtractions preserves RV32M results while eliminating duplicated multiplier hardware without adding pipeline latency.\"}\n3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Split execute datapath into two pipeline stages\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline P&R critical path runs from the ID/EX register through the\\nforwarded-operand muxes and 32-bit EX arithmetic into EX/MEM, consuming\\nroughly 4.1-4.4 ns and limiting the worst seed to 127.03 MHz.  CoreMark is\\nalready close to the LUT budget, so improving timing through retiming is a\\nmore promising structural lever than widening the machine.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline P&R critical path runs from the ID/EX register through the\\nforwarded-operand muxes and 32-bit EX arithmetic into EX/MEM, consuming\\nroughly 4.1-4.4 ns and limiting the worst seed to 127.03 MHz.  CoreMark is\\nalready close to the LUT budget, so improving timing through retiming is a\\nmore promising structural lever than widening the machine.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Retiming the execute path into EX1 and EX2 with an EX1-to-EX2 register will\\nseparate forwarding/operand selection from the ALU and branch-result cone.\\nKeep EX2 fully pipelined so it still accepts one instruction per cycle, and\\nupdate valid, redirect, load-use, and forwarding bookkeeping for the extra\\nstage.  The shorter combinational paths should raise Fmax enough to offset\\nthe additional taken-branch recovery cycle on CoreMark.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Retiming and control integration for the new EX1/EX2 pipeline stages, including redirect and retirement alignment.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the inter-stage payload needed to carry decoded operands, control, PC, and RVFI metadata across EX1.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split operand forwarding/selection from arithmetic and branch resolution with a registered EX1-to-EX2 boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retimed stall and flush rules for the extra execute stage and its delayed branch recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Adjust producer visibility and forwarding priorities for the retimed execute pipeline.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Retiming and control integration for the new EX1/EX2 pipeline stages, including redirect and retirement alignment.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the inter-stage payload needed to carry decoded operands, control, PC, and RVFI metadata across EX1.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split operand forwarding/selection from arithmetic and branch resolution with a registered EX1-to-EX2 boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retimed stall and flush rules for the extra execute stage and its delayed branch recovery.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\