{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r5s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r5s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r5s1\ntitle: \"Move division into an iterative EX sidecar\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current combinational ALU contains both signed and unsigned divide\n  and remainder operators on the EX critical path.  Those wide arithmetic\n  cones consume LUTs and routing even though CoreMark executes relatively\n  few DIV/REM instructions, while every ordinary instruction pays their\n  timing cost through the shared EX stage.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 32-iteration restoring divider sidecar and make DIV, DIVU, REM, and\n  REMU multi-cycle EX operations.  On a divide issue, hold the in-order\n  pipeline behind EX until the sidecar completes, then inject exactly one\n  result into the existing EX/MEM path with normal forwarding and RVFI\n  retirement.  Keep ADD/branch/load/store/MUL operations on the existing\n  single-cycle path, preserve divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 behavior, and\n  retain the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS combinational substitutions so formal\n  checking remains tractable.  Removing the synthesized / and % cones from\n  the common path should raise Fmax with limited CoreMark cycle cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real DIV/REM operators from the common ALU path while retaining ALTOPS and all non-divider RV32M operations.\"\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact iterative signed/unsigned quotient-remainder unit with start, busy, done, and RV32M edge-case handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Issue divider operations to the sidecar, hold the in-order execute boundary while busy, and return one completed result through the existing EX/MEM metadata path.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate divider busy/complete control so decode and fetch stall only for the active multi-cycle divide while retirement remains single-issue and ordered.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a divider interlock with priority over normal decode progress and preserve load-use, data-bus, and redirect semantics.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
