{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r6s1.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r6s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\ntitle: \"Bypass completed loads directly into execute\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage topology inserts a full bubble after every load\n  whenever the following instruction uses the loaded register, even when the\n  data bus is zero-wait and the load data is already available combinationally.\n  CoreMark has a dense load/use stream, so this structural coupling costs IPC\n  independently of the instruction prefetch improvement.\nhypothesis: |\n  Repartition the MEM-to-EX boundary with a direct load-result bypass.  When a\n  load in EX/MEM has a valid, aligned response and io_dmemReady is high, feed\n  the extracted byte/halfword/word value directly into the EX operand mux of\n  the younger dependent instruction and allow ID/EX to advance without the\n  load-use bubble.  Keep the existing MEM/WB capture and forwarding path as\n  the architectural retirement path, and retain the interlock whenever the\n  response is stalled, the access is misaligned, or the producer is not a\n  completed load.  This should improve CoreMark iterations per cycle with\n  only a localized bypass mux and no additional pipeline storage.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose a valid direct-load-forward value using the existing load extraction and alignment checks, without changing MEM/WB or RVFI fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add MEM-to-EX load-data selection with correct priority over ALU forwarding and preserve all normal operand, branch, and trap behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Suppress the load-use bubble only for a completed aligned load response; continue stalling for dmem backpressure and unsafe cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the load-forward value and valid handshake from MEM to EX and hazard control while preserving the top-level IO and single retirement channel.\"\n{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\", \"title\"=>\"Bypass completed loads directly into execute\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"motivation\"=>\"The current five-stage topology inserts a full bubble after every load\\nwhenever the following instruction uses the loaded register, even when the\\ndata bus is zero-wait and the load data is already available combinationally.\\nCoreMark has a dense load/use stream, so this structural coupling costs IPC\\nindependently of the instruction prefetch improvement.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Repartition the MEM-to-EX boundary with a direct load-result bypass.  When a\\nload in EX/MEM has a valid, aligned response and io_dmemReady is high, feed\\nthe extracted byte/halfword/word value directly into the EX operand mux of\\nthe younger dependent instruction and allow ID/EX to advance without the\\nload-use bubble.  Keep the existing MEM/WB capture and forwarding path as\\nthe architectural retirement path, and retain the interlock whenever the\\nresponse is stalled, the access is misaligned, or the producer is not a\\ncompleted load.  This should improve CoreMark iterations per cycle with\\nonly a localized bypass mux and no additional pipeline storage.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>4, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Expose a valid direct-load-forward value using the existing load extraction and alignment checks, without changing MEM/WB or RVFI fields.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add MEM-to-EX load-data selection with correct priority over ALU forwarding and preserve all normal operand, branch, and trap behavior.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Suppress the load-use bubble only for a completed aligned load response; continue stalling for dmem backpressure and unsafe cases.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Wire the load-forward value and valid handshake from MEM to EX and hazard control while preserving the top-level IO and single retirement channel.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
