{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r7s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r7s1\ntitle: \"Resolve conditional branches at decode\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Conditional branches currently resolve in EX, after the two-entry fetch\n  queue and decode have admitted sequential-path instructions.  Every taken\n  branch therefore requires a queue flush and recovery fetch, which directly\n  reduces CoreMark iterations per cycle.  The prior predictor experiments\n  showed that adding speculative target logic to the fetch path is fragile\n  and can hurt timing, so moving the existing branch decision earlier is a\n  more contained structural opportunity.\nhypothesis: |\n  Repartition conditional-branch handling so a valid queue-head branch is\n  compared in ID using register-file operands plus narrowly scoped\n  EX/MEM-to-ID and MEM/WB-to-ID forwarding.  On a taken branch, atomically\n  consume the branch, flush only younger queue entries, and restart the\n  independent fetch PC at the aligned target; on a not-taken branch, keep\n  sequential fetch flowing without an EX-time recovery redirect.  Stall the\n  branch when an older load has not produced a usable value, preserve the\n  existing EX/MEM retirement payload, and carry an early-resolved marker so\n  EX does not redirect or resolve the same branch twice.  JAL/JALR, illegal\n  instructions, misalignment traps, RVFI next-PC fields, and single-issue\n  ordering remain unchanged.  Removing the normal taken-branch recovery\n  bubble should raise CoreMark IPC without a predictor table or a deeper\n  fetch structure.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate decode-stage branch resolution, early-target queue control, ID forwarding, and the existing EX redirect/trap signals while preserving RVFI retirement ordering.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add an early-branch-resolved marker and target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an atomic queue-head branch consume/flush operation that uses the decode-resolved target and keeps fetch_pc_q, imem_addr, and queued PCs consistent.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose branch source operands and decoded branch metadata for early compare/target generation while retaining normal branch retirement fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add conservative ID branch interlocks for unresolved older producers, especially loads and data-bus stalls, without weakening existing load-use or redirect stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress duplicate EX-time conditional-branch redirects for early-resolved branches and preserve branch RVFI pc_wdata and misalignment-trap behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
