{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The structural history has one clear success: the two-entry decoupled fetch queue. The other structural attempts either changed producer timing, added expensive buffering, or stalled correctness. I’m selecting a contained follow-on: predecode each instruction as it enters that existing queue, so the ID/EX boundary no longer pays decoder/immediate-generation logic while preserving the five-stage execution and branch timing."}}
