tored target;\n  carry the prediction with the branch and let EX recover only when the\n  resolved next PC differs.  Keep reset, imem stalls, alignment traps,\n  RVFI pc_next, and predictor training coordinated with the same queue\n  transaction so untrained, exit, and unstable branches remain sequential.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a resettable two-entry tagged loop-target table with saturating confidence, stored targets, queue-head lookup, and EX outcome training.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted-valid, predicted-taken, and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and connect the predictor, including queue-head lookup, EX training, prediction mismatch recovery, and complete RTL source integration.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Perform an atomic confident-loop prediction transaction that flushes younger entries and updates fetch_pc_q from the stored target while preserving redirect and imem-ready priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate loop prediction metadata alongside the consumed instruction into ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the stored prediction with the resolved conditional-branch next PC and redirect only on mismatch, preserving traps and RVFI semantics.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
