{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r11s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Retirement-trained ABI return stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The bench core resolves indirect ABI returns in EX, so every correctly\n  behaved function return still flushes or waits behind the two-entry fetch\n  queue.  Earlier broad branch predictors lost heavily because tag/counter\n  lookup and target selection were placed on the normal fetch timing path.\n  CoreMark has a frequent, exact return form that can be predicted with a\n  very small structure and without direction speculation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a four-entry return-address stack trained only when legal direct calls\n  and ABI returns retire.  Recognize only JALR x0, x1, 0 at the valid queue\n  head, and predict it when the stack is nonempty; use the registered stack\n  top as the target, carry a prediction marker with that instruction, and\n  suppress EX recovery only on an exact aligned match.  Push pc+4 for JAL ra\n  and pop for the matching return at retirement, so wrong-path queue entries\n  and stalls cannot corrupt predictor state.  Isolate the prediction request\n  from the ordinary sequential imem address path and preserve atomic queue\n  flush/refill, imem stalls, RVFI pc_next, and normal recovery on misses.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a compact four-entry retirement-trained ABI return-address stack with top-of-stack lookup, push/pop handling, reset, and exact return-form qualification.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add prediction-valid and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect retirement call/return training, queue-head return prediction, and the prediction recovery path while preserving the existing core and RVFI interfaces.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an atomic, queue-head-only return prediction transaction that uses a registered target request, flushes younger sequential entries, and preserves the two-entry queue and imem handshake semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate return prediction metadata with the consumed instruction into ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare predicted return targets with the resolved JALR next PC and redirect only on mismatch or an unpredicted return, retaining alignment traps and RVFI next-PC correctness.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
