BY 11:50:24 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:06  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:06  Status: failed\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:07 (7)\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:04 (4)\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 step 20\\nSBY 11:50:25 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFull run log: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r1s1/formal/last_run-60451.log\\nPer-check logs in: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_6-luna-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20260710-002-r1s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-60451/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r1s1 (broken, n/a): Splitting EX into EX1/EX2 changes producer availability, so forwarding, valid/flush, and load-use hazard logic must be derived from the exact new stage timing or dependent instructions can corrupt architectural register writes.\"}\n4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static backward-branch taken predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage bench core resolves conditional branches in EX and fetches\\nsequentially until then, so taken loop branches flush younger instructions.\\nCoreMark contains many tight backward branches with a strongly taken bias;\\nrecovering those bubbles is a direct iterations-per-cycle opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage bench core resolves conditional branches in EX and fetches\\nsequentially until then, so taken loop branches flush younger instructions.\\nCoreMark contains many tight backward branches with a strongly taken bias;\\nrecovering those bubbles is a direct iterations-per-cycle opportunity.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a decode-light static BTFNT predictor in IF for legal, word-aligned\\nB-type conditional branches whose immediate is negative. Compute pc plus\\nthe branch immediate in IF and fetch from that target immediately, while\\ncarrying predicted_taken and predicted_target through IF/ID and ID/EX.\\nEX should redirect only when the resolved architectural next PC differs from\\nthe carried prediction; mispredictions still flush normally and RVFI\\npc_wdata continues to report the resolved next PC. Keep JAL and JALR on\\ntheir existing EX-resolution paths so this remains a single predictor change.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted_taken and predicted_target metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize legal aligned backward conditional branches, compute their predicted target, and use it for next-PC selection while respecting stalls, flushes, reset, and EX redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate the IF prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and decoded control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried prediction and generate redirect only for a conditional-branch misprediction, preserving misalignment traps and RVFI next-PC semantics.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted_taken and predicted_target metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize legal aligned backward conditional branches, compute their predicted target, and use it for next-PC selection while respecting stalls, flushes, reset, and EX redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate the IF prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and decoded control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried prediction and generate redirect only for a conditional-branch misprediction, preserving misalignment traps and RVFI next-PC semantics.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 247.83, \"delta_pct\": -12.37, \"vs_baseline\": -12.37, \"fmax_mhz\": 106.8, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10078, \"ff\": 1897, \"seeds\": [122.99, 106.8, 105.51], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T14:46:49.428927Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -12.37%): Static BTFNT in IF was too aggressive for CoreMark\\u2014backward-branch exits and weakly taken backward branches trigger EX-time redirect/flush penalties, so fetch-side speculation must be benchmark-profiled or made selective.\"}\n5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Source-aware load-use hazard gating\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessary one-cycle\\npipeline stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessary one-cycle\\npipeline stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add precise source-use metadata for the instruction in IF/ID and gate the\\nload-use comparison with it: compare rs1 only for instructions that read\\nrs1, rs2 only for instructions that read rs2, and neither for instructions\\nwith no register sources.  Preserve the existing x0 exclusion, redirect\\nflushing, and dmem-stall priority.  Removing false bubbles should improve\\nCoreMark iterations per cycle with negligible area and timing cost while\\nleaving the architectural forwarding behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each validated RV32I/RV32M instruction class, defaulting unused sources off.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decoder's IF/ID source-use metadata to the top-level hazard-control wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use metadata from decode into the load-use hazard unit without changing the core IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each validated RV32I/RV32M instruction class, defaulting unused sources off.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decoder's IF/ID source-use metadata to the top-level hazard-control wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use metadata from decode into the load-use hazard unit without changing the core IO contract.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"formal_failed: reg_ch0\\ncd\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace_tb.v\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace.smtc\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace.yw\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:12  Status: failed\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:13 (13)\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:10 (10)\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: reg_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_reg_check_sv_42_56 at rvfi_reg_check.sv:42.6-42.59 step 20\\nSBY 11:57:39 [reg_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\\n\\nFormal: 52 passed, 1 failed\\nFailed: reg_ch0\\n\\n--- reg_ch0/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\\nSBY 11:57:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 9..\\nSBY 11:57:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 10..\\nSBY 11:57:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 11..\\nSBY 11:57:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 12..\\nSBY 11:57:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 13..\\nSBY 11:57:27 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:00  Skipping step 14..\\nSBY 11:57:27