l_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-10T17:42:31.493583Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r10s2 (regression, -57.55%): Confidence gating did not make a two-entry loop-target predictor cheap enough because queue-head `if_head_*` lookup, `predict_fire` target selection, and carried prediction metadata still widen the fetch/redirect control path; predictor selectivity cannot offset front-end timing overhead unless the prediction transaction is isolated from ordinary `imem_addr` selection.\"}\n34:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r11s2\", \"title\": \"Retirement-trained ABI return stack predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench core resolves indirect ABI returns in EX, so every correctly\\nbehaved function return still flushes or waits behind the two-entry fetch\\nqueue.  Earlier broad branch predictors lost heavily because tag/counter\\nlookup and target selection were placed on the normal fetch timing path.\\nCoreMark has a frequent, exact return form that can be predicted with a\\nvery small structure and without direction speculation.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core resolves indirect ABI returns in EX, so every correctly\\nbehaved function return still flushes or waits behind the two-entry fetch\\nqueue.  Earlier broad branch predictors lost heavily because tag/counter\\nlookup and target selection were placed on the normal fetch timing path.\\nCoreMark has a frequent, exact return form that can be predicted with a\\nvery small structure and without direction speculation.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a four-entry return-address stack trained only when legal direct calls\\nand ABI returns retire.  Recognize only JALR x0, x1, 0 at the valid queue\\nhead, and predict it when the stack is nonempty; use the registered stack\\ntop as the target, carry a prediction marker with that instruction, and\\nsuppress EX recovery only on an exact aligned match.  Push pc+4 for JAL ra\\nand pop for the matching return at retirement, so wrong-path queue entries\\nand stalls cannot corrupt predictor state.  Isolate the prediction request\\nfrom the ordinary sequential imem address path and preserve atomic queue\\nflush/refill, imem stalls, RVFI pc_next, and normal recovery on misses.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a compact four-entry retirement-trained ABI return-address stack with top-of-stack lookup, push/pop handling, reset, and exact return-form qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add prediction-valid and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX pipeline bundles.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Connect retirement call/return training, queue-head return prediction, and the prediction recovery path while preserving the existing core and RVFI interfaces.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an atomic, queue-head-only return prediction transaction that uses a registered target request, flushes younger sequential entries, and preserves the two-entry queue and imem handshake semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Propagate return prediction metadata with the consumed instruction into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare predicted return targets with the resolved JALR next PC and redirect only on mismatch or an unpredicted return, retaining alignment traps and RVFI next-PC correctness.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Implement a compact four-entry retirement-trained ABI return-address stack with top-of-stack lookup, push/pop handling, reset, and exact return-form qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \