{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r13s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Transaction-safe return stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark contains frequent ABI function returns, but the current EX-only\n  JALR resolution flushes younger sequential fetches. Broad target predictors\n  previously hurt Fmax, while the prior return-stack attempt was functionally\n  broken because stack state and prediction metadata lost instruction identity\n  across queue stalls and flushes.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a compact four-entry return-address stack that predicts only the exact\n  ABI return form JALR x0, x1, 0 when a valid queue-head transaction has a\n  registered nonempty stack top. Train it only at retirement: push the retiring\n  pc+4 for direct JAL x1 calls and pop only for a retiring matching return, so\n  wrong-path instructions cannot mutate predictor state. Carry a prediction\n  token and target atomically with each queue entry through pop/refill and\n  ID/EX; use one effective target for fetch PC, queue contents, and recovery.\n  EX suppresses redirect only for an aligned exact match, and all misses,\n  stalls, traps, and non-ABI JALRs retain the conservative path. Keep lookup\n  off the ordinary sequential imem-address critical path by issuing the\n  registered target request only as an atomic return-prediction transaction.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a resettable four-entry retirement-trained RAS with strict call/return qualification, nonempty top lookup, and push/pop ordering.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add prediction token, target, and transaction identity fields to IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so stalls and queue replacement cannot retag a return.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the RAS lookup and retirement training while preserving single-issue RVFI ordering, precise traps, and source-list inclusion.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an atomic queue-head return-prediction request that uses the registered RAS target, invalidates younger entries, and keeps fetch PC and queued target identity consistent.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the return prediction token and target with the consumed instruction into ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved JALR return target with the carried prediction token and redirect only on mismatch or an unpredicted return, retaining alignment-trap behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
