{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"predictor\\\") | [.id, .title, (.hypothesis.hypothesis // \\\"\\\"), ((.changes // []) | map(.file) | join(\\\",\\\"))] | \\\"\\\\nID: \\\\(. [0])\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(. [1])\\\\nHYP: \\\\(. [2])\\\\nFILES: \\\\(. [3])\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\nTITLE: Static backward-branch taken predictor\nHYP: Add a decode-light static BTFNT predictor in IF for legal, word-aligned\nB-type conditional branches whose immediate is negative. Compute pc plus\nthe branch immediate in IF and fetch from that target immediately, while\ncarrying predicted_taken and predicted_target through IF/ID and ID/EX.\nEX should redirect only when the resolved architectural next PC differs from\nthe carried prediction; mispredictions still flush normally and RVFI\npc_wdata continues to report the resolved next PC. Keep JAL and JALR on\ntheir existing EX-resolution paths so this remains a single predictor change.\n\nFILES: rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\nTITLE: Tiny trained branch target predictor\nHYP: Add a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a tag, cached target,\nand two-bit saturating direction counter per entry.  IF predicts a\nconditional branch only on a valid BTB hit whose counter is weakly or\nstrongly taken, so cold branches and recently observed exits remain\nsequential; the target comes from the BTB rather than a new IF adder.\nUpdate the entry and counter at EX resolution, carry the prediction through\nthe existing pipeline metadata, and redirect only on a prediction mismatch.\nThis should capture stable CoreMark loops while limiting misprediction and\npreserving the baseline timing more closely than static BTFNT.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/core.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\nTITLE: Low-cost call and return predictor\nHYP: Add a narrowly scoped call/return predictor rather than a general branch\npredictor.  A fetch-side predecode should predict every legal direct JAL\nfrom its encoded target, and a small return-address stack should predict\nthe common CoreMark ABI return form JALR x0, ra, 0 using return addresses\npushed by calls.  Carry the predicted next PC with each queued instruction;\nEX compares it with the resolved next PC and flushes only on a genuine\nmismatch, preserving the existing recovery path.  Keep conditional B-type\nbranches and non-return JALR instructions sequential, and implement the\nstack as compact registered state without a tag/counter lookup, limiting\nboth misprediction exposure and Fmax/ LUT cost while removing exact call\nand return redirect bubbles.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv,rtl/core.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\nTITLE: Exact direct-JAL queue predictor\nHYP: Add a decode-time exact predictor for legal, aligned direct JAL instructions.\nCompute and carry the JAL target while the instruction is admitted to the\nprefetch queue or consumed by decode, invalidate younger sequential queue\nentries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to that target before EX\nresolves the JAL.  Compare the carried prediction with the resolved next PC\nfor recovery and preserve the existing misalignment/trap behavior.  Do not\npredict conditional branches or indirect JALR returns.  Keeping this as a\none-instruction predecode with no BTB tags, counters, or IF lookup mux should\nremove direct-call bubbles while avoiding the prior predictor timing cliff.\n\nFILES: rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv,rtl/core.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\nTITLE: Queue-safe return-address stack predictor\nHYP: Add a small return-address stack trained only by legal direct JAL calls and\nused only for the exact ABI return form JALR x0, x1, 0.  Compute the return\ntarget from the RAS and the ID-stage register value when the queue head is\nconsumed, then atomically replace the queue contents and fetch PC with that\ntarget; leave conditional branches, indirect jumps, and direct JAL fetches\non the existing EX-resolution path.  Carry the prediction target through\nID/EX and suppress the EX redirect only when the resolved return target\nexactly matches it, otherwise use the normal recovery redirect.  Update\npush/pop state at the same queue transaction boundary and invalidate the\nprediction on reset or an empty RAS.  This should remove correctly\npredicted return bubbles while keeping predictor logic off the existing\nimem address critical path and avoiding the prior desynchronization bug.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/core.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\nTITLE: Queue-head adaptive conditional branch predictor\nHYP: Add a compact 2-bit saturating branch-history table indexed by low PC bits,\nconsulted only when the valid queue head is consumed.  For a conditional\nbranch, predict taken only in the strong/weak-taken states and compute its\nimmediate target from the queue-head instruction; if taken, atomically flush\nyounger queue entries and restart the registered fetch PC at that target.\nCarry the prediction through ID/EX, train the table from the EX-resolved\noutcome, and redirect on any predicted-versus-resolved next-PC mismatch.\nKeep JAL/JALR and non-branches on their existing path, preserve alignment\ntraps and RVFI next-PC behavior, and ensure reset, imem stalls, and queue\nreplacement use one coordinated state transition.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv,rtl/core.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\nTITLE: Atomic direct-call queue predictor\nHYP: Recognize only legal, word-aligned direct JAL instructions with rd=x1 at\nthe valid queue head and predict their immediate target when the head is\nconsumed.  Atomically discard younger sequential queue entries, fetch the\ntarget using the same effective target for imem_addr, fetch_pc, and queued\nentry metadata, and retain a pending target when imemReady is low.  Carry\nprediction metadata with the call so EX suppresses the later redirect only\nwhen the exact target was predicted; leave indirect jumps, conditional\nbranches, misaligned targets, and all normal recovery behavior unchanged.\n\nFILES: rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\nTITLE: Retirement-trained ABI return stack predictor\nHYP: Add a small return-address stack used only for the exact RV32 ABI return\nform JALR x0, x1, 0.  Push pc+4 when a legal JAL ra instruction retires and\npop when a legal ABI return retires, so nested calls, stalls, and wrong-path\nqueue contents cannot corrupt the predictor state.  At queue-head consume,\nuse a nonempty RAS top to atomically replace the younger sequential queue\nentries and set fetch_pc_q to the predicted return target; carry a\npredicted-return marker through ID/EX and suppress EX recovery only when\nthe resolved aligned JALR target exactly matches the prediction.  If the\nstack is empty or the target mismatches, retain the existing EX redirect\npath and architectural result.  Do not predict conditional branches,\ndirect JALs, or other JALR forms, and keep predictor target selection out of\nthe normal fetch lookup by using the registered queue transaction path.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/core.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r9s2\nTITLE: Queue-head loop trip-count predictor\nHYP: Add a tiny tagged loop predictor that learns the trip count of eligible\nbackward conditional branches from EX-resolved outcomes.  At queue-head\nconsumption, predict a trained loop branch taken until its learned final\niteration, then predict not-taken for the exit; untrained or unstable\nbranches remain sequential.  For a taken prediction, atomically replace\nyounger queue entries and advance the registered fetch PC to the encoded\nbranch target.  Carry prediction metadata through ID/EX and recover only\nwhen the resolved next PC differs, while training and all queue replacement\nstate transitions remain coordinated so RVFI PCs and stalls are unchanged.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/core.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r10s2\nTITLE: Confidence-gated loop target predictor\nHYP: Add a two-entry tagged loop-target table trained only by EX-resolved\nconditional branches.  Each entry stores the branch PC, its resolved\ntaken target, and a saturating confidence state; predict taken only after\nrepeated same-PC taken outcomes, and stop predicting after a not-taken\noutcome has decayed the confidence.  The queue-head lookup uses the\nregistered target from the table rather than computing a PC-plus-immediate\nadder on the ordinary imem address path.  On a confident hit, atomically\nreplace younger queue contents and advance fetch to the stored target;\ncarry the prediction with the branch and let EX recover only when the\nresolved next PC differs.  Keep reset, imem stalls, alignment traps,\nRVFI pc_next, and predictor training coordinated with the same queue\ntransaction so untrained, exit, and unstable branches remain sequential.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/core.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r11s2\nTITLE: Retirement-trained ABI return stack predictor\nHYP: Add a four-entry return-address stack trained only when legal direct calls\nand ABI returns retire.  Recognize only JALR x0, x1, 0 at the valid queue\nhead, and predict it when the stack is nonempty; use the registered stack\ntop as the target, carry a prediction marker with that instruction, and\nsuppress EX recovery only on an exact aligned match.  Push pc+4 for JAL ra\nand pop for the matching return at retirement, so wrong-path queue entries\nand stalls cannot corrupt predictor state.  Isolate the prediction request\nfrom the ordinary sequential imem address path and preserve atomic queue\nflush/refill, imem stalls, RVFI pc_next, and normal recovery on misses.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/core.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r12s2\nTITLE: Fetch-response direct-JAL target predictor\nHYP: Add a zero-table direct-JAL predictor in the fetch-response transaction.\nWhen an imem word is accepted and is a legal, aligned JAL, compute its\ntarget in the sequential queue-update path, discard only queue entries\nyounger than that JAL, and set the independent fetch PC to the target for\nthe next request.  Carry a predicted-valid bit and target with the JAL\nthrough every queue pop, refill, and ID/EX transfer; EX must suppress its\nnormal JAL redirect only when that marker and target match, while retaining\nthe normal redirect and precise misalignment behavior for all misses.\nThis removes direct-call bubbles without adding a tag lookup or mux to the\nsteady-state imem address path, and the atomic queue update avoids the\ndesynchronization seen in earlier direct-JAL experiments.\n\nFILES: rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r13s2\nTITLE: Transaction-safe return stack predictor\nHYP: Add a compact four-entry return-address stack that predicts only the exact\nABI return form JALR x0, x1, 0 when a valid queue-head transaction has a\nregistered nonempty stack top. Train it only at retirement: push the retiring\npc+4 for direct JAL x1 calls and pop only for a retiring matching return, so\nwrong-path instructions cannot mutate predictor state. Carry a prediction\ntoken and target atomically with each queue entry through pop/refill and\nID/EX; use one effective target for fetch PC, queue contents, and recovery.\nEX suppresses redirect only for an aligned exact match, and all misses,\nstalls, traps, and non-ABI JALRs retain the conservative path. Keep lookup\noff the ordinary sequential imem-address critical path by issuing the\nregistered target request only as an atomic return-prediction transaction.\n\nFILES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv,rtl/core_pkg.sv,rtl/core.sv,rtl/if_stage.sv,rtl/id_stage.sv,rtl/ex_stage.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
