{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r14s2.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r14s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"Shadow-link-register return predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark contains frequent ABI returns, but JALR resolution currently waits\n  for EX and flushes sequential fetch. General BTB/BHT and RAS attempts either\n  hurt Fmax or lost instruction identity across queue stalls. The common ABI\n  return target is already the architectural x1 value, so a narrowly scoped\n  predictor can avoid a tag table, stack management, and target-add arithmetic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Maintain a registered shadow of architectural x1 from the writeback stream\n  and predict only a valid queue-head JALR with rd=x0, rs1=x1, and imm=0 when\n  no older in-flight instruction can still write x1. Use x1 with bit zero\n  cleared as the target, atomically replace younger prefetch entries and the\n  fetch PC with that target, and carry a prediction token and target through\n  ID/EX. EX suppresses its redirect only for an aligned exact match; all\n  hazards, shadow misses, non-ABI JALRs, and mismatches use the existing\n  conservative recovery path. Keep the predictor state transaction aligned\n  with queue consume/refill and imem stalls so a stalled return cannot retag\n  its instruction or violate RVFI pc_next ordering.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Track the committed x1 shadow, conservatively gate return prediction on older x1 writers, and wire the atomic predictor transaction between ID, IF, and EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add return-prediction-valid and predicted-target fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads while preserving the RVFI metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize the exact queue-head ABI return and atomically flush younger entries, issue the shadow-x1 target, and retain a pending target across imem stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Qualify the exact ABI return and latch its prediction token and target with the consumed instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the carried shadow-link prediction with the resolved aligned JALR target and suppress recovery only on an exact match.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
