{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.category==\\\"predictor\\\") | [.id,.title,.outcome,(.delta_pct // \\\"n/a\\\"),(.fitness // \\\"n/a\\\"),(.lesson // \\\"\\\")] | @tsv' experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\tStatic backward-branch taken predictor\tregression\t-12.37\t247.83\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (regression, -12.37%): Static BTFNT in IF was too aggressive for CoreMark—backward-branch exits and weakly taken backward branches trigger EX-time redirect/flush penalties, so fetch-side speculation must be benchmark-profiled or made selective.\nhyp-20260710-003-r2s2\tTiny trained branch target predictor\tregression\t-46.8\t215.32\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, -46.80%): A direct-mapped BTB/BHT can remain functionally correct yet lose heavily when its combinational tag/counter lookup and predicted-target mux sit on the IF next-PC path, so predictor timing must be isolated or kept off the fetch critical path.\nhyp-20260710-003-r3s2\tLow-cost call and return predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t\nhyp-20260710-003-r4s2\tExact direct-JAL queue predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r4s2 (broken, n/a): An early direct-JAL redirect must update the prefetch queue and independent `fetch_pc_q` from the same predicted target; splitting `predict_fire` from that atomic state transition can desynchronize fetch and corrupt CoreMark.\nhyp-20260710-003-r5s2\tQueue-safe return-address stack predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (broken, n/a): Instantiating a new `branch_predictor` in `core.sv` without adding its RTL implementation to the build makes cosimulation fail before predictor behavior is tested, so pipeline experiments must verify module and source-list integration first.\nhyp-20260710-003-r6s2\tQueue-head adaptive conditional branch predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (broken, n/a): A predicted queue-head redirect must use one effective target consistently for `imem_addr`, `fetch_pc_q`, and the queued entry PC; mixing the predicted target with EX's resolved `redirect_target` corrupts branch RVFI PCs and fails `pc_fwd`.\nhyp-20260710-003-r7s2\tAtomic direct-call queue predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t\nhyp-20260710-003-r8s2\tRetirement-trained ABI return stack predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t\nhyp-20260710-003-r9s2\tQueue-head loop trip-count predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t\nhyp-20260710-003-r10s2\tConfidence-gated loop target predictor\tregression\t-57.55\t196.39\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r10s2 (regression, -57.55%): Confidence gating did not make a two-entry loop-target predictor cheap enough because queue-head `if_head_*` lookup, `predict_fire` target selection, and carried prediction metadata still widen the fetch/redirect control path; predictor selectivity cannot offset front-end timing overhead unless the prediction transaction is isolated from ordinary `imem_addr` selection.\nhyp-20260710-003-r11s2\tRetirement-trained ABI return stack predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r11s2 (broken, n/a): Retirement-only RAS updates must remain aligned with the valid IF queue head and its carried prediction marker across stalls and flushes, or wrong-path calls/returns can consume a different stack top and break CoreMark cosimulation.\nhyp-20260710-003-r12s2\tFetch-response direct-JAL target predictor\tregression\t-2.3\t451.97\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r12s2 (regression, -2.30%): A table-free direct-JAL predictor still regressed when every accepted response added opcode/target arithmetic plus prediction metadata through the two-entry queue and ID/EX, showing that response-side speculation must earn back its queue-control and bundle-routing cost even when it leaves the steady-state imem address path untouched.\nhyp-20260710-003-r13s2\tTransaction-safe return stack predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r13s2 (broken, n/a): A registered RAS response cannot be treated as a decode-only `prediction_wait`; queue pop, prediction-token capture, fetch-target update, and EX recovery must share one valid transaction or a stalled return loses instruction identity and fails RVFI `pc_fwd` and register checks.\nhyp-20260710-003-r14s2\tShadow-link-register return predictor\tbroken\tn/a\tn/a\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The history rules out broad BTB/BHT lookups on the IF address path and broad RAS/return schemes that add fragile queue metadata. The remaining viable direction is a narrowly qualified, response-side predictor with atomic queue state, so I’m checking the exact prior mechanisms before selecting the new variant."}}
