nditional branches, compute their predicted target, and use it for next-PC selection while respecting stalls, flushes, reset, and EX redirect priority.\n\n## hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 Static backward-branch taken predictor [regression]\nAdd a decode-light static BTFNT predictor in IF for legal, word-aligned\nB-type conditional branches whose immediate is negative. Compute pc plus\nthe branch immediate in IF and fetch from that target immediately, while\ncarrying predicted_taken and predicted_target through IF/ID and ID/EX.\nEX should redirect only when the resolved architectural next PC differs from\nthe carried prediction; mispredictions still flush normally and RVFI\npc_wdata continues to report the resolved next PC. Keep JAL and JALR on\ntheir existing EX-resolution paths so this remains a single predictor change.\n\nCHANGES:\n- rtl/id_stage.sv: Propagate the IF prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and decoded control.\n\n## hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 Static backward-branch taken predictor [regression]\nAdd a decode-light static BTFNT predictor in IF for legal, word-aligned\nB-type conditional branches whose immediate is negative. Compute pc plus\nthe branch immediate in IF and fetch from that target immediately, while\ncarrying predicted_taken and predicted_target through IF/ID and ID/EX.\nEX should redirect only when the resolved architectural next PC differs from\nthe carried prediction; mispredictions still flush normally and RVFI\npc_wdata continues to report the resolved next PC. Keep JAL and JALR on\ntheir existing EX-resolution paths so this remains a single predictor change.\n\nCHANGES:\n- rtl/ex_stage.sv: Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried prediction and generate redirect only for a conditional-branch misprediction, preserving misalignment traps and RVFI next-PC semantics.\n\n## hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 Tiny trained branch target predictor [regression]\nAdd a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a tag, cached target,\nand two-bit saturating direction counter per entry.  IF predicts a\nconditional branch only on a valid BTB hit whose counter is weakly or\nstrongly taken, so cold branches and recently observed exits remain\nsequential; the target comes from the BTB rather than a new IF adder.\nUpdate the entry and counter at EX resolution, carry the prediction through\nthe existing pipeline metadata, and redirect only on a prediction mismatch.\nThis should capture stable CoreMark loops while limiting misprediction and\npreserving the baseline timing more closely than static BTFNT.\n\nCHANGES:\n- rtl/branch_predictor.sv: Add a small direct-mapped BTB with branch-PC tags, cached targets, two-bit saturating counters, reset state, combinational lookup, and EX-resolution training signals.\n\n## hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 Tiny trained branch target predictor [regression]\nAdd a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a tag, cached target,\nand two-bit saturating direction counter per entry.  IF predicts a\nconditional branch only on a valid BTB hit whose counter is weakly or\nstrongly taken, so cold branches and recently observed exits remain\nsequential; the target comes from the BTB rather than a new IF adder.\nUpdate the entry and counter at EX resolution, carry the prediction through\nthe existing pipeline metadata, and redirect only on a prediction mismatch.\nThis should capture stable CoreMark loops while limiting misprediction and\npreserving the baseline timing more closely than static BTFNT.\n\nCHANGES:\n- rtl/core_pkg.sv: Extend IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted-taken and predicted-target metadata needed to validate conditional-branch predictions.\n\n## hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 Tiny trained branch target predictor [regression]\nAdd a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a tag, cached target,\nand two-bit saturating direction counter per entry.  IF predicts a\nconditional branch only on a valid BTB hit whose counter is weakly or\nstrongly taken, so cold branches and recently observed exits remain\nsequential; the target comes from the BTB rather than a new IF adder.\nUpdate the entry and counter at EX resolution, carry the prediction through\nthe existing pipeline metadata, and redirect only on a prediction mismatch.\nThis should capture stable CoreMark loops while limiting misprediction and\npreserving the baseline timing more closely than static BTFNT.\n\nCHANGES:\n- rtl/core.sv: Integrate the BTB/BHT lookup and EX update path, while preserving the existing imem/dmem and RVFI contracts.\n\n## hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 Tiny trained branch target predictor [regression]\nAdd a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a tag, cached target,\nand two-bit saturating direction counter per entry.  IF predicts a\nconditional branch only on a valid BTB hit whose counter is weakly or\nstrongly taken, so cold branches and recently observed exits remain\nsequential; the target comes from the BTB rather than a new IF adder.\nUpdate the entry and counter at EX resolution, carry the prediction through\nthe existing pipeline metadata, and redirect only on a prediction mismatch.\nThis should capture stable CoreMark loops while limiting misprediction and\npreserving the baseline timing more closely than static BTFNT.\n\nCHANGES:\n- rtl/if_stage.sv: Select a trained BTB target for eligible conditional branches, with redirect, stall, flush, and sequential-fetch priority rules intact.\n\n## hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 Tiny trained branch target predictor [regression]\nAdd a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a tag, cached target,\nand two-bit saturating direction counter per entry.  IF predicts a\nconditional branch only on a valid BTB hit whose counter is weakly or\nstrongly taken, so cold branches and recently observed exits remain\nsequential; the target comes from the BTB rather than a new IF adder.\nUpdate the entry and counter at EX resolution, carry the prediction through\nthe existing pipeline metadata, and redirect only 