{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r15s2.yaml && git status --short -- experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r15s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r15s2\ntitle: \"Registered loop-target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The bench core pays an EX redirect and queue flush for every taken\n  conditional loop branch.  Broad BTB/BHT lookups previously damaged Fmax,\n  while static backward prediction mispredicted loop exits.  A predictor that\n  learns only stable taken loop targets can recover the repeated-loop bubbles\n  without putting a tag lookup or target mux on ordinary sequential fetch.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small tagged loop-target table trained by resolved conditional\n  branches, with a saturating taken-confidence state and the resolved target\n  stored in each entry.  Perform the lookup through a registered queue-head\n  transaction rather than combinationally selecting the normal imem address;\n  predict only an aligned, strongly/weakly taken conditional branch whose\n  table tag matches.  On a prediction, atomically consume the branch, discard\n  younger queue contents, and restart fetch at the stored target.  Carry one\n  prediction token and target with that exact queue entry through refill,\n  stalls, and ID/EX, and have EX redirect only on a resolved next-PC mismatch.\n  Train and invalidate entries at the resolved EX boundary, retain the\n  conservative sequential path for cold or exiting branches, and preserve\n  precise RVFI pc_next, alignment traps, and recovery behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a compact tagged loop-target table with registered lookup, saturating taken confidence, reset, and EX-resolution training/invalidation.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add prediction-valid, predicted-target, and transaction identity fields to IF/ID and ID/EX payloads so queue stalls and replacement cannot retag a branch.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Integrate the queue-head-only registered prediction transaction, atomically flush younger entries, and keep fetch_pc_q, imem_addr, and queued PCs consistent.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect predictor lookup and EX training while preserving dmem/imem backpressure, single-issue retirement, and RVFI ordering.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the carried prediction with the resolved conditional next PC, suppress only exact matches, and retain normal redirect and misalignment-trap semantics on misses.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
