{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r3s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Low-cost call and return predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The two prior conditional predictors either guessed CoreMark loop exits\n  incorrectly or placed a BTB/BHT lookup and target mux on the fetch timing\n  path.  The five-stage core also resolves unconditional calls and ABI returns\n  in EX, flushing useful prefetch-queue entries even though direct calls are\n  exactly decodable and returns are highly regular.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a narrowly scoped call/return predictor rather than a general branch\n  predictor.  A fetch-side predecode should predict every legal direct JAL\n  from its encoded target, and a small return-address stack should predict\n  the common CoreMark ABI return form JALR x0, ra, 0 using return addresses\n  pushed by calls.  Carry the predicted next PC with each queued instruction;\n  EX compares it with the resolved next PC and flushes only on a genuine\n  mismatch, preserving the existing recovery path.  Keep conditional B-type\n  branches and non-return JALR instructions sequential, and implement the\n  stack as compact registered state without a tag/counter lookup, limiting\n  both misprediction exposure and Fmax/ LUT cost while removing exact call\n  and return redirect bubbles.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact direct-JAL predecoder and return-address stack with call push, ABI-return pop, reset, prediction metadata, and resolved-control-flow recovery/update signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the prefetch-queue and ID/EX payloads with predicted next-PC validity and target metadata used to validate call/return speculation.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Integrate registered call/return prediction into queue fill and fetch-PC sequencing while keeping conditional branches sequential and preserving redirect priority and queue flush semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the queued prediction metadata into ID/EX without changing decoded architectural control signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare resolved JAL/JALR next-PC behavior with the carried call/return prediction and issue redirects only for mismatches, retaining alignment traps and RVFI pc_wdata.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect predictor lookup, training, and recovery across the existing fetch queue and execute stage without changing the RV32IM or RVFI interface.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
