{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.yaml && rg -n '\"'^id:|''^category:|fitness_delta_pct:|confidence:|file:'\"' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Exact direct-JAL queue predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage core resolves unconditional JAL control flow in EX,\n  flushing prefetched sequential instructions even though a direct JAL target\n  is fully encoded in the instruction.  General BTFNT and BTB predictors have\n  either mispredicted CoreMark branches or damaged Fmax with IF-side lookup\n  logic, so a narrower exact-target opportunity is more attractive.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a decode-time exact predictor for legal, aligned direct JAL instructions.\n  Compute and carry the JAL target while the instruction is admitted to the\n  prefetch queue or consumed by decode, invalidate younger sequential queue\n  entries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to that target before EX\n  resolves the JAL.  Compare the carried prediction with the resolved next PC\n  for recovery and preserve the existing misalignment/trap behavior.  Do not\n  predict conditional branches or indirect JALR returns.  Keeping this as a\n  one-instruction predecode with no BTB tags, counters, or IF lookup mux should\n  remove direct-call bubbles while avoiding the prior predictor timing cliff.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add exact-next-PC prediction metadata to the prefetch and ID/EX payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Predecode direct JALs at queue admission or head consumption, flush younger sequential entries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to the encoded target without a BTB lookup.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the direct-JAL prediction metadata into ID/EX with the decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate the exact JAL prediction against the resolved next PC and retain alignment-trap and redirect semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the queue/decode prediction and recovery signals while preserving the existing memory and RVFI contracts.\"\n1:id: hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\n3:category: predictor\n21:  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n22:  confidence: medium\n24:  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n26:  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n28:  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n30:  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n32:  - file: rtl/core.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
