{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml && git diff -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Queue-safe return-address stack predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The two-entry prefetch queue already hides instruction-bus stalls, but\n  unconditional ABI returns still resolve in EX and flush otherwise useful\n  queued instructions.  General direction/BTB predictors damaged Fmax or\n  mispredicted CoreMark branches, while the previous combined call/return\n  attempt failed because its speculative queue and fetch-PC updates were not\n  atomic.  A narrowly scoped return predictor can target highly regular\n  JALR x0, ra, 0 returns without adding a tag/counter lookup to IF.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small return-address stack trained only by legal direct JAL calls and\n  used only for the exact ABI return form JALR x0, x1, 0.  Compute the return\n  target from the RAS and the ID-stage register value when the queue head is\n  consumed, then atomically replace the queue contents and fetch PC with that\n  target; leave conditional branches, indirect jumps, and direct JAL fetches\n  on the existing EX-resolution path.  Carry the prediction target through\n  ID/EX and suppress the EX redirect only when the resolved return target\n  exactly matches it, otherwise use the normal recovery redirect.  Update\n  push/pop state at the same queue transaction boundary and invalidate the\n  prediction on reset or an empty RAS.  This should remove correctly\n  predicted return bubbles while keeping predictor logic off the existing\n  imem address critical path and avoiding the prior desynchronization bug.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a compact resettable return-address stack with exact ABI-return qualification, call push/pop training, top-of-stack lookup, and one-cycle prediction metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the prefetch and ID/EX payloads with return-prediction-valid and predicted-target fields used for atomic queue control and EX validation.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the queue-head decode operands, RAS training, prediction fire/target, and recovery signals without changing the memory or RVFI interfaces.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add an atomic return-prediction queue transaction that discards younger sequential entries and advances fetch from the RAS target while preserving normal redirect and bus-stall priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch return-prediction metadata with the consumed instruction and expose the ID-stage return qualification/value needed by the predictor.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Validate predicted ABI returns against the resolved aligned JALR target and redirect only on a mismatch, retaining existing jump and trap behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
