{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The prior predictor attempts show two constraints: IF-side BTB/BTFNT logic hurt timing or mispredicted CoreMark, while queue-integrated direct-JAL/RAS work was fragile. I’m narrowing this to a decode-time, adaptive conditional-branch predictor: a tiny 2-bit BHT consulted only when the queue head is consumed, with one atomic queue/fetch-PC transaction and EX recovery on mismatch."}}
