{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.yaml && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Queue-head adaptive conditional branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Conditional branches currently resolve in EX after the two-entry fetch queue\n  has admitted sequential instructions, so taken loop branches pay a recovery\n  penalty.  Static backward prediction was a regression because CoreMark has\n  loop exits and weakly biased branches, while a direct-mapped BTB put lookup\n  logic on the IF timing path.  A small adaptive predictor can learn those\n  outcomes without committing the prior IF-side timing cost.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a compact 2-bit saturating branch-history table indexed by low PC bits,\n  consulted only when the valid queue head is consumed.  For a conditional\n  branch, predict taken only in the strong/weak-taken states and compute its\n  immediate target from the queue-head instruction; if taken, atomically flush\n  younger queue entries and restart the registered fetch PC at that target.\n  Carry the prediction through ID/EX, train the table from the EX-resolved\n  outcome, and redirect on any predicted-versus-resolved next-PC mismatch.\n  Keep JAL/JALR and non-branches on their existing path, preserve alignment\n  traps and RVFI next-PC behavior, and ensure reset, imem stalls, and queue\n  replacement use one coordinated state transition.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement a small resettable 2-bit BHT with queue-head lookup, conditional-branch qualification, saturating EX-outcome training, and predicted-target generation.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add prediction-valid, predicted-taken, and predicted-target metadata to the IF/ID and ID/EX payloads.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Perform the queue-head prediction transaction atomically: flush younger sequential entries on predicted taken branches and advance the registered fetch PC to the computed target without an IF tag lookup.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate branch prediction metadata with the consumed instruction into ID/EX while leaving architectural decode controls unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare resolved conditional-branch next PC against the carried prediction, issue recovery redirects only on mismatches, and retain existing misalignment-trap and RVFI semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect queue-head lookup, prediction fire, EX training, and recovery signals while preserving the single-issue RVFI and memory interfaces.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
