"motivation\": \"The current load-use detector compares a load destination against both\\nencoded register fields of every following instruction.  For immediate,\\nupper-immediate, jump, fence, and other instructions, one or both fields\\nare not register sources, so CoreMark can receive unnecessary one-cycle\\npipeline stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add precise source-use metadata for the instruction in IF/ID and gate the\\nload-use comparison with it: compare rs1 only for instructions that read\\nrs1, rs2 only for instructions that read rs2, and neither for instructions\\nwith no register sources.  Preserve the existing x0 exclusion, redirect\\nflushing, and dmem-stall priority.  Removing false bubbles should improve\\nCoreMark iterations per cycle with negligible area and timing cost while\\nleaving the architectural forwarding behavior unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each validated RV32I/RV32M instruction class, defaulting unused sources off.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the decoder's IF/ID source-use metadata to the top-level hazard-control wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire source-use metadata from decode into the load-use hazard unit without changing the core IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate load-use matching with decoded rs1/rs2 source-use signals so immediate and source-free instructions do not stall unnecessarily.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Produce precise source-use metadata for each