{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The history rules out a conventional BTB/BHT and broad static BTFNT: both hurt timing or mispredict exits. The remaining high-value angle is a narrowly scoped exact-target predictor for indirect returns, with updates tied to retirement and a single atomic queue transition so it does not perturb conditional-branch prediction. I’m checking the prior RAS failure details before finalizing the YAML."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\\(.id)\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\nHYP: \\\\(.hypothesis.hypothesis)\\\\nCHANGES: \\\\(.changes | map(.file + \\\" :: \\\" + .description) | join(\\\"\\\\n\\\"))\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\(.outcome) ERROR: \\\\(.error // \\\"\\\")\\\\n---\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -r 'select(.id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\\\" or .id == \\\"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\\\") | \\\"ID: \\\\(.id)\\\\nTITLE: \\\\(.title)\\\\nHYP: \\\\(.hypothesis.hypothesis)\\\\nCHANGES: \\\\(.changes | map(.file + \\\" :: \\\" + .description) | join(\\\"\\\\n\\\"))\\\\nOUTCOME: \\\\(.outcome) ERROR: \\\\(.error // \\\"\\\")\\\\n---\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"ID: hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\nTITLE: Low-cost call and return predictor\nHYP: Add a narrowly scoped call/return predictor rather than a general branch\npredictor.  A fetch-side predecode should predict every legal direct JAL\nfrom its encoded target, and a small return-address stack should predict\nthe common CoreMark ABI return form JALR x0, ra, 0 using return addresses\npushed by calls.  Carry the predicted next PC with each queued instruction;\nEX compares it with the resolved next PC and flushes only on a genuine\nmismatch, preserving the existing recovery path.  Keep conditional B-type\nbranches and non-return JALR instructions sequential, and implement the\nstack as compact registered state without a tag/counter lookup, limiting\nboth misprediction exposure and Fmax/ LUT cost while removing exact call\nand return redirect bubbles.\n\nCHANGES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv :: Add a compact direct-JAL predecoder and return-address stack with call push, ABI-return pop, reset, prediction metadata, and resolved-control-flow recovery/update signals.\nrtl/core_pkg.sv :: Extend the prefetch-queue and ID/EX payloads with predicted next-PC validity and target metadata used to validate call/return speculation.\nrtl/if_stage.sv :: Integrate registered call/return prediction into queue fill and fetch-PC sequencing while keeping conditional branches sequential and preserving redirect priority and queue flush semantics.\nrtl/id_stage.sv :: Propagate the queued prediction metadata into ID/EX without changing decoded architectural control signals.\nrtl/ex_stage.sv :: Compare resolved JAL/JALR next-PC behavior with the carried call/return prediction and issue redirects only for mismatches, retaining alignment traps and RVFI pc_wdata.\nrtl/core.sv :: Connect predictor lookup, training, and recovery across the existing fetch queue and execute stage without changing the RV32IM or RVFI interface.\nOUTCOME: broken ERROR: cosim_failed: coremark.elf\n---\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\nTITLE: Exact direct-JAL queue predictor\nHYP: Add a decode-time exact predictor for legal, aligned direct JAL instructions.\nCompute and carry the JAL target while the instruction is admitted to the\nprefetch queue or consumed by decode, invalidate younger sequential queue\nentries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to that target before EX\nresolves the JAL.  Compare the carried prediction with the resolved next PC\nfor recovery and preserve the existing misalignment/trap behavior.  Do not\npredict conditional branches or indirect JALR returns.  Keeping this as a\none-instruction predecode with no BTB tags, counters, or IF lookup mux should\nremove direct-call bubbles while avoiding the prior predictor timing cliff.\n\nCHANGES: rtl/core_pkg.sv :: Add exact-next-PC prediction metadata to the prefetch and ID/EX payloads.\nrtl/if_stage.sv :: Predecode direct JALs at queue admission or head consumption, flush younger sequential entries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to the encoded target without a BTB lookup.\nrtl/id_stage.sv :: Propagate the direct-JAL prediction metadata into ID/EX with the decoded instruction.\nrtl/ex_stage.sv :: Validate the exact JAL prediction against the resolved next PC and retain alignment-trap and redirect semantics.\nrtl/core.sv :: Connect the queue/decode prediction and recovery signals while preserving the existing memory and RVFI contracts.\nOUTCOME: broken ERROR: cosim_failed: coremark.elf\n---\nID: hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\nTITLE: Queue-safe return-address stack predictor\nHYP: Add a small return-address stack trained only by legal direct JAL calls and\nused only for the exact ABI return form JALR x0, x1, 0.  Compute the return\ntarget from the RAS and the ID-stage register value when the queue head is\nconsumed, then atomically replace the queue contents and fetch PC with that\ntarget; leave conditional branches, indirect jumps, and direct JAL fetches\non the existing EX-resolution path.  Carry the prediction target through\nID/EX and suppress the EX redirect only when the resolved return target\nexactly matches it, otherwise use the normal recovery redirect.  Update\npush/pop state at the same queue transaction boundary and invalidate the\nprediction on reset or an empty RAS.  This should remove correctly\npredicted return bubbles while keeping predictor logic off the existing\nimem address critical path and avoiding the prior desynchronization bug.\n\nCHANGES: rtl/branch_predictor.sv :: Implement a compact resettable return-address stack with exact ABI-return qualification, call push/pop training, top-of-stack lookup, and one-cycle prediction metadata.\nrtl/core_pkg.sv :: Extend the prefetch and ID/EX payloads with return-prediction-valid and predicted-target fields used for atomic queue control and EX validation.\nrtl/core.sv :: Connect the queue-head decode operands, RAS training, prediction fire/target, and recovery signals without changing the memory or RVFI interfaces.\nrtl/if_stage.sv :: Add an atomic return-prediction queue transaction that discards younger sequential entries and advances fetch from the RAS target while preserving normal redirect and bus-stall priority.\nrtl/id_stage.sv :: Latch return-prediction metadata with the consumed instruction and expose the ID-stage return qualification/value needed by the predictor.\nrtl/ex_stage.sv :: Validate predicted ABI returns against the resolved aligned JALR target and redirect only on a mismatch, retaining exi