{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"jq -c 'select(.category==\\\"predictor\\\") | {id,title,motivation,hypothesis,changes,outcome,error,implementation_notes}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\",\"title\":\"Static backward-branch taken predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The five-stage bench core resolves conditional branches in EX and fetches\\nsequentially until then, so taken loop branches flush younger instructions.\\nCoreMark contains many tight backward branches with a strongly taken bias;\\nrecovering those bubbles is a direct iterations-per-cycle opportunity.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The five-stage bench core resolves conditional branches in EX and fetches\\nsequentially until then, so taken loop branches flush younger instructions.\\nCoreMark contains many tight backward branches with a strongly taken bias;\\nrecovering those bubbles is a direct iterations-per-cycle opportunity.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a decode-light static BTFNT predictor in IF for legal, word-aligned\\nB-type conditional branches whose immediate is negative. Compute pc plus\\nthe branch immediate in IF and fetch from that target immediately, while\\ncarrying predicted_taken and predicted_target through IF/ID and ID/EX.\\nEX should redirect only when the resolved architectural next PC differs from\\nthe carried prediction; mispredictions still flush normally and RVFI\\npc_wdata continues to report the resolved next PC. Keep JAL and JALR on\\ntheir existing EX-resolution paths so this remains a single predictor change.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted_taken and predicted_target metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Recognize legal aligned backward conditional branches, compute their predicted target, and use it for next-PC selection while respecting stalls, flushes, reset, and EX redirect priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the IF prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and decoded control.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried prediction and generate redirect only for a conditional-branch misprediction, preserving misalignment traps and RVFI next-PC semantics.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted_taken and predicted_target metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Recognize legal aligned backward conditional branches, compute their predicted target, and use it for next-PC selection while respecting stalls, flushes, reset, and EX redirect priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the IF prediction metadata into the ID/EX register alongside the instruction and decoded control.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare the resolved branch next PC with the carried prediction and generate redirect only for a conditional-branch misprediction, preserving misalignment traps and RVFI next-PC semantics.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\",\"title\":\"Tiny trained branch target predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The prior static backward-taken predictor reduced fitness because it\\npredicted loop exits and weakly taken backward branches incorrectly, while\\nits IF-side target calculation also created a severe timing regression.\\nCoreMark still has repeated conditional branches where trained direction and\\na cached target can remove the EX redirect bubbles.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The prior static backward-taken predictor reduced fitness because it\\npredicted loop exits and weakly taken backward branches incorrectly, while\\nits IF-side target calculation also created a severe timing regression.\\nCoreMark still has repeated conditional branches where trained direction and\\na cached target can remove the EX redirect bubbles.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a small direct-mapped branch target buffer with a tag, cached target,\\nand two-bit saturating direction counter per entry.  IF predicts a\\nconditional branch only on a valid BTB hit whose counter is weakly or\\nstrongly taken, so cold branches and recently observed exits remain\\nsequential; the target comes from the BTB rather than a new IF adder.\\nUpdate the entry and counter at EX resolution, carry the prediction through\\nthe existing pipeline metadata, and redirect only on a prediction mismatch.\\nThis should capture stable CoreMark loops while limiting misprediction and\\npreserving the baseline timing more closely than static BTFNT.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a small direct-mapped BTB with branch-PC tags, cached targets, two-bit saturating counters, reset state, combinational lookup, and EX-resolution training signals.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted-taken and predicted-target metadata needed to validate conditional-branch predictions.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the BTB/BHT lookup and EX update path, while preserving the existing imem/dmem and RVFI contracts.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Select a trained BTB target for eligible conditional branches, with redirect, stall, flush, and sequential-fetch priority rules intact.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the IF prediction metadata through the ID/EX register alongside decoded instruction state.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare resolved branch next-PC behavior against the carried prediction and generate redirects only for conditional-branch mispredictions, retaining jump and trap behavior.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a small direct-mapped BTB with branch-PC tags, cached targets, two-bit saturating counters, reset state, combinational lookup, and EX-resolution training signals.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX bundles with predicted-taken and predicted-target metadata needed to validate conditional-branch predictions.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate the BTB/BHT lookup and EX update path, while preserving the existing imem/dmem and RVFI contracts.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Select a trained BTB target for eligible conditional branches, with redirect, stall, flush, and sequential-fetch priority rules intact.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the IF prediction metadata through the ID/EX register alongside decoded instruction state.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare resolved branch next-PC behavior against the carried prediction and generate redirects only for conditional-branch mispredictions, retaining jump and trap behavior.\"}],\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"error\":null,\"implementation_notes\":\"\"}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\",\"title\":\"Low-cost call and return predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The two prior conditional predictors either guessed CoreMark loop exits\\nincorrectly or placed a BTB/BHT lookup and target mux on the fetch timing\\npath.  The five-stage core also resolves unconditional calls and ABI returns\\nin EX, flushing useful prefetch-queue entries even though direct calls are\\nexactly decodable and returns are highly regular.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The two prior conditional predictors either guessed CoreMark loop exits\\nincorrectly or placed a BTB/BHT lookup and target mux on the fetch timing\\npath.  The five-stage core also resolves unconditional calls and ABI returns\\nin EX, flushing useful prefetch-queue entries even though direct calls are\\nexactly decodable and returns are highly regular.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a narrowly scoped call/return predictor rather than a general branch\\npredictor.  A fetch-side predecode should predict every legal direct JAL\\nfrom its encoded target, and a small return-address stack should predict\\nthe common CoreMark ABI return form JALR x0, ra, 0 using return addresses\\npushed by calls.  Carry the predicted next PC with each queued instruction;\\nEX compares it with the resolved next PC and flushes only on a genuine\\nmismatch, preserving the existing recovery path.  Keep conditional B-type\\nbranches and non-return JALR instructions sequential, and implement the\\nstack as compact registered state without a tag/counter lookup, limiting\\nboth misprediction exposure and Fmax/ LUT cost while removing exact call\\nand return redirect bubbles.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":3,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a compact direct-JAL predecoder and return-address stack with call push, ABI-return pop, reset, prediction metadata, and resolved-control-flow recovery/update signals.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the prefetch-queue and ID/EX payloads with predicted next-PC validity and target metadata used to validate call/return speculation.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate registered call/return prediction into queue fill and fetch-PC sequencing while keeping conditional branches sequential and preserving redirect priority and queue flush semantics.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the queued prediction metadata into ID/EX without changing decoded architectural control signals.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare resolved JAL/JALR next-PC behavior with the carried call/return prediction and issue redirects only for mismatches, retaining alignment traps and RVFI pc_wdata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect predictor lookup, training, and recovery across the existing fetch queue and execute stage without changing the RV32IM or RVFI interface.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Add a compact direct-JAL predecoder and return-address stack with call push, ABI-return pop, reset, prediction metadata, and resolved-control-flow recovery/update signals.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the prefetch-queue and ID/EX payloads with predicted next-PC validity and target metadata used to validate call/return speculation.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Integrate registered call/return prediction into queue fill and fetch-PC sequencing while keeping conditional branches sequential and preserving redirect priority and queue flush semantics.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the queued prediction metadata into ID/EX without changing decoded architectural control signals.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Compare resolved JAL/JALR next-PC behavior with the carried call/return prediction and issue redirects only for mismatches, retaining alignment traps and RVFI pc_wdata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect predictor lookup, training, and recovery across the existing fetch queue and execute stage without changing the RV32IM or RVFI interface.\"}],\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"error\":\"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\",\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\",\"title\":\"Exact direct-JAL queue predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The current five-stage core resolves unconditional JAL control flow in EX,\\nflushing prefetched sequential instructions even though a direct JAL target\\nis fully encoded in the instruction.  General BTFNT and BTB predictors have\\neither mispredicted CoreMark branches or damaged Fmax with IF-side lookup\\nlogic, so a narrower exact-target opportunity is more attractive.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The current five-stage core resolves unconditional JAL control flow in EX,\\nflushing prefetched sequential instructions even though a direct JAL target\\nis fully encoded in the instruction.  General BTFNT and BTB predictors have\\neither mispredicted CoreMark branches or damaged Fmax with IF-side lookup\\nlogic, so a narrower exact-target opportunity is more attractive.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a decode-time exact predictor for legal, aligned direct JAL instructions.\\nCompute and carry the JAL target while the instruction is admitted to the\\nprefetch queue or consumed by decode, invalidate younger sequential queue\\nentries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to that target before EX\\nresolves the JAL.  Compare the carried prediction with the resolved next PC\\nfor recovery and preserve the existing misalignment/trap behavior.  Do not\\npredict conditional branches or indirect JALR returns.  Keeping this as a\\none-instruction predecode with no BTB tags, counters, or IF lookup mux should\\nremove direct-call bubbles while avoiding the prior predictor timing cliff.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add exact-next-PC prediction metadata to the prefetch and ID/EX payloads.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Predecode direct JALs at queue admission or head consumption, flush younger sequential entries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to the encoded target without a BTB lookup.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the direct-JAL prediction metadata into ID/EX with the decoded instruction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Validate the exact JAL prediction against the resolved next PC and retain alignment-trap and redirect semantics.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the queue/decode prediction and recovery signals while preserving the existing memory and RVFI contracts.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Add exact-next-PC prediction metadata to the prefetch and ID/EX payloads.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Predecode direct JALs at queue admission or head consumption, flush younger sequential entries, and redirect the independent fetch PC to the encoded target without a BTB lookup.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Propagate the direct-JAL prediction metadata into ID/EX with the decoded instruction.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Validate the exact JAL prediction against the resolved next PC and retain alignment-trap and redirect semantics.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the queue/decode prediction and recovery signals while preserving the existing memory and RVFI contracts.\"}],\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"error\":\"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\",\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\",\"title\":\"Queue-safe return-address stack predictor\",\"motivation\":\"The two-entry prefetch queue already hides instruction-bus stalls, but\\nunconditional ABI returns still resolve in EX and flush otherwise useful\\nqueued instructions.  General direction/BTB predictors damaged Fmax or\\nmispredicted CoreMark branches, while the previous combined call/return\\nattempt failed because its speculative queue and fetch-PC updates were not\\natomic.  A narrowly scoped return predictor can target highly regular\\nJALR x0, ra, 0 returns without adding a tag/counter lookup to IF.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The two-entry prefetch queue already hides instruction-bus stalls, but\\nunconditional ABI returns still resolve in EX and flush otherwise useful\\nqueued instructions.  General direction/BTB predictors damaged Fmax or\\nmispredicted CoreMark branches, while the previous combined call/return\\nattempt failed because its speculative queue and fetch-PC updates were not\\natomic.  A narrowly scoped return predictor can target highly regular\\nJALR x0, ra, 0 returns without adding a tag/counter lookup to IF.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a small return-address stack trained only by legal direct JAL calls and\\nused only for the exact ABI return form JALR x0, x1, 0.  Compute the return\\ntarget from the RAS and the ID-stage register value when the queue head is\\nconsumed, then atomically replace the queue contents and fetch PC with that\\ntarget; leave conditional branches, indirect jumps, and direct JAL fetches\\non the existing EX-resolution path.  Carry the prediction target through\\nID/EX and suppress the EX redirect only when the resolved return target\\nexactly matches it, otherwise use the normal recovery redirect.  Update\\npush/pop state at the same queue transaction boundary and invalidate the\\nprediction on reset or an empty RAS.  This should remove correctly\\npredicted return bubbles while keeping predictor logic off the existing\\nimem address critical path and avoiding the prior desynchronization bug.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":2,\"confidence\":\"low\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a compact resettable return-address stack with exact ABI-return qualification, call push/pop training, top-of-stack lookup, and one-cycle prediction metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the prefetch and ID/EX payloads with return-prediction-valid and predicted-target fields used for atomic queue control and EX validation.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the queue-head decode operands, RAS training, prediction fire/target, and recovery signals without changing the memory or RVFI interfaces.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add an atomic return-prediction queue transaction that discards younger sequential entries and advances fetch from the RAS target while preserving normal redirect and bus-stall priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch return-prediction metadata with the consumed instruction and expose the ID-stage return qualification/value needed by the predictor.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Validate predicted ABI returns against the resolved aligned JALR target and redirect only on a mismatch, retaining existing jump and trap behavior.\"}]},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a compact resettable return-address stack with exact ABI-return qualification, call push/pop training, top-of-stack lookup, and one-cycle prediction metadata.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\"description\":\"Extend the prefetch and ID/EX payloads with return-prediction-valid and predicted-target fields used for atomic queue control and EX validation.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the queue-head decode operands, RAS training, prediction fire/target, and recovery signals without changing the memory or RVFI interfaces.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Add an atomic return-prediction queue transaction that discards younger sequential entries and advances fetch from the RAS target while preserving normal redirect and bus-stall priority.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Latch return-prediction metadata with the consumed instruction and expose the ID-stage return qualification/value needed by the predictor.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Validate predicted ABI returns against the resolved aligned JALR target and redirect only on a mismatch, retaining existing jump and trap behavior.\"}],\"outcome\":\"broken\",\"error\":\"cosim_failed: coremark.elf\",\"implementation_notes\":null}\n{\"id\":\"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\",\"title\":\"Queue-head adaptive conditional branch predictor\",\"motivation\":\"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX after the two-entry fetch queue\\nhas admitted sequential instructions, so taken loop branches pay a recovery\\npenalty.  Static backward prediction was a regression because CoreMark has\\nloop exits and weakly biased branches, while a direct-mapped BTB put lookup\\nlogic on the IF timing path.  A small adaptive predictor can learn those\\noutcomes without committing the prior IF-side timing cost.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"Conditional branches currently resolve in EX after the two-entry fetch queue\\nhas admitted sequential instructions, so taken loop branches pay a recovery\\npenalty.  Static backward prediction was a regression because CoreMark has\\nloop exits and weakly biased branches, while a direct-mapped BTB put lookup\\nlogic on the IF timing path.  A small adaptive predictor can learn those\\noutcomes without committing the prior IF-side timing cost.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Add a compact 2-bit saturating branch-history table indexed by low PC bits,\\nconsulted only when the valid queue head is consumed.  For a conditional\\nbranch, predict taken only in the strong/weak-taken states and compute its\\nimmediate target from the queue-head instruction; if taken, atomically flush\\nyounger queue entries and restart the registered fetch PC at that target.\\nCarry the prediction through ID/EX, train the table from the EX-resolved\\noutcome, and redirect on any predicted-versus-resolved next-PC mismatch.\\nKeep JAL/JALR and non-branches on their existing path, preserve alignment\\ntraps and RVFI next-PC behavior, and ensure reset, imem stalls, and queue\\nreplacement use one coordinated state transition.\\n\",\"expected_impact\":{\"fitness_delta_pct\":4,\"confidence\":\"medium\"},\"changes\":[{\"file\":\"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\"description\":\"Implement a small resettable 2-bit BHT with queue-head lookup, conditional-branch qualification, saturating EX-outcome training, and predicted-target generation.\"},{\"file\":\