{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short && git diff --stat && git diff --check && sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" D cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/z_core.sv\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           | 250 --------------------------------------\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |  13 ++\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py |   2 +-\n 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 251 deletions(-)\n# Implementation notes\n\n## What changed\n\n- Reworked `rtl/z_core.sv` around a decoded instruction slot and a two-entry\n  ordered completion FIFO.\n- A normal ALU/branch result becomes a ready completion immediately. An\n  aligned load/store becomes a stable FIFO-resident memory transaction with\n  separate `mem_pending` and `ready` state; the bus response updates that\n  entry in place.\n- The FIFO permits one younger independent completion behind a stalled data\n  transaction, forwards ready results from both entries, and blocks only on\n  unavailable producer values, completion capacity, a second memory\n  transaction, or conservative MMIO/misaligned handling.\n- Retirement, register writes, and RVFI output are driven only from the FIFO\n  head, preserving single-channel order and avoiding duplicate writes.\n- Added `completion_t` and raw bus-address metadata to `rtl/core_pkg.sv`.\n\n## Deviations and concerns\n\n- The existing stage modules remain in the RTL source tree for compatibility\n  with the unit-test source list, but the top-level core now owns the\n  decoupled execute, memory, and completion control directly.\n- The completion structure is intentionally only two entries deep: one\n  memory transaction plus one younger holding entry. It does not overlap two\n  data-bus transactions.\n- Local lint and Yosys elaboration pass. The complete bench cocotb suite\n  passes (5 test modules, including 11 end-to-end pipeline cases).\n\n## Formal status\n\nFormal was not reached locally. `formal/run_all.sh` stages into the shared\nvendored `formal/riscv-formal` symlink, but this sandbox denies writes there:\nthe run failed at stale-directory cleanup/staging with `Operation not\npermitted`, including when retried with a unique `CORE_NAME`. This is a\nharness filesystem restriction, not a reported RTL counterexample.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
